created_by: midori
creation_date: 2011-03-29T05:53:56Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0000023
name: small cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a cell has an abnormally low volume." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term is not classified as a type of abnormal cell shape, small cells, have the same proportions as a subset of wild-type cells, and simply do not grow to the full length seen in wild type. Elongated cells, in contrast, have proportions (length:diameter ratio) that are never observed in wild-type cells, and so are classified under both abnormal cell shape and abnormal cell size.
synonym: "cell size: decreased" RELATED [SGD:phenotype_annotation]
synonym: "decreased cell size" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced cell size" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001127 ! abnormal cell size
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2011-03-29T05:53:56Z

[Term]
