[Term]
id: FYPO:0000025
name: swollen cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a cell has a larger volume than normal. In a swollen cell, both length and diameter are greater than normal, although the cell is only considered elongated if the length:diameter ratio is also greater than normal." [PomBase:mah]
