id: FYPO:0000256
name: mutator
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which mutations occur at a higher frequency than normal." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased mutation rate" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "mutator during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mutator during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0007431 ! altered mutation rate
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2011-04-19T02:59:38Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0000257
name: normal phenotype
def: "A phenotype that shows no detectable differences from normal. In fission yeast, the characteristics of wild type cells of the sequenced strain (972 h-) or the isogenic h+ or h90 strains are regarded as normal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This is a high-level term whose primary purpose is to organize terms beneath it in the ontology, and we expect that it will not be used for direct annotations. Please consider using a more specific term to annotate each phenotype.
subset: qc_do_not_annotate
subset: qc_do_not_manually_annotate
synonym: "fission yeast normal phenotype" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "no obvious phenotype" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000001 ! phenotype
relationship: inheres_in FYPO:0000001 ! phenotype
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2011-04-19T02:59:38Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0000258
name: obsolete normal phenotype during exponential phase
def: "OBSOLETE. A cell phenotype that shows no detectable differences from normal during exponential growth." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because it was not sufficiently distinguished from its parent.
synonym: "fission yeast normal phenotype during exponential phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "no phenotype in exponential phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal phenotype during exponential phase during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal phenotype during exponential phase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_obsolete: true
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2011-04-19T02:59:38Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0000260
