[Term]
id: FYPO:0000303
name: decreased conjugation frequency
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population undergoes conjugation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term refers specifically to conjugation, whereas experiments that measure mating efficiency often do so by counting zygotes plus asci, sometimes also including spores. For such experiments, we recommend using 'decreased mating efficiency' (FYPO:0000708).
synonym: "decreased conjugation efficiency" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased mating frequency" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased occurrence of mating" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced conjugation efficiency" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced conjugation frequency" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced zygote formation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
