[Term]
id: FYPO:0000321
name: obsolete inviable mixed population including spores and undivided germinated spores
def: "OBSOLETE. A mixed population phenotype in which all cells in a population are inviable, and the population includes a mixture of ungerminated spores and germinated spores that fail to divide." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because a "mixed population" observation would be better represented as two or more separate phenotype annotations, each with penetrance specified.
