[Term]
id: FYPO:0000324
name: mitotic metaphase/anaphase transition delay
alt_id: FYPO:0000393
alt_id: FYPO:0004309
def: "A cell cycle phenotype in which the onset of anaphase of the mitotic cell cycle begins later than normal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Often anaphase onset and anaphase B onset are used interchangeably since they are stablished by monitoring cdc13 levels or the switch from phase II to III of spindle elongation. Also, I am not aware of any phenotype where anaphase A starts but anaphase B does not. {xref="PomBase:mlr"}
synonym: "cell cycle passage through the metaphase-anaphase transition: delayed" RELATED [SGD:phenotype_annotation]
synonym: "delayed cell cycle passage through mitotic metaphase-anaphase transition" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed mitotic anaphase B" NARROW [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed mitotic metaphase/anaphase transition" EXACT []
synonym: "delayed onset of anaphase B during mitotic cell cycle" NARROW [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed onset of mitotic anaphase" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "delayed onset of mitotic anaphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed onset of mitotic anaphase B" NARROW []
synonym: "delayed onset of mitotic anaphase B during vegetative growth" NARROW [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased duration of metaphase during mitosis" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased duration of mitotic metaphase" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "metaphase/anaphase transition delay during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic anaphase delay" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic cell cycle delay at metaphase/anaphase transition" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic metaphase/anaphase transition delay during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "transient cell cycle arrest in mitotic metaphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0006477 ! abnormal mitotic metaphase/anaphase transition
relationship: has_output FYPO:0000274 ! increased duration of mitotic M phase
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2011-05-09T04:36:10Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0000325
name: abnormal attachment of spindle microtubules to kinetochore
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the attachment of spindle microtubules to the kinetochore during a mitotic or meiotic nuclear division is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000628 ! abnormal cellular process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2011-05-11T01:50:15Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0000326
name: abnormal mitotic sister chromatid biorientation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the stable attachment of sister chromatids to microtubules emanating from opposite poles of the mitotic spindle during metaphase plate congression is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term is more specific than 'abnormal attachment of mitotic spindle microtubules to kinetochore' (FYPO:0004213) because sister chromatid biorientation normally occurs only as part of metaphase plate congression, not during other stages of mitosis. FYPO:0004213 can be used for abnormal attachment observed at any time during mitosis. Consider also annotating to 'unequal mitotic sister chromatid segregation' (FYPO:0003241) because a problem with biorientation usually results in unequal chromosome segregation.
synonym: "abnormal sister chromatid biorientation during mitosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal sister chromatid biorientation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal sister chromatid biorientation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000325 ! abnormal attachment of spindle microtubules to kinetochore
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2011-05-11T01:51:05Z

