[Term]
id: FYPO:0000375
name: abolished apoptotic process
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which programmed cell death by apoptosis does not occur. Apoptosis is a form of cell death characterized by rounding-up of the cell, retraction of pseudopodes, reduction of cellular volume (pyknosis), chromatin condensation, nuclear fragmentation (karyorrhexis), plasma membrane blebbing and fragmentation of the cell into apoptotic bodies." [GO:0006915, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished apoptosis" NARROW [GO:0006915]
synonym: "absent apoptotic process" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "apoptosis: absent" RELATED [SGD:phenotype_annotation]
synonym: "apoptotic process abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000629 ! abnormal apoptotic process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2011-07-14T06:06:09Z

