[Term]
id: FYPO:0000392
name: obsolete abnormal cell cycle arrest at mitotic metaphase/anaphase transition
def: "OBSOLETE. A cellular process phenotype in which progression through the mitotic cell cycle is arrested at the metaphase/anaphase transition under conditions where arrest does not normally occur." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because the metaphase/anaphase transition is a single all-or-nothing switch that cannot be started and then stopped before completion. Use 'abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic metaphase' (FYPO:0000620).
