[Term]
id: FYPO:0000444
name: abnormal mitotic cell cycle arrest with replicated DNA
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which progression through the mitotic cell cycle is arrested when cells have replicated genomic DNA, under conditions where arrest does not normally occur." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Arrest with replicated DNA may occur between late S and G2/M; if only DNA content is measured, the arrest point cannot be determined with greater precision.
synonym: "abnormal cell cycle arrest with replicated DNA during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
