[Term]
id: FYPO:0000732
name: short bipolar mitotic spindle
def: "A spindle phenotype in which the mitotic spindle is shorter than normal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that short mitotic spindles are usually not parallel to the long axis of the cell, because short spindle formation takes place before spindle orientation is established (see GO:0000132).
