[Term]
id: FYPO:0000850
name: resistance to stress during vegetative growth
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show decreased sensitivity to a stress. Typically, a cell population is deemed resistant to a stress if cells in the population grow and divide when exposed to the stress at an intensity at which wild-type cells stop growing (and may die)." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased vegetative cell population growth during cellular response to stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistance to stress during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistant to stress during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
