name: decreased histone methylation during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which histone methylation occurs to a lower extent than normal. All histone methylation may be affected, or methylation of specific sites on specific histones may be decreased." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased histone methylation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced histone methylation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
