[Term]
id: FYPO:0000897
name: normal mitochondrial fission
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which mitochondrial fission, the division of a mitochondrion into two or more separate compartments, is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [GO:0000266, PomBase:mah]
