creation_date: 2012-03-29T03:41:35Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0000907
name: abolished mitochondrion inheritance during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which mitochondrion inheritance is abolished, resulting in the formation of a daughter cell that lacks mitochondria." [GO:0000001, PomBase:mah]
