name: swollen spheroid vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is shaped in the form of a spheroid, and has a larger volume than normal. In a swollen cell, both length and diameter may be greater than normal, although the cell is only considered elongated if the length:diameter ratio is also greater than normal." [PomBase:mah]
