[Term]
id: FYPO:0000970
name: sensitive to mitomycin C
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to mitomycin C. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of mitomycin C that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:mah]
