[Term]
id: FYPO:0001005
name: fragmented DNA during nitrogen starvation
def: "A cell phenotype in which DNA is broken into small fragments when the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation." [PMID:19366728, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any circumstances in which cells are starved for nitrogen. Note that cells may enter G0 (quiescence) when subjected to prolonged nitrogen starvation; this term is not restricted to G0. Use 'fragmented DNA' (FYPO:0000160) or one of its descendants if DNA was detected using a method that can resolve molecule sizes (e.g. gel electrophoresis) or detect DNA ends (e.g. TUNEL assay). Otherwise, consider using 'fragmented nucleus' (FYPO:0001919) or one of its descendants.
synonym: "DNA fragmentation during nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
