name: normal growth during cellular response to osmotic stress
def: "A cell population growth phenotype in which vegetative cells grow normally (i.e. indistinguishably from wild type) during a cellular response to osmotic stress." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell population growth during cellular response to osmotic stress" EXACT [PomBase:al, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "normal cellular response to osmotic stress" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal vegetative cell population growth during cellular response to osmotic stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001357 ! normal vegetative cell population growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-04-30T02:50:20Z

[Term]
