[Term]
id: FYPO:0001046
name: premature mitosis
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which cells enter mitosis earlier, relative to cell size or DNA integrity checkpoint status, than normal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term for any experiments that detect early mitosis by any criteria. If you have measured CDK activity or calculated the transition point, also consider using 'premature mitotic G2/M transition' (FYPO:0002516). Also consider annotating to 'viable small vegetative cell' (FYPO:0000648), if mitosis takes place when cells are smaller than normal.
synonym: "advanced mitosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "early mitosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "premature mitosis during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "premature mitosis during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001204 ! mistimed mitosis
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-05-11T01:28:00Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0001047
name: obsolete mitotic catastrophe
def: "OBSOLETE. A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell proceeds through the mitotic metaphase/anaphase transition in the presence of an uncorrected problem (such as chromosome structure or kinetochore attachment), and as a result undergoes abnormal nuclear division and subsequently dies." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because "mitotic catastrophe" has not been clearly defined for fission yeast.
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_obsolete: true
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-05-11T01:34:45Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0001049
name: obsolete mitotic catastrophe, small cell
def: "OBSOLETE. An inviable phenotype in which a cell undergoes mitotic catastrophe (i.e. enters mitosis prematurely and with defective chromosome segregation), entering mitosis when smaller than wild type." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because "mitotic catastrophe" has not been clearly defined for fission yeast.
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe, small cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe, small cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FYPO:0001052
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-05-11T01:59:31Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0001050
name: obsolete mitotic catastrophe, normal size cell
def: "OBSOLETE. An inviable phenotype in which a cell undergoes mitotic catastrophe (i.e. enters mitosis prematurely and with defective chromosome segregation), entering mitosis at the same size as wild type." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because "mitotic catastrophe" has not been clearly defined for fission yeast.
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe, normal size cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe, normal size cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FYPO:0001053
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-05-11T02:09:56Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0001051
name: obsolete mitotic catastrophe, elongated cell
def: "OBSOLETE. An inviable phenotype in which a cell undergoes mitotic catastrophe (i.e. enters mitosis prematurely and with defective chromosome segregation), entering mitosis when longer than wild type." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because "mitotic catastrophe" has not been clearly defined for fission yeast.
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe, elongated cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe, elongated cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe, long cell" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
