created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-05-11T02:16:25Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0001052
name: cut, small cell
def: "An inviable phenotype in which a cell enters mitosis when smaller than wild type, and then septates to give rise to a cut phenotype. In a cut phenotype, a cell undergoes septation despite abnormal mitosis such that the septum physically divides the nucleus into two parts." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cut following advanced onset of mitosis" EXACT [PomBase:jh, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "cut, small cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cut, small cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe with cut, small cell" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "septation following abnormal nuclear division, small cell" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "small cut cell" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000951 ! inviable small vegetative cell
is_a: FYPO:0003165 ! cut with abnormal chromosome segregation
relationship: has_part FYPO:0000951 ! inviable small vegetative cell
relationship: has_part FYPO:0003165 ! cut with abnormal chromosome segregation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-05-11T02:38:12Z

