is_a: FYPO:0002196 ! abnormal vegetative cell shape
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-06-07T11:47:07Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0001120
name: pear-shaped vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a cell is shaped in the form of a pear in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle. One end is rounded, while the other resembles an end of a normal rod-shaped cell. The normally shaped end has the same diameter as a wild-type cell." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cell morphology, pear shaped during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "ice cream cone-shaped cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PMID:2236039, PomBase:vw]
