[Term]
id: FYPO:0001222
name: binucleate vegetative cell
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell contains two nuclei." [PomBase:mah]
comment: When using this term, also consider annotating to a cell cycle arrest term, such as 'abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic telophase' (FYPO:0000622); 'abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic anaphase' (FYPO:0000619) may be applicable if the assay detects DNA masses. Binucleate cells often arise as a result of cell cycle arrest.
synonym: "binucleate cells during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:al]
synonym: "binucleate during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "binucleate vegetative cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
