[Term]
id: FYPO:0001262
name: obsolete stubby cell during cellular hyperosmotic response
def: "OBSOLETE. A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the cell diameter is larger than normal and the cell length is shorter than normal, during a cellular hyperosmotic response." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because the phenotype would be better represented by annotating to the morphology term with conditions specified.
