creation_date: 2012-07-19T16:21:16Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0001263
name: obsolete branched, elongated cell during cellular hyperosmotic response
def: "OBSOLETE. A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is branched and septated, and longer than normal, during a cellular hyperosmotic response." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because the phenotype would be better represented by annotating to the morphology term with conditions specified.
