[Term]
id: FYPO:0001429
name: swollen elongated cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a cell has a larger volume, greater length, greater diameter, and greater length:diameter ratio than normal." [PMID:10388806, PomBase:mah]
comment: The distinction between this phenotype and centrally constricted (dumbbell-shaped) cells (FYPO:0000779) is that swollen elongated cells do not have a constriction along the long axis. Swollen elongated cells may have a uniform diameter, or may be swollen only around the nucleus.
synonym: "elongated cell with increased cell volume" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "enlarged elongated cell" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "large elongated cell" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
