creation_date: 2012-08-22T15:16:12Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0001430
name: abnormal mitotic cell cycle arrest with unreplicated DNA
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which progression through the mitotic cell cycle is arrested before cells have replicated genomic DNA, under conditions where arrest does not normally occur." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Arrest with unreplicated DNA may occur between mitosis and the beginning of S phase; if only DNA content is measured, the arrest point cannot be determined with greater precision.
synonym: "abnormal cell cycle arrest with unreplicated DNA during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic cell cycle arrest with 1C DNA content" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic cell cycle arrest with unreplicated DNA during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
