[Term]
id: FYPO:0001588
name: decreased lysine import during nitrogen starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the import of lysine into the cell occurs to a lower extent than normal when the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any circumstances in which cells are starved for nitrogen. Note that cells may enter G0 (quiescence) when subjected to prolonged nitrogen starvation; this term is not restricted to G0.
