[Term]
id: FYPO:0001662
name: decreased cellular cAMP level during glucose starvation
def: "A cell phenotype in which the amount of trehalose measured in a cell is lower than normal when the cell is subject to glucose starvation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.
synonym: "decreased cellular cAMP accumulation during glucose starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cellular cAMP level during glucose depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased cellular cAMP level during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased cellular cAMP level during glucose limitation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cellular cyclic AMP level during cellular response to glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced cellular cAMP level during glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001660 ! decreased cellular cAMP level
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-10-03T15:57:38Z

