[Term]
id: FYPO:0001790
name: normal plasmid loss
def: "A cell phenotype in which plasmids are lost at the same frequency as in wild-type cells. Plasmid loss occurs when one or both daughter cells do not inherit copies of a plasmid from the mother cell, and may result from failure of plasmid replication or segregation." [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000002 ! cell phenotype
is_a: FYPO:0001312 ! normal vegetative phenotype
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2012-11-21T15:52:33Z

