[Term]
id: FYPO:0001899
name: P-bodies present in decreased numbers during glucose starvation
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which cells contain fewer cytoplasmic mRNA processing bodies (P-bodies) than normal when the cell is subject to glucose starvation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.
synonym: "cytoplasmic mRNA processing bodies present in decreased numbers during glucose starvation" EXACT [GO:0000932]
synonym: "decreased number of P-bodies present during glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased P-body formation during glucose starvation" RELATED [PomBase:al]
synonym: "decreased P-body number during glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "fewer P-bodies present during glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "P bodies present in decreased numbers during glucose starvation" EXACT [GO:0000932]
synonym: "P-bodies present in decreased numbers during glucose depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "P-bodies present in decreased numbers during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "P-bodies present in decreased numbers during glucose limitation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "P-bodies present in reduced numbers during glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001898 ! P-bodies present in decreased numbers
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2013-01-30T17:03:35Z

