[Term]
id: FYPO:0002048
name: normal cell morphology during nitrogen starvation
alt_id: FYPO:0001957
alt_id: FYPO:0001958
def: "A cell phenotype characterized by normal cell morphology (i.e. size, shape, and structure indistinguishable from wild type) when the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation. Wild-type cells become spherical upon nitrogen starvation, and have a smaller volume than under nitrogen-replete conditions." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any circumstances in which cells are starved for nitrogen. Note that cells may enter G0 (quiescence) when subjected to prolonged nitrogen starvation; this term is not restricted to G0.
synonym: "cell morphology, round cells during nitrogen starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cell morphology, rounded cells during nitrogen starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell morphology during nitrogen depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "normal cell morphology during nitrogen deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "orb during nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:jh, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "rounded cell during nitrogen starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "small spherical cell during nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "spherical cell during nitrogen depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "spherical cell during nitrogen deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "spherical cell during nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "spheroid cell during nitrogen depletion" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "spheroid cell during nitrogen deprivation" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "spheroid cell during nitrogen starvation" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0000672 ! normal cell morphology
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2013-03-14T16:29:43Z

