[Term]
id: FYPO:0002082
name: increased protein ubiquitination during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the occurrence of ubiquitination of one or more specific proteins, or of specific protein sites, is increased." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Consider also annotating to 'increased level of ubiquitinated protein in cell during vegetative growth' (FYPO:0002774). We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
