[Term]
id: FYPO:0002083
name: inviable swollen elongated cell with enlarged nucleus
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a vegetative cell is inviable, is swollen, is elongated, and in which the nucleus is larger than normal. The cell contains one nucleus and no septum. In a swollen cell, both length and diameter may be greater than normal, although the cell is only considered elongated if the length:diameter ratio is also greater than normal." [PMID:10388806, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: The distinction between this phenotype and centrally constricted (dumbbell-shaped) cells (FYPO:0000779) is that swollen elongated cells do not have a constriction along the long axis. Swollen elongated cells may have a uniform diameter, or may be swollen only around the nucleus. This phenotype is usually seen in diploid cells, so consider also annotating to 'increased spontaneous diploidization' (FYPO:0000252).
synonym: "inviable elongated cell with enlarged nucleus and increased cell volume" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable elongated vegetative cell with swollen medial region" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable enlarged elongated cell with enlarged nucleus" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable large elongated cell with enlarged nucleus" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "inviable swollen elongated mononucleate aseptate cell with enlarged nucleus" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "inviable swollen elongated vegetative cell with enlarged nucleus" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "lethal; swollen elongated cell with enlarged nucleus" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002251 ! inviable swollen elongated vegetative cell
is_a: FYPO:0005440 ! swollen elongated cell with enlarged nucleus
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2013-05-01T16:06:42Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0002084
