[Term]
id: FYPO:0002093
name: decreased meiotic sister chromatid cohesion
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which cohesion between sister chromatids is decreased during meiosis." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Abnormal cohesion may cause separation of sister chromatids during the first meiotic nuclear division, leading to equational segregation. If this occurs, also annotate to 'equational sister chromatid separation during meiosis I' (FYPO:0005634).
synonym: "decreased sister chromatid cohesion during meiosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced meiotic sister chromatid cohesion" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
