[Term]
id: FYPO:0002167
name: sensitive to ethyl methanesulfonate
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to ethyl methanesulfonate. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of ethyl methanesulfonate that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:mah]
