[Term]
id: FYPO:0002179
name: obsolete inviable mixed population, vegetative cells with abnormal morphology, including long cells
def: "OBSOLETE. A mixed population phenotype in which a microcolony forms, all cells in the population are inviable and have abnormal morphology (i.e. size, shape, or structure), some cells may divide, and some cells are longer than normal." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because a "mixed population" observation would be better represented as two or more separate phenotype annotations, each with penetrance specified.
