[Term]
id: FYPO:0002181
name: obsolete inviable mixed population including germinated spores and spheroid cells
def: "OBSOLETE. A mixed population phenotype in which all cells in a population are inviable, and the population includes a mixture of germinated spores and spheroid vegetative cells. The spheroid cells arise from division of some of the germinated spores, and may form a microcolony of up to 64 cells." [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: This term was made obsolete because a "mixed population" observation would be better represented as two or more separate phenotype annotations, each with penetrance specified.
synonym: "inviable mixed population including germinated spores and rounded cells" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_obsolete: true
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2013-06-04T15:53:26Z

