[Term]
id: FYPO:0002222
name: long meiosis II spindle
def: "A spindle phenotype in which the meiotic spindle is longer than normal during meiosis II." [PomBase:mah]
comment: In extreme examples of this phenotype, the two elongating spindles may meet in the middle of the cell.
synonym: "elongated meiosis II spindle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "long spindle during meiosis II" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "long spindle during second meiotic nuclear division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
