[Term]
id: FYPO:0002292
name: obsolete viable tapered vegetative cell population
def: "OBSOLETE. A cell population phenotype in which all cells in the population are viable and taper at one end to a diameter smaller than the other, in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because it is redundant with annotating to the equivalent cell phenotype plus a full-penetrance extension.
synonym: "population of tapered viable cells" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "viable bottle/skittle vegetative cell population" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "viable skittle-shaped vegetative cell population" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
