[Term]
id: FYPO:0002371
name: obsolete inviable mixed population including spores, undivided germinated spores and divided germinated spores
def: "OBSOLETE. A mixed population phenotype in which all cells in a population are inviable, and the population includes a mixture of spores, undivided germinated spores, and germinated spores that go on to divide once or twice. Some germinated spores remain septated and do not complete cell division." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because a "mixed population" observation would be better represented as two or more separate phenotype annotations, each with penetrance specified.
synonym: "inviable mixed population including spores and undivided and divided germinated spores" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_obsolete: true
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2013-07-25T13:32:16Z

[Term]
