[Term]
id: FYPO:0002390
name: normal mitotic sister chromatid cohesion
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which mitotic sister chromatid cohesion is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Mitotic sister chromatid cohesion is the process in which the sister chromatids of a replicated chromosome are joined along the entire length of the chromosome, from their formation in S phase through metaphase during a mitotic cell cycle." [GO:0007064, PomBase:mah]
