[Term]
id: FYPO:0002424
name: normal actin cortical patch localization during mitotic interphase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which actin cortical patch localization is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle. Cortical patches are normally present at both old and new ends of the cell." [PomBase:mah]
