[Term]
id: FYPO:0002425
name: abnormal actin cable organization during mitosis
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which actin cable organization is abnormal during mitosis. The process normally results in the assembly, arrangement of constituent parts, or disassembly of an actin cable. Actin cables are parallel actin filament bundles nucleated by formin, and are the most common form of actin filament bundles found in yeasts." [GO:0070648, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal actin cable organisation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal actin cable organization during mitotic interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal actin cable organization during mitotic M phase" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal actin cable organization during mitotic nuclear division" EXACT [GO:0140014]
synonym: "abnormal formin-nucleated actin cable organization during mitotic interphase" EXACT [GO:0070648]
is_a: FYPO:0002030 ! abnormal actin cable organization
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2013-08-01T17:15:08Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0002426
name: obsolete inviable mixed population including divided and undivided germinated spores
def: "OBSOLETE. A mixed population phenotype in which all cells in a population are inviable germinated spores, and in which some cells divide once and others do not divide. In the cells that divide once, an inviable cell forms from the growing end of the germ tube, but does not divide further." [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: This term was made obsolete because a "mixed population" observation would be better represented as two or more separate phenotype annotations, each with penetrance specified.
is_obsolete: true
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2013-08-02T14:13:03Z

