[Term]
id: FYPO:0002452
name: inviable septated vegetative cell with abnormal cell morphology
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell contains one or more septa, has abnormal morphology (i.e. size, shape, or structure) and is inviable." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "lethal; septated vegetative cell with abnormal cell morphology" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
