[Term]
id: FYPO:0002496
name: normal metabolic process
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which a cellular metabolic process is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). A metabolic process is any set of chemical reactions and pathways, including anabolism and catabolism, by which living organisms transform chemical substances." [GO:0044237, PomBase:mah]
comment: This is a high-level term whose primary purpose is to organize terms beneath it in the ontology, and we expect that it will not be used for direct annotations. Please consider using a more specific term to annotate each phenotype.
