[Term]
id: FYPO:0002553
name: abnormal double-strand break processing
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which double-strand break processing is abnormal. Double-strand break processing is the 5' to 3' exonucleolytic resection of the DNA at the site of the break to form a 3' single-strand DNA overhang." [GO:0000729, PomBase:mah]
