[Term]
id: FYPO:0002649
name: elongated kinetochore during mitosis
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the kinetochore is longer than normal during mitosis." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This phenotype can be observed in metaphase and/or anaphase. Use this term in cases where "stretching" describes the apparent length of a single kinetochore. For example, a merotelically attached kinetochore can stretch to the extent that it appears as two spots by fluorescence microscopy.
