[Term]
id: FYPO:0002664
name: increased level of stress responsive gene mRNA during vegetative growth
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of one or more messenger RNAs that are normally expressed during a cellular response to stress measured in a cell is higher than normal (i.e. higher than observed in wild-type cells during vegetative growth)." [PomBase:mah]
