[Term]
id: FYPO:0002733
name: inviable after spore germination, multiple cell divisions, elongated tapered cell
def: "A phenotype in which a spore germinates to produce a cell that is elongated and tapered, i.e. tapers at one end to a diameter smaller than the other, undergoes two or more rounds of cell division and then dies." [PomBase:al, PomBase:mah]
