[Term]
id: FYPO:0002799
name: normal protein degradation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which protein degradation is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Protein degradation, also known as protein catabolism, is any metabolic process that results in the destruction of the native, active configuration of a protein, with or without the hydrolysis of peptide bonds." [GO:0030163, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
