def: "A regulation phenotype in which the basal activity of a protein kinase is increased relative to normal. Basal protein kinase activity is the activity observed in the absence of a regulator. Abnormally elevated basal activity may or may not reach the levels observed in the normal activated state." [PomBase:al, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "constitutive protein kinase activity during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "constitutive protein kinase activity during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "constitutively active protein kinase" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000683 ! constitutive catalytic activity
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2013-11-04T14:49:21Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0002829
name: decreased cellular phytochelatin level
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of phytochelatin measured in a cell is lower than normal." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cellular cadystin level" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cellular phytochelatin level during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cellular phytochelatin level during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
