[Term]
id: FYPO:0002878
name: increased transcription during glucose starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which transcription occurs to a greater extent than normal when the cell is subject to glucose starvation. All genes, or a specific subset of genes, may be affected." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.
synonym: "increased transcription during cellular response to glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased transcription during glucose depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased transcription during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased transcription during glucose limitation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
