[Term]
id: FYPO:0002890
name: abnormal horsetail nucleus morphology
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which the size, shape, or structure of the horsetail nucleus is abnormal. The horsetail nucleus forms during the rapid oscillatory movement at meiotic prophase I." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that an abnormal nucleus organization process may, but does not necessarily, result in abnormal nuclear morphology. Consider also annotating to 'abnormal horsetail movement' (FYPO:0000197).
synonym: "abnormal horsetail nuclear morphology" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
