[Term]
id: FYPO:0002903
name: viable pear-shaped vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a cell is viable and shaped in the form of a pear in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle. One end is rounded, while the other resembles an end of a normal rod-shaped cell. The normally shaped end has the same diameter as a wild-type cell." [PomBase:mah]
