def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which ubiquitination of lysine at position 119 of histone H2B is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Lysine 119 corresponds to the conserved C-terminal lysine of H2B." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal histone H2B conserved C-terminal lysine ubiquitination during vegetative growth" EXACT [GO:0071894, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal histone H2B-K119 ubiquitination during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
