[Term]
id: FYPO:0002987
name: inviable after spore germination, without cell division, swollen binucleate cell with central constriction
alt_id: FYPO:0003288
def: "A phenotype in which a spore germinates to produce an inviable cell that does not divide, contains two nuclei, has a larger diameter and volume than normal, and has an abnormal shape featuring a constriction at the center of the cell, corresponding to the cell division site. In some such cells, the diameter at the ends is much greater than in wild-type cells." [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "inviable after spore germination, binucleate without cell division, swollen cell with central constriction" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "inviable after spore germination, undivided swollen binucleate cell with central constriction" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable after spore germination, without cell division, swollen binucleate cell with constricted region at cell division site" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
