[Term]
id: FYPO:0003015
name: cell lysis during cellular response to salt stress
def: "An inviable phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell lyses, i.e. the plasma membrane ruptures and cytoplasm is lost, during a cellular response to salt stress. Note that in fission yeast cell lysis, the integrity of the cell wall is also compromised." [PomBase:mah]
