creation_date: 2014-01-15T14:42:37Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0003025
name: decreased homologous chromosome pairing
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which homologous chromosome pairing during meiosis (synapsis) is decreased. Synapsis is the process in which the side by side pairing and physical juxtaposition of homologous chromosomes is established and maintained. Pairing may be assayed globally or at one or more specific loci." [GO:0007129, PomBase:mah]
