[Term]
id: FYPO:0003026
name: delayed onset of homologous chromosome pairing
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which homologous chromosome pairing during meiosis (synapsis) begins later than normal. Synapsis is the process in which the side by side pairing and physical juxtaposition of homologous chromosomes is established and maintained. Pairing may be assayed globally or at one or more specific loci." [GO:0007129, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed homologous chromosome pairing" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed onset of homologous chromosome pairing at meiosis" EXACT [GO:0007129]
