[Term]
id: FYPO:0003124
name: abnormal cytoplasmic translation
def: "A metabolism phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which translation in the cytoplasm is abnormal. Translation is the synthesis of a protein using the sequence of a mature mRNA molecule to specify the sequence of amino acids in a polypeptide chain." [GO:0002183, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term should be used only when an experiment measures protein synthesis directly, e.g. by measuring incorporation of a radiolabeled amino acid. Consider annotating to 'altered protein level' (FYPO:0000834) or one of its descendants.
synonym: "abnormal cytoplasmic protein biosynthesis" EXACT [GO:0006412, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal cytoplasmic protein synthesis" EXACT [GO:0006412, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal cytoplasmic translation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal cytoplasmic translation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001797 ! abnormal translation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2014-02-19T16:10:41Z

[Term]
