[Term]
id: FYPO:0003216
name: decreased chromatin silencing at rDNA
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromatin silencing at ribosomal DNA repeat regions is decreased." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Chromatin silencing phenotypes may reflect the assembly or maintenance of heterochromatin. See the GO cellular component term 'heterochromatin' (GO:0000792), and the biological process term 'heterochromatin organization' (GO:0070828).
