[Term]
id: FYPO:0003345
name: abolished cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase in response to nitrogen starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the occurrence of cell cycle arrest in response to nitrogen starvation does not occur; arrest normally occurs in G1 phase." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any circumstances in which cells are starved for nitrogen. Note that cells may enter G0 (quiescence) when subjected to prolonged nitrogen starvation; this term is not restricted to G0.
