def: "A cellular process phenotype in which reciprocal meiotic recombination is abnormal at the silent mating-type cassettes. Meiotic recombination is a cellular process in which double strand breaks are formed and repaired through a double Holliday junction intermediate, resulting in the equal exchange of genetic material between non-sister chromatids in a pair of homologous chromosomes." [GO:0007131, PomBase:mah]
