[Term]
id: FYPO:0003440
name: cell lysis during cytokinesis
def: "An inviable phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell lyses, i.e. the plasma membrane ruptures and cytoplasm is lost, during cytokinesis. Note that in fission yeast cell lysis, the integrity of the cell wall is also compromised." [PMID:24798735, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cell lysis during cytokinesis during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cell lysis during cytokinesis during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
