[Term]
id: FYPO:0003557
name: increased antisense RNA level
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of antisense RNA measured in a cell is higher than normal. Antisense RNA is transcribed from the coding, rather than the template, strand of DNA." [PomBase:mah, SO:0000644]
