[Term]
id: FYPO:0003591
name: abnormal protein complex binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of one protein to a protein complex is abnormal. The protein whose binding to the protein complex is affected may be encoded by the mutated gene, or may be encoded by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any interaction with a protein complex that is affected by a mutation, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
