[Term]
id: FYPO:0003677
name: branched, curved, elongated, multiseptate vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell forms one or more branches near a septum, is elongated, has more than one septum, and is curved along the long axis." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "branched, curved, elongated, multiseptate cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "branched, curved, elongated, multiseptate vegetative cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
