[Term]
id: FYPO:0003729
name: protein mislocalized to nuclear periphery
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a protein that is not normally found in the nuclear periphery is observed there." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term can be used to annotate any case where a protein is found in the nuclear periphery in a mutant, but not in wild type. In some cases, there may be enough additional information to annotate to 'abnormal protein localization' (FYPO:0000443) or one of its descendants. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
