id: FYPO:0003743
name: decreased cell population growth during glucose starvation
def: "A cell growth phenotype in which cell population growth is decreased relative to normal under conditions of glucose starvation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.
synonym: "decreased cell population growth during glucose depletion" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cell population growth during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cell population growth during glucose limitation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cell population growth in response to glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "hypersensitive to glucose starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced cell population growth during glucose starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to glucose starvation" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "slow cell population growth during glucose starvation" NARROW [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001355 ! decreased vegetative cell population growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2014-09-08T11:52:09Z

