[Term]
id: FYPO:0003926
name: increased number of converged replication forks
def: "A cell phenotype in which a cell contains a larger number of sites where replication forks have converged than normal. Additional converged forks are usually detected at sites that are normally replicated unidirectionally." [PMID:22426534, PomBase:mah]
