[Term]
id: FYPO:0003938
name: increased cell population growth during glucose starvation
def: "A cell growth phenotype in which cell population growth is increased relative to normal under conditions of glucose starvation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.
synonym: "fast cell population growth during glucose starvation" NARROW [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased cell population growth during glucose depletion" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased cell population growth during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased cell population growth during glucose limitation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased cell population growth in response to glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistant to glucose starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003937 ! increased cell population growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2014-10-29T11:58:39Z

