[Term]
id: FYPO:0004210
name: mitotic spindle elongation without chromosome separation with centromeric DNA dissociated from spindle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which mitotic spindle elongation begins, but mitotic sister chromatid segregation stops before completing separation of chromosomes, DNA remains in a single mass at or near the midpoint of the mitotic spindle, and centromeric DNA is not closely associated with the mitotic spindle." [PMID:16855021, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
