[Term]
id: FYPO:0004292
name: abnormal septum
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which the position or morphology of all or part of the septum is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that an abnormal septum organization process may, but does not necessarily, result in a physically abnormal septum.
synonym: "abnormal septum physical object quality" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000287 ! abnormal subcellular component
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-01-14T14:54:41Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0004293
name: mislocalized septum
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which a cell or hypha has a septum in an abnormal location. The normal location during yeast-form growth is at the midpoint of the long axis of the cell." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that the location of the septum is determined by the location of the contractile ring, which in turn is determined by the location of the cell division site, so an abnormality in cell division site determination can be inferred from this phenotype.
synonym: "abnormal septum localization" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal septum location" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal septum position" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal septum positioning" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "asymmetric septum" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "asymmetrically located septum" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mislocalised septum" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "misplaced septum" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0004292 ! abnormal septum
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-01-14T14:55:00Z

