def: "OBSOLETE. A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which acetylation of lysine at positions 5, 8, 12 and 16 of histone H4 at the centromere central core occurs to a greater extent than normal." [PMID:18493607, PomBase:mah]
