[Term]
id: FYPO:0004325
name: sensitive to 5-fluorouracil
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to 5-fluorouracil. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of 5-fluorouracil that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "hypersensitive to 5-fluorouracil" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to 5-fluorouracil during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
