[Term]
id: FYPO:0004329
name: normal mitotic rDNA separation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which mitotic sister chromatid separation is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) in regions containing ribosomal DNA (rDNA). Mitotic sister chromatid separation is the process in which sister chromatids are physically detached from each other during mitosis." [GO:0051306, PMID:17032733, PomBase:mah]
