created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-01-29T11:23:10Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0004330
name: normal mitotic telomeric DNA separation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which mitotic sister chromatid separation is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) at telomeres. Mitotic sister chromatid separation is the process in which sister chromatids are physically detached from each other during mitosis." [GO:0051306, PMID:17032733, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal mitotic chromosome separation at telomere" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
