[Term]
id: FYPO:0004418
name: cut cell with decreased poly(A)+ mRNA export from nucleus
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell undergoes septation despite abnormal chromosome segregation, and in which the export of polyadenylated mRNA from the nucleus is decreased. The daughter cells produced by septation are both inviable. Export of all polyadenylated mRNAs or a specific mRNA may be affected." [PMID:14511667, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "cut cell with decreased poly(A)+ mRNA export from nucleus during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cut cell with decreased poly(A)+ mRNA export from nucleus during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cut cell with reduced poly(A)+ mRNA export from nucleus" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cut with decreased poly(A)+ mRNA export from nucleus" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased poly(A) mRNA export in cut" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "septation following abnormal mitotic chromosome segregation with decreased poly(A)+ mRNA export from nucleus" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0003755 ! abnormal vegetative cell phenotype
relationship: has_part FYPO:0000229 ! cut
relationship: has_part FYPO:0002522 ! decreased poly(A)+ mRNA export from nucleus
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-02-19T11:10:36Z

