[Term]
id: FYPO:0004474
name: normal mitotic cell cycle DNA replication checkpoint
def: "A cell cycle checkpoint phenotype in which the mitotic cell cycle DNA replication checkpoint is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). The mitotic DNA replication checkpoint normally prevents the initiation of mitosis until DNA replication is complete." [PomBase:mah]
