[Term]
id: FYPO:0004494
name: inviable branched, swollen, elongated vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is inviable, branched, septated, and has a larger volume and is longer, than normal. In a swollen cell, both length and diameter may be greater than normal, although the cell is only considered elongated if the length:diameter ratio is also greater than normal." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable branched, elongated, swollen vegetative cell" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "inviable branched, swollen, elongated cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
