created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-03-11T16:01:12Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0004495
name: inviable branched, swollen, elongated, multiseptate vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is inviable, branched, has more than one septum, and has a larger volume and is longer, than normal. In a swollen cell, both length and diameter may be greater than normal, although the cell is only considered elongated if the length:diameter ratio is also greater than normal." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable branched, elongated, swollen, multiseptate vegetative cell" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "inviable branched, swollen, elongated, multiseptate cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
