[Term]
id: FYPO:0004511
name: long curved interphase microtubules
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells form cytoplasmic microtubules that are longer than normal and are curved, i.e. follow a smooth bend rather than a straight line, during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle." [PomBase:mah]
comment: In severe instances of this phenotype, microtubules grow long enough to curve around the cell tip.
synonym: "elongated curved interphase microtubules" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
