[Term]
id: FYPO:0004532
name: abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic M phase with abnormal spindle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which progression through the mitotic cell cycle is arrested in M phase under conditions where arrest does not normally occur, and the position or morphology of the mitotic spindle is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Metaphase is defined as the part of mitosis when chromosomes are aligned in the middle of the spindle. If no spindle is present, do not use this term, but consider 'abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic prophase' (FYPO:0003145). If you cannot tell whether a spindle is present, or if metaphase cannot be clearly detected, annotate to the more general term 'abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic M phase' (FYPO:0000608).
synonym: "abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic M phase with abnormal mitotic spindle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic M phase with abnormal spindle during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic M phase with condensed chromosomes and abnormal spindle" RELATED [Pombase:vw]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic cell cycle arrest in M phase with abnormal spindle" EXACT [GO:0000089]
is_a: FYPO:0000338 ! abnormal mitotic spindle
is_a: FYPO:0000608 ! abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic M phase
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-03-31T14:23:17Z

