[Term]
id: FYPO:0004613
name: abolished microtubule attachment to spindle pole body
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the spindle pole body is not attached to any interphase cytoplasmic microtubules; as a result, the microtubules are not connected to the nucleus. Normally, the spindle pole body is attached to at least one cytoplasmic microtubule bundle." [PMID:15772152, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: This phenotype may result from either absence of the microtubule bundle that would normally attach to the SPB, or from a problem with the SPB-microtubule attachment process.
synonym: "abolished microtubule attachment to nucleus" BROAD [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abolished microtubule attachment to spindle pole body during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished microtubule attachment to spindle pole body during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cytoplasmic microtubules absent from mitotic spindle pole body" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "cytoplasmic microtubules detached from spindle pole body" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "interphase microtubules detached from nucleus" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "interphase microtubules detached from spindle pole body" EXACT [Pombase:vw]
synonym: "SPB detached from cytoplasmic microtubules" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
