[Term]
id: FYPO:0004661
name: obsolete normal protein tyrosine phosphorylation during vegetative growth
def: "OBSOLETE. A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the phosphorylation of tyrosine residues of one or more specific proteins is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete to implement a decision that protein modification terms should only include residue-specific information in cases where it is especially biologically significant, such as in histones or the RNA polymerase II CTD. In all other cases, phenotypic effects on specific modified residues should be captured in annotation extensions.
synonym: "normal protein tyrosine phosphorylation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FYPO:0000776
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-05-27T16:42:15Z

