creation_date: 2015-06-12T15:05:16Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0004700
name: bent vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is bent along the long axis. In a bent cell, the long axis has one or more angles, rather than following a straight line." [PomBase:mah]
