[Term]
id: FYPO:0004703
name: viable curved, elongated, swollen vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a vegetatively growing cell is viable, is longer and has a larger volume than normal, and is curved along the long axis. In a curved cell, the long axis follows a smooth bend rather than a straight line." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that if you have done an experiment that assays the viability of a population of cells, such as looking at colony growth or growth in liquid culture, you should also annotate to 'viable cell population' (FYPO:0002058) or one of its descendants.
