[Term]
id: FYPO:0004742
name: normal chromatin silencing at centromere outer repeat
def: "A transcription regulation phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromatin silencing at the outer repeat region of the centromere is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that the centromere outer repeat region corresponds to SO:0001799. Chromatin silencing phenotypes may reflect the assembly or maintenance of heterochromatin. See the GO cellular component term 'heterochromatin' (GO:0000792), and the biological process term 'heterochromatin organization' (GO:0070828).
