[Term]
id: FYPO:0004800
name: abolished premeiotic DNA replication during azygotic meiotic cell cycle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which premeiotic DNA replication does not occur during a cycle of azygotic meiosis and sporulation. Azygotic meiosis and sporulation occur when meiosis takes place within a diploid cell rather than in a zygote produced by sporulation. Zygotes can resume vegetative growth and form colonies of diploid cells if returned to rich media before commitment to meiosis; under nitrogen starvation, diploid cells heterozygous for mating type will undergo azygotic meiosis. Azygotic asci have a characteristic linear morphology resembling that of a single vegetatively growing cell." [PMID:22558440, PMID:25891897, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished DNA replication before azygotic meiotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished premeiotic DNA replication during azygotic meiosis" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished premeiotic DNA replication during azygotic meiosis and sporulation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "absent premeiotic DNA replication during azygotic meiotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "premeiotic DNA replication abolished during azygotic meiotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002044 ! abolished premeiotic DNA replication
