[Term]
id: FYPO:0004812
name: abnormal termination of RNA polymerase II transcription at rDNA
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the termination of transcription by RNA polymerase II at sites in ribosomal DNA (rDNA) is abnormal." [PMID:25417108, PomBase:mah]
comment: Although rDNA is normally transcribed by RNA polymerase I, RNA polymerase II mediates antisense transcription in subtelomeric rDNA repeats on chromosome III.
