[Term]
id: FYPO:0004870
name: decreased duration of mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint
def: "A cell cycle checkpoint phenotype in which the duration of mitotic cell cycle arrest or delay due to regulation by the mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint is shorter than normal. The DNA replication checkpoint normally prevents the initiation of mitosis until DNA replication is complete." [PomBase:mah]
