[Term]
id: FYPO:0004941
name: decreased mannose level in glycoprotein glycan
def: "A phenotype in which the glycan moiety of a glycoprotein contains a lower amount of mannose residues than normal. In wild-type cells, glycoprotein glycans contain mannose and galactose residues in a 1:1.2 ratio." [PMID:11015724, PMID:8782411, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased mannose level in glycoprotein oligosaccharide" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "reduced mannose level in glycoprotein glycan" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
