[Term]
id: FYPO:0005000
name: protein mislocalized to nucleus during mitotic interphase
def: "A cell phenotype in which a protein that is not normally found in the nucleus is observed there during interphase of a mitotic cell cycle." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term can be used to annotate any case where a protein is found in the nucleus in a mutant, but not in wild type. In some cases, there may be enough additional information to annotate to 'abnormal protein localization' (FYPO:0000443) or one of its descendants. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "ectopic protein localization to nucleus during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "protein mislocalised to nucleus during interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein mislocalised to nucleus during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein mislocalized to nucleus during interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein mislocalized to nucleus during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
