[Term]
id: FYPO:0005004
name: decreased protein level in anaphase-promoting complex
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of a protein measured in the anaphase-promoting complex is lower than normal." [PMID:22906049, PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term for cases where the relative abundance of one or more specific proteins in the anaphase-promoting complex is decreased, altering the anaphase-promoting complex stoichiometry. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
