[Term]
id: FYPO:0005005
name: increased level of hexose transport gene mRNA during vegetative growth
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of one or more hexose transport RNAs measured in a cell is higher than normal (i.e. higher than observed in wild-type cells). Hexose transport RNAs are transcribed from genes whose products are involved in transport of six-carbon sugars." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Consider annotating to a term describing abnormal transcription or abnormal regulation of transcription, but note that changes in RNA levels may result from changes in RNA stability as well as changes in transcription.
synonym: "increased hexose transport gene mRNA accumulation during vegetative growth" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased level of hexose transport gene mRNA during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased level of hexose transport gene RNA during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased level of hexose transport gene transcripts during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0004490 ! increased level of transport gene mRNA during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-10-28T14:40:32Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005006
name: obsolete normal protein serine phosphorylation
def: "OBSOLETE. A cellular process phenotype in which the phosphorylation of serine residues of one or more specific proteins is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete to implement a decision that protein modification terms should only include residue-specific information in cases where it is especially biologically significant, such as in histones or the RNA polymerase II CTD. In all other cases, phenotypic effects on specific modified residues should be captured in annotation extensions.
synonym: "normal peptidyl-serine phosphorylation" EXACT [GO:0018105]
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: FYPO:0004422
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-10-28T14:44:03Z

