[Term]
id: FYPO:0005023
name: inviable elongated septated mononucleate vegetative cell
def: "A cell phenotype in which a cell is inviable, contains one nucleus and one or more septa and is elongated. Cells with this phenotype are inviable, and the nucleus is not in the normal location." [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: In cells with this phenotype, septation has proceeded despite chromosome segregation failing to complete normally. Chromosome segregation may be incomplete or entirely abolished. Consider also annotating to 'cut' (FYPO:0003155), 'septation following abnormal chromosome segregation, with binucleate and anucleate compartment formation' (FYPO:0003166), or their descendants, because these phenotypes often co-occur.
synonym: "elongated cell with cytokinesis in the absence of nuclear division" RELATED [PomBase:al, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "elongated cell with cytokinesis without nuclear division" RELATED [PomBase:al, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "elongated cell with septation in the absence of nuclear division" RELATED [PomBase:al, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "elongated cell with septation independent of mitosis" RELATED [PomBase:al, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "elongated cell with septation without nuclear division" RELATED [PomBase:al, PomBase:vw]
