[Term]
id: FYPO:0005027
name: inviable after spore germination, without cell division, swollen binucleate multiseptate cell with central constriction
def: "A phenotype in which a spore germinates to produce an inviable cell that does not divide, has a larger diameter and volume than normal, contains two nuclei and more than one septum, and has an abnormal shape featuring a constriction at the center of the cell, corresponding to the cell division site. In some such cells, the diameter at the ends is much greater than in wild-type cells." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable after spore germination, binucleate without cell division, swollen with multiple septa" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "inviable after spore germination, undivided swollen binucleate multiseptate cell with central constriction" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
