def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the phosphorylation of one or more specific proteins occurs to a lower extent than normal when the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any circumstances in which cells are starved for nitrogen. Note that cells may enter G0 (quiescence) when subjected to prolonged nitrogen starvation; this term is not restricted to G0. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "decreased protein phosphorylation during cellular response to nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein phosphorylation during nitrogen depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
