[Term]
id: FYPO:0005054
name: normal cell cycle regulation during cellular response to latrunculin A
def: "A cellular response phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the regulation of the mitotic cell cycle in response to latrunculin A is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Normally, cell cycle progression is slowed or arrested transiently following exposure to latrunculin A." [PMID:15537703, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell cycle delay following latrunculin A exposure" NARROW [PomBase:al]
synonym: "normal cell cycle regulation during cellular response to LatA" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
