is_a: FYPO:0001254 ! multinucleate multiseptate vegetative cell, septa grouped
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-11-18T13:52:17Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005057
name: abolished meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping does not occur. Meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping is the process by which SPO11/Rec12-oligonucleotide complexes are removed from 5' DNA double-strand breaks induced during meiosis." [GO:1990898, PMID:26130711, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000008 ! abnormal meiotic recombination
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-11-18T14:12:20Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005058
name: decreased meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping is decreased. Meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping is the process by which SPO11/Rec12-oligonucleotide complexes are removed from 5' DNA double-strand breaks induced during meiosis." [GO:1990898, PMID:26130711, PomBase:mah]
