creation_date: 2015-11-18T14:13:45Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005059
name: decreased meiotic DNA double-strand break resection
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which meiotic DNA double-strand break resection is decreased. Meiotic DNA double-strand break resection is the process by which long-tract single-stranded 3'-end DNA is generated by removal of bases from a 5' end from which SPO11/Rec12-oligonucleotide complexes have been removed." [GO:1990899, PMID:26130711, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased meiotic DNA double-strand break resectioning" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced meiotic DNA double-strand break resection" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000008 ! abnormal meiotic recombination
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-11-18T14:22:37Z

