creation_date: 2015-11-18T15:27:49Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005068
name: increased number of double-strand break sites during mitotic S phase
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the number of sites of double-strand breaks in DNA is greater than normal during S phase of the mitotic cell cycle." [PMID:18180284, PomBase:mah]
comment: Because Rad22 often accumulates at double-strand breaks, consider also annotating to 'increased number of Rad52 foci during vegetative growth' (FYPO:0000972).
synonym: "accumulation of DNA damage foci during mitotic S phase" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "accumulation of double-strand break sites during mitotic S phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
