[Term]
id: FYPO:0005077
name: elongated cell during glucose starvation
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a cell becomes elongated, i.e. has a greater length and length:diameter ratio than normal, when the cell is subject to glucose starvation." [PMID:17179073, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.
synonym: "cell morphology, elongated cell during glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "elongated cell during glucose depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "elongated cell during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "long cell during glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0000017 ! elongated cell
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-11-23T14:05:29Z

