[Term]
id: FYPO:0005092
name: inviable after spore germination, multiple cell divisions, swollen, elongated pear-shaped cell
def: "A phenotype in which a spore germinates to produce a cell that has a greater length, diameter, and volume than normal, is shaped in the form of a pear, and undergoes two or more rounds of cell division and then dies. In a pear-shaped cell, one end is rounded, while the other resembles an end of a normal rod-shaped cell." [PomBase:mah]
