[Term]
id: FYPO:0005115
name: elongated vegetative cell with central constriction
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is elongated and has an abnormal shape featuring a constriction at the center of the cell, corresponding to the cell division site. In some such cells, the diameter at the ends is much greater than in wild-type cells." [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: Note that cell with this phenotype, often called dumbbell-shaped, are usually also elongated. The distinction between this phenotype and swollen elongated cells (FYPO:0001429) is that dumbbell-shaped cells have a constriction along the long axis, whereas swollen elongated cells do not. Note that if you have done an experiment that assays the viability of a population of cells, such as looking at colony growth or growth in liquid culture, you should also annotate to 'inviable cell population' (FYPO:0002059) or one of its descendants.
synonym: "cell morphology, elongated dumbbell" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cell morphology, long dumbbell" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "elongated cell with central constriction during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "elongated cell with central constriction during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "elongated dumbbell morphology" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "elongated dumbbell-shaped vegetative cell" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "elongated swollen vegetative cell with constricted region at cell division site" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0001122 ! elongated vegetative cell
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-12-07T13:54:25Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005116
name: increased punctate nuclear protein localization
def: "A cell phenotype in which a protein is localized to discrete regions in the nucleus, visible as foci or dots by microscopy, to a greater extent observed than in normal (wild type) cells." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for protein that do not normally localize to discrete nuclear regions, or for proteins that do normally show punctate localization but with such localization increased in a mutant. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased protein localization to nuclear puncta" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased punctate nuclear protein localisation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased punctate nuclear protein localization during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased punctate nuclear protein localization during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
