created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-12-08T16:21:53Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005117
name: normal transcription during nitrogen starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which transcription occurs to is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) in extent, timing, start or termination site, etc. when the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation. All genes, or a specific subset of genes, may be measured." [PomBase:mah]
