[Term]
id: FYPO:0005118
name: decreased transcription during nitrogen starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which transcription occurs to a lower extent than normal when the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation. All genes, or a specific subset of genes, may be affected." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term if there is evidence, such as labeled nucleotide incorporation, showing that transcription rather than RNA stability is affected; otherwise, use 'decreased RNA level' (FYPO:0000826).
synonym: "decreased transcription during cellular response to nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased transcription during nitrogen depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased transcription during nitrogen deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased transcription during nitrogen limitation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased transcription in response to nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased transcriptional response to nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:al]
synonym: "reduced transcription during nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002876 ! decreased transcription
is_a: FYPO:0006550 ! decreased gene expression during nitrogen starvation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-12-08T16:26:01Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005119
name: altered protein binding specificity
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which a mutation causes a gene product to bind to one or more proteins with different specificity from normal. For example, a protein may bind to a protein in a mutant that it does not bind in wild type. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PMID:25487150, PomBase:mah]
comment: Also consider annotating to another term under 'abnormal protein binding', such as 'increased protein binding' (FYPO:0001571), to capture more details about the effect on protein binding specificity.
synonym: "abnormal protein binding specificity" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "altered protein-protein interaction specificity" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000704 ! abnormal protein-protein interaction
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-12-14T12:00:51Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005120
name: increased RNA level during meiotic cell cycle
def: "A cell phenotype in which the amount of RNA measured in a cell is greater than normal during the meiotic cell cycle. Total RNA or a specific RNA may be affected." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Consider annotating to a term describing abnormal transcription or abnormal regulation of transcription, but note that changes in RNA levels may result from changes in RNA stability as well as changes in transcription. We recommend noting which RNA(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased RNA accumulation during meiotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased transcript level during meiotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0001890 ! increased RNA level
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-12-14T12:10:13Z

[Term]
