[Term]
id: FYPO:0005179
name: abnormal mitotic cell cycle regulation during cellular response to UV during mitotic G1 phase
def: "A cellular response phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the regulation of the mitotic cell cycle in response to ultraviolet light (UV) exposure during mitotic G1 phase is abnormal. Normally, cell cycle progression is slowed or arrested transiently following exposure to UV. The most common abnormality is for the cell cycle to progress as in the absence of UV." [PMID:15498101, PomBase:mah]
