[Term]
id: FYPO:0005197
name: increased protein phosphorylation during glucose starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the phosphorylation of one or more specific proteins occurs to a greater extent than normal when the cell is subject to glucose starvation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased protein phosphorylation during glucose depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased protein phosphorylation during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
