[Term]
id: FYPO:0005268
name: abnormal mitotic cell cycle regulation during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate
def: "A cellular response phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the regulation of the mitotic cell cycle in response to methyl methanesulfonate (MMS) is abnormal. Normally, cell cycle progression is slowed or arrested transiently following exposure to MMS. The most common abnormality is for the cell cycle to progress as in the absence of MMS." [PomBase:mah]
