[Term]
id: FYPO:0005293
name: decreased protein-protein interaction during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of one protein to another occurs to a lower extent than normal during a cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate. The relevant proteins may include the one encoded by the mutated gene, or may both be encoded by different genes." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any protein-protein interaction that is affected by a mutation, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
