name: abolished protein localization to cytoplasm, with protein mislocalized to nucleus during mitotic interphase
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of a protein to the cytoplasm is abolished, and the protein is instead present in the nucleus, during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle." [PMID:9635190, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "abolished protein localisation to cytoplasm, with protein mislocalised to nucleus during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished protein localization to cytoplasm, with protein mislocalized to nucleus during interphase during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished protein localization to cytoplasm, with protein mislocalized to nucleus during mitotic interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein localization to cytoplasm abolished, with protein mislocalized to nucleus during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001179 ! abolished protein localization during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-04-11T12:39:57Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005347
name: pointed nucleus during mitotic interphase
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the nucleus has a pointed shape during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle." [PMID:12390246, PomBase:mah]
comment: Nuclear chromatin within the nucleus also assumes a pointed shape, and the point is associated with the spindle pole body.
synonym: "pointed nucleus during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "pointed nucleus during mitotic interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000062 ! abnormal nuclear morphology during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-04-11T13:35:04Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005348
name: abnormal spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which spindle pole body (SPB)-led chromosome movement is abnormal. SPB-led chromosome movement is a microtubule-based process in which chromosomes migrate as a result of rapid spindle pole body (SPB) and centrosome oscillations during mitotic interphase." [PomBase:mah] {comment="GO:0140404"}
synonym: "abnormal maintenance of mitotic spindle pole body localization" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal maintenance of SPB localization" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic SPB oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic spindle pole body movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic spindle pole body oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal SPB-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000534 ! abnormal mitotic spindle pole body localization
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-04-11T13:08:55Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005349
name: increased spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the mitotic spindle pole body (SPB) moves rapidly back and forth to a greater extent and over a larger area than normal, causing increased chromosome movement. Normally, SPB oscillation occurs during mitotic interphase (as well as prophase) but is restricted to a small space." [PMID:12390246, PMID:19001497, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased mitotic SPB oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased mitotic spindle pole body movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased mitotic spindle pole body oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased SPB-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0005348 ! abnormal spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-04-11T13:12:53Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005350
name: abnormal chromatin organization resulting in peripheral chromatin distribution
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which nuclear chromatin organization is abnormal, such that chromatin is distributed in a ring-shaped structure around the nuclear periphery rather than throughout the nucleus." [PMID:16453724, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal chromatin organisation resulting in peripheral chromatin distribution" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal chromatin organization resulting in peripheral chromatin distribution during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal chromatin organization resulting in peripheral chromatin distribution during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal chromatin organization resulting in ring-shaped chromatin distribution" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abnormal nuclear chromatin organization resulting in peripheral chromatin distribution" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "chromatin abnormally dispersed around nuclear periphery" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0001352 ! abnormal chromatin organization during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-03-16T13:58:17Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005351
name: increased guanyl-nucleotide exchange factor activity
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the observed rate or other property of a guanyl-nucleotide exchange factor activity is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can mean that the mutated gene product itself has greater GEF activity than wild type, or that a mutation in one gene increases GEF activation by a second gene product. When using this term, it is therefore recommended to note the specific protein(s) affected.
synonym: "increased GEF activity" EXACT [GO:0005085]
is_a: FYPO:0000707 ! abnormal molecular function
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-04-11T13:56:31Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005352
name: normal attachment of mitotic spindle microtubules to kinetochore
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the physical attachment of sister chromatids to mitotic spindle microtubules is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal attachment of spindle microtubules to kinetochore mitosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal attachment of mitotic spindle microtubules to kinetochore during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal attachment of spindle microtubules to kinetochore during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001334 ! regulation phenotype during vegetative growth
is_a: FYPO:0003570 ! normal attachment of spindle microtubules to kinetochore
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-04-11T14:01:33Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005353
name: normal replication fork arrest at RTS1 barrier
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which replication fork arrest at the RTS1 barrier is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Note that the RTS1 barrier usually occurs in the mating type locus, but might be assayed at ectopic loci to maximise the distance that a restarted fork travels." [] {comment="PomBase:vw"}
synonym: "normal replication fork arrest at mating-type locus" RELATED []
synonym: "normal replication fork arrest at mating-type locus during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal replication fork arrest at mating-type locus during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0008191 ! normal replication fork arrest
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-04-11T14:59:17Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005354
name: normal site-specific DNA replication termination at RTS1 barrier
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which site-specific DNA replication termination at the RTS1 barrier in the mating type region is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal site-specific DNA replication termination at RTS1 barrier during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal site-specific DNA replication termination at RTS1 barrier during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001319 ! normal cellular process during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-04-11T15:03:01Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005355
name: abnormal site-specific DNA replication termination at RTS1 barrier
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which site-specific DNA replication termination at RTS1 barrier in the mating type region is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal site-specific DNA replication termination at RTS1 barrier during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal site-specific DNA replication termination at RTS1 barrier during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
