[Term]
id: FYPO:0005364
name: decreased rate of kinetochore sliding during chromosome recapture
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate, or speed, of kinetochore sliding, i.e. the movement of a kinetochore along spindle microtubules, during mitotic chromosome recapture is decreased." [PMID:18256284, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that, although the movement affected in this phenotype is often described as "kinetochore migration" or "kinetochore sliding", the entire chromosome moves along the spindle microtubules.
synonym: "decreased rate of chromosome migration during chromosome recapture" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased rate of chromosome movement during chromosome recapture" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased rate of kinetochore migration during chromosome recapture" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
