[Term]
id: FYPO:0005367
name: inviable mononucleate aseptate cell with cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a vegetative cell is inviable, contains one nucleus, has no septum, and progression through the mitotic cell cycle is arrested at the mitotic G2/M phase transition." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that if you have done an experiment that assays the viability of a population of cells, such as looking at colony growth or growth in liquid culture, you should also annotate to 'inviable cell population' (FYPO:0002059) or one of its descendants.
synonym: "inviable mononucleate aseptate cell with mitotic cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable mononucleate aseptate vegetative cell arrested at G2/M" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "inviable mononucleate aseptate vegetative cell with cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
