id: FYPO:0005404
name: telomeric regions absent from linear chromosomes
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromosomes remain linear, but lose telomeric repeats. Subtelomeric DNA may also be lost." [PMID:12930956, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "telomeric regions absent from linear chromosomes during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "telomeric regions absent from linear chromosomes during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000848 ! abnormal chromosome morphology during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-05-04T15:34:59Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005405
name: increased DNA recombination at telomere during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the occurrence of DNA recombination is increased in telomeric regions." [PMID:12930956, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this phenotype can be observed in haploid cells that have not undergone meiosis, sporulation and spore germination.
synonym: "increased DNA recombination at telomere during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA recombination frequency at telomere during vegetative growth" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA recombination rate at telomere during vegetative growth" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased recombination at telomere during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0001345 ! abnormal DNA recombination during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-05-04T15:38:05Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005406
name: increased DNA recombination at telomere following meiotic cell cycle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the occurrence of DNA recombination is increased in telomeric regions in haploid cells that have undergone meiosis, sporulation and spore germination." [PMID:12930956, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA recombination at telomere during meiotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA recombination frequency at telomere following meiotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA recombination rate at telomere following meiotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased recombination at telomere following meiotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0000063 ! abnormal DNA recombination
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-05-04T15:39:46Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005407
name: increased DNA recombination at telomere during nitrogen starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the occurrence of DNA recombination is increased in telomeric regions when the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation." [PMID:12930956, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this phenotype can be observed in haploid cells that have not undergone meiosis, sporulation and spore germination.
synonym: "increased DNA recombination at telomere during nitrogen depletion" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA recombination at telomere during nitrogen deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA recombination frequency at telomere during nitrogen starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA recombination rate at telomere during nitrogen starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased recombination at telomere during nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0000063 ! abnormal DNA recombination
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-05-04T15:41:07Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005408
name: decreased duration of mitotic S phase during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the duration of progression through S phase of the mitotic cell cycle is shorter than normal during a cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term if the duration of S phase is decreased relative to wild type cells exposed to MMS, no matter how the mutant S phase compares to S phase in untreated wild type cells.
synonym: "decreased duration of mitotic S phase during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased duration of mitotic S phase during cellular response to methyl methanesulphonate" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased duration of mitotic S phase during cellular response to MMS" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased duration of S phase during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced duration of mitotic S phase during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000615 ! decreased duration of mitotic S phase
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-05-10T12:00:52Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005409
name: normal protein level during cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase in response to nitrogen starvation
def: "A cell phenotype in which the amount of protein measured in a cell that has arrested the mitotic cell cycle G1 phase in response to nitrogen starvation is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Total protein or a specific protein may be affected." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "normal cellular protein level during cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase in response to nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein accumulation during cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase in response to nitrogen starvation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein level during cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase in response to nitrogen depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "normal protein level during cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase in response to nitrogen deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "normal protein level during mitotic G1 arrest in response to nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein level during nitrogen deprivation-induced G1 arrest" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0004084 ! normal protein level during nitrogen starvation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-05-13T13:14:57Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005410
name: normal protein degradation during mitosis
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which protein degradation is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during mitosis. Protein degradation, also known as protein catabolism, is any metabolic process that results in the destruction of the native, active configuration of a protein, with or without the hydrolysis of peptide bonds." [GO:0030163, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "normal protein breakdown during mitosis" EXACT [GO:0030163, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein catabolic process during mitosis" EXACT [GO:0030163, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein catabolism during mitosis" EXACT [GO:0030163, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein degradation during mitosis during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein degradation during mitosis during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein degradation during mitotic M phase" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein degradation during mitotic nuclear division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002799 ! normal protein degradation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-05-13T13:28:33Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005411
name: increased number of unattached kinetochores
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the attachment of spindle microtubules to the kinetochore results in a larger number of kinetochores remaining unattached than normal." [PMID:18256284, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
