[Term]
id: FYPO:0005418
name: abolished ATPase activator activity
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which a gene product (usually a protein) that normally has ATPase activator activity has no activity in a mutant. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any ATPase activator activity that is abolished by a mutation, whether or not the mutated gene product normally acts as an ATPase activator.
synonym: "ATPase activator activity abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000707 ! abnormal molecular function
is_a: FYPO:0007690 ! catalytic activity regulator phenotype
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-05-13T14:33:16Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005419
name: abnormal mitochondrial crista morphology
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the size, shape, or structure of the mitochondrial cristae is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitochondrial crista morphology during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitochondrial crista morphology during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitochondrial cristae morphology" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
