[Term]
id: FYPO:0005423
name: decreased mitotic spindle microtubule depolymerization during mitotic anaphase A
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which mitotic spindle microtubule depolymerization, i.e. the removal of tubulin dimers from a microtubule in the mitotic spindle, occurs to a lesser extent than normal during anaphase A." [PomBase:mah]
