created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-06-06T13:13:04Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005428
name: delayed onset of UV-damage excision repair
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which UV-damage excision repair begins later than normal. UV-damage excision repair is a DNA repair process that is initiated by an endonuclease that introduces a single-strand incision immediately 5' of a UV-induced damage site, and that acts on both cyclobutane pyrimidine dimers (CPDs) and pyrimidine-pyrimidone 6-4 photoproducts (6-4PPs)." [GO:0070914, PMID:15329725, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed onset of cyclobutane pyrimidine dimer repair" NARROW [GO:0070914]
synonym: "delayed onset of pyrimidine-pyrimidone 6-4 photoproduct repair" NARROW [GO:0070914]
synonym: "delayed onset of removal of 6-4 photoproducts" NARROW [GO:0070914, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "delayed onset of removal of cyclobutane pyrimidine dimers" NARROW [GO:0070914, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "delayed onset of UV-damage excision repair during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed onset of UV-damage excision repair during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed UV-damage excision repair" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000188 ! abnormal DNA repair during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-06-06T13:28:39Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005429
name: decreased UV-damage excision repair during mitotic G2 phase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which UV-damage excision repair occurs to a lower extent than normal during G2 phase of the mitotic cell cycle. UV-damage excision repair is a DNA repair process that is initiated by an endonuclease that introduces a single-strand incision immediately 5' of a UV-induced damage site, and that acts on both cyclobutane pyrimidine dimers (CPDs) and pyrimidine-pyrimidone 6-4 photoproducts (6-4PPs)." [GO:0070914, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased UV-damage excision repair during G2 phase of mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased UV-damage excision repair during mitotic G2 during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced UV-damage excision repair during mitotic G2 phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0004031 ! decreased UV-damage excision repair
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-06-06T13:32:35Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005430
name: aggregated actin cortical patches during vegetative growth
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which actin cortical patches cluster together more than normal." [PMID:8522609, PomBase:mah]
