[Term]
id: FYPO:0005451
name: decreased break-induced loss of heterozygosity
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which one of two different alleles of a gene is lost less frequently than normal after a double-strand break forms nearby." [PMID:17724078, PomBase:mah]
comment: This phenotype may be observed in diploid cells, or in cells that have two copies of one or more reporter loci but are otherwise haploid.
synonym: "decreased break-induced loss of heterozygosity during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased break-induced loss of heterozygosity during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced break-induced loss of heterozygosity" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
