[Term]
id: FYPO:0005491
name: decreased maintenance of protein localization in vacuole, with protein secreted
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the maintenance of protein localization in vacuole occurs to a lower extent than normal, and some of the protein is secreted, i.e. some of a protein that normally resides in the vacuole is instead secreted." [PMID:22484924, PomBase:mah]
comment: The difference between this term and 'decreased protein targeting to vacuole, with protein secreted' (FYPO:0005547) is that this term refers to proteins remaining in the vacuole after they are targeted there, whereas FYPO:0005547 refers to the initial targeting of proteins to the vacuole. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "decreased maintenance of protein localisation in vacuole, with protein secreted" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased maintenance of protein localization in vacuole, with protein secreted, during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
