[Term]
id: FYPO:0005504
name: abolished galactose-specific flocculation
def: "A phenotype in which galactose-specific flocculation does not occur. Galactose-specific flocculation is the non-sexual aggregation of single cells, mediated by the binding of cell wall proteins on one cell to galactose residues on the other." [GO:0036349, PMID:23236291, PomBase:mah]
