[Term]
id: FYPO:0005522
name: increased forward centromeric outer repeat transcript level
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which RNAs transcribed in the forward direction from the centromere outer repeat region are present at greater levels than normal." [PMID:22990236, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term encompasses both unprocessed RNA transcribed from the centromere outer repeat region and siRNAs derived by dicer-mediated processing of the primary transcripts. Use this term only for levels of RNA transcribed from endogenous centromere outer repeat sequences. For levels of RNA transcribed from an exogenous reporter gene placed in the outer repeat region, consider 'decreased chromatin silencing at centromere outer repeat region' (FYPO:0003412).
