[Term]
id: FYPO:0005546
name: decreased protein-protein interaction during mitotic S phase
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of one protein to another occurs to a lower extent than normal during S phase of the mitotic cell cycle. The relevant proteins may include the one encoded by the mutated gene, or may both be encoded by different genes." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any protein-protein interaction that is affected by a mutation, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "decreased protein binding during mitotic S phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced protein-protein interaction during mitotic S phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
