[Term]
id: FYPO:0005547
name: decreased protein targeting to vacuole, with protein secreted
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which protein targeting to the vacuole occurs to a lower extent than normal, and some of the protein is secreted." [PMID:22484924, PomBase:mah]
comment: The difference between this term and 'decreased maintenance of protein localization in vacuole, with protein secreted' (FYPO:0005491) is that this term refers to the initial targeting of proteins to the vacuole, whereas FYPO:0005491 refers to proteins remaining in the vacuole after they are targeted there. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "decreased protein targeting to vacuole, with protein secreted, during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein targeting to vacuole, with protein secreted, during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein partially mislocalized from vacuole to extracellular region" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "reduced protein targeting to vacuole, with protein secreted" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000676 ! abnormal protein targeting to vacuole
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-08-01T13:42:06Z

