[Term]
id: FYPO:0005577
name: decreased protein phosphorylation during meiotic cell cycle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the phosphorylation of one or more specific proteins occurs to a lower extent than normal during the meiotic cell cycle." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any circumstances in which cells are starved for nitrogen. Note that cells may enter G0 (quiescence) when subjected to prolonged nitrogen starvation; this term is not restricted to G0. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "reduced protein phosphorylation during meiotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
