[Term]
id: FYPO:0005626
name: normal mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint during cellular response to UV during mitotic S phase
def: "A cell cycle checkpoint phenotype in which the mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) when the cell is exposed to ultraviolet light during S phase of the mitotic cell cycle. The mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint negatively regulates progression through the G2/M transition of the mitotic cell cycle in response to DNA damage." [PMID:26652183, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal G2 DNA damage checkpoint during cellular response to UV during S phase of mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint activation during cellular response to UV during mitotic S phase" EXACT [PomBase:al]
