[Term]
id: FYPO:0005641
name: abnormal chromosome segregation during meiosis I with premature sister kinetochore separation, lagging chromosomes, and normal chromosome separation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which kinetochores become separated during the first meiotic nuclear division, and in which homologous chromosomes do not move towards the spindle poles at the same time during anaphase, but are eventually separated normally." [PMID:21920317, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: This term describes the premature separation of paired, intact sister kinetochores. It has a related synonym using "split kinetochores" because that phrase is often used in the literature to describe this phenotype. It should not be confused with the FYPO terms that have "split kinetochore" in the names, because those names refer to cases where a single kinetochore has broken into parts.
synonym: "abnormal chromosome segregation during first meiotic nuclear division with premature sister kinetochore separation, lagging chromosomes, and normal chromosome separation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal chromosome segregation during meiosis I with precocious centromeric dissociation, lagging chromosomes, and normal chromosome separation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abnormal chromosome segregation during meiosis I with premature sister kinetochore separation, lagging chromosomes, and normal chromosome segregation" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abnormal chromosome segregation during meiosis I with split kinetochores, lagging chromosomes, and normal chromosome separation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0004159 ! abnormal homologous chromosome segregation
is_a: FYPO:0005633 ! sister kinetochore dissociation in meiotic metaphase I, normal chromosome segregation in meiosis I, and sister chromatid non-disjunction in meiosis II
relationship: has_part FYPO:0004393 ! lagging chromosomes during meiosis I
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-08-26T14:07:01Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005642
name: abnormal meiotic homologous chromosome biorientation with abnormal kinetochore orientation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which homologous chromosome biorientation is abnormal during meiosis, with chromosomes that are not correctly oriented with the kinetochores facing outwards. Homologous chromosome biorientation is the process in which the sister centromeres of one chromosome attach to microtubules that emanate from the same spindle pole, ensuring that homologous maternal and paternal chromosomes are pulled in opposite directions at anaphase of meiosis I." [PMID:21920317, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abnormal homologous chromosome biorientation with abnormal kinetochore orientation during meiosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal homologous chromosome orientation involved in meiotic metaphase I plate congression with abnormal kinetochore orientation" EXACT [GO:0031619]
synonym: "abnormal meiotic homologous chromosome biorientation with abnormal kinetochore position" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003177 ! abnormal meiotic homologous chromosome biorientation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-08-26T14:19:36Z

