creation_date: 2016-09-06T14:47:51Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005653
name: increased level of iron ion starvation-induced proteins during glutathione starvation
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of protein encoded by genes normally induced during iron ion starvation measured in a cell is higher than normal when the cell is subject to glutathione starvation." [PMID:25806539, PomBase:mah]
