[Term]
id: FYPO:0005669
name: obsolete cut with abnormal chromosome segregation during cellular response to hydroxyurea
def: "OBSOLETE. A cut phenotype with abnormal chromosome segregation that is observed when a cell is exposed to hydroxyurea. In this type of cut phenotype, a cell undergoes septation despite abnormal chromosome segregation such that the nucleus forms a single mass through which the septum forms." [PomBase:mah]
