[Term]
id: FYPO:0005691
name: decreased spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the mitotic spindle pole body (SPB) moves rapidly back and forth to a lower extent and over a smaller area than normal, causing decreased chromosome movement. Normally, SPB oscillation occurs during mitotic interphase (as well as prophase) but is restricted to a small space." [PMID:12390246, PMID:19001497, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased mitotic SPB oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased mitotic spindle pole body movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
