id: FYPO:0005743
name: normal invertase activity during glucose starvation
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the observed rate of invertase activity (beta-fructofuranosidase activity) is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) under conditions of glucose starvation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.
synonym: "normal beta-fructofuranosidase activity during glucose starvation" EXACT [GO:0004564]
synonym: "normal invertase activity during cellular response to glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal invertase activity during glucose depletion" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal invertase activity during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal invertase activity during glucose limitation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000660 ! normal catalytic activity
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-11-02T15:03:30Z

