created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-11-04T15:09:40Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005778
name: abnormal chromosome morphology during cellular response to acetaldehyde
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the size, shape, or structure of one or more chromosomes is abnormal during a cellular response to acetaldehyde." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that an abnormal chromosome organization process may, but does not necessarily, result in abnormal chromosome morphology.
synonym: "abnormal chromosome morphology during cellular response to acetaldehyde during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal chromosome morphology during cellular response to acetaldehyde during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000848 ! abnormal chromosome morphology during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-11-04T15:11:12Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005779
name: normal protein localization to kinetochore during mitosis
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of a protein to the kinetochore of a chromosome is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during mitosis." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "normal protein localisation to kinetochore during mitosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein localization to kinetochore during mitotic M phase" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein localization to kinetochore during mitotic nuclear division" RELATED [GO:0140014]
is_a: FYPO:0002901 ! normal protein localization to kinetochore during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-11-09T13:35:38Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005780
name: decreased response to mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint signaling
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which a mitotic cell cycle arrest that normally occurs in response to the mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint is decreased. The mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint normally delays the metaphase/anaphase transition of a mitotic nuclear division until the spindle is correctly assembled and chromosomes are attached to the spindle. In a mutant, the checkpoint may fail to arrest or delay cell cycle progression under appropriate conditions, or the incidence or duration of arrest or delay may differ from wild type under any specified set of conditions." [GO:0072479, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased response to mitotic cell cycle spindle assembly checkpoint signaling" EXACT [GO:0072479]
synonym: "decreased spindle assembly checkpoint during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced response to mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint signaling" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000168 ! abnormal mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-11-09T13:49:57Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005781
name: decreased duration of mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint
def: "A cell cycle checkpoint phenotype in which the duration of cell cycle arrest or delay due to regulation by the mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint is lower than in wild type." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased duration of mitotic cell cycle spindle assembly checkpoint" EXACT [GO:0007094]
synonym: "decreased duration of mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint activation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased duration of mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased duration of spindle assembly checkpoint during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "premature mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint deactivation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced duration of mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000168 ! abnormal mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-11-09T13:50:11Z

