[Term]
id: FYPO:0005784
name: decreased extent and duration of protein-protein interaction
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of one protein to another occurs to a lower extent, and for a shorter time, than normal. The relevant proteins may include the one encoded by the mutated gene, or may both be encoded by different genes." [PMID:26882497, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any protein-protein interaction that is affected by a mutation, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "decreased extent and duration of protein binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased level and duration of protein-protein interaction" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced extent and duration of protein-protein interaction" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001645 ! decreased protein-protein interaction
is_a: FYPO:0005785 ! decreased duration of protein-protein interaction
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-11-09T14:26:18Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005785
name: decreased duration of protein-protein interaction
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of one protein to another occurs for a shorter time than normal. The relevant proteins may include the one encoded by the mutated gene, or may both be encoded by different genes." [PMID:26882497, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any protein-protein interaction that is affected by a mutation, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "decreased duration of protein binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced duration of protein-protein interaction" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000704 ! abnormal protein-protein interaction
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-11-09T14:27:22Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005786
name: decreased spatial extent of double-strand break processing
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which double-strand break processing extends for a shorter distance from the breaks site than normal. Double-strand break processing is the 5' to 3' exonucleolytic resection of the DNA at the site of the break to form a 3' single-strand DNA overhang." [GO:0000729, PMID:27729451, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased spatial extent of double-strand break processing during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased spatial extent of double-strand break processing during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased spatial extent of double-strand break resection" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased spatial extent of DSB processing" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced spatial extent of double-strand break processing" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002553 ! abnormal double-strand break processing
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-11-09T14:36:22Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005787
name: normal spatial extent of double-strand break processing
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which double-strand break processing extends for a normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) distance from the break site. Double-strand break processing is the 5' to 3' exonucleolytic resection of the DNA at the site of the break to form a 3' single-strand DNA overhang." [GO:0000729, PMID:27729451, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of double-strand break processing during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
