[Term]
id: FYPO:0005789
name: C-shaped vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is curved along the long axis to form a \"C\" shape. In a curved cell, the long axis follows a smooth bend rather than a straight line. In a C-shaped cell, the curve is centered at the midpoint of the long axis of the cell." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "C-shaped cell" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "C-shaped cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "C-shaped vegetative cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cell morphology, C-shaped" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
