[Term]
id: FYPO:0005823
name: increased phosphatidylserine externalization
def: "A cell phenotype in which the amount of phosphatidylserine measured in the outer leaflet of the plasma membrane is higher than normal when the cell is in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle. Normally, phosphatidylserine is restricted to the inner leaflet of the plasma membrane." [PMID:20192774, PMID:27886462, PomBase:mah]
comment: The appearance of phosphatidylserine on the external side of the plasma membrane is a marker for apoptosis.
synonym: "increased phosphatidylserine externalisation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased phosphatidylserine externalization during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased phosphatidylserine externalization during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased phosphatidylserine level in external side of cell membrane during vegetative growth" EXACT [GO:0005886]
synonym: "increased phosphatidylserine level in outer leaflet of plasma membrane" EXACT [GO:0009897]
synonym: "increased PS externalization" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001505 ! increased cellular phosphatidylserine level
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-12-05T15:02:42Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005824
name: increased plasma membrane permeability
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the permeability of the plasma membrane to one or more substances is greater than normal." [PMID:27886462, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that an abnormal plasma membrane organization process may, but does not necessarily, result in abnormal plasma membrane morphology.
synonym: "increased plasma membrane permeability during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased plasma membrane permeability during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000364 ! abnormal plasma membrane morphology during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2016-12-05T15:08:33Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005825
name: sensitive to iron
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to iron ions. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of iron ions that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "hypersensitive to iron" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to iron during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to iron during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
