[Term]
id: FYPO:0005872
name: incomplete septum formed from asymmetrically located sites
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the septum is in two asymmetrically located parts and does not completely bisect the cell. Arises when septum assembly begins at two sites which are not on opposite sides of the medial cortex and terminates prematurely on both sides." [PMID:27898700, PomBase:mah]
comment: Consider also annotating to 'abnormal contractile ring localization' (FYPO:0000033) because if the contractile ring forms in an abnormal location, the septum will also do so. The positions of both the contractile ring and the septum are determined by the processes that select the site of cell division.
synonym: "abnormal septum site selection from asymmetrically located sites, forming incomplete septum" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "incomplete division septum formed from asymmetrically located sites" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "incomplete septum formed from asymmetrically located sites during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "incomplete septum formed from asymmetrically located sites during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
