[Term]
id: FYPO:0005883
name: abolished anaerobic cell population growth
def: "A vegetative cell population growth phenotype in which a cell population does not grow under anaerobic conditions." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term for a population of cells that does not grow under anaerobic conditions, but does grow under aerobic or semi-aerobic conditions (a cell population that does not grow at any oxygen level would be considered inviable). Note that cell growth terms refer to growth under aerobic conditions unless stated otherwise.
synonym: "abolished anaerobic vegetative cell population growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "anaerobic cell population growth abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001575 ! abolished vegetative cell population growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2017-01-11T13:45:58Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005884
name: normal growth on myxothiazol
def: "A phenotype in which vegetative cell population growth is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) in a medium containing myxothiazol." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell population growth in presence of myxothiazol" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
