[Term]
id: FYPO:0005887
name: ectopic CENP-A containing chromatin assembly
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromatin containing the histone H3 variant CenH3 (also called CENP-A; Cnp1 in S. pombe) are assembled in one or more regions of the chromosome away from the centromere. CENP-A-containing nucleosomes are normally assembled into chromatin at the centromeres, encompassing the central core and centromeric inner repeat regions." [GO:0034080, PMID:27666591, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "CENP-A containing nucleosome assembly away from centromere" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "ectopic CenH3-containing nucleosome assembly at centromere" RELATED [GO:0034080]
