[Term]
id: FYPO:0005903
name: incomplete actomyosin contractile ring contraction
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which actomyosin contractile ring contraction begins, but stops before the ring completely constricts and is disassembled." [PMID:19570908, PomBase:mah]
