[Term]
id: FYPO:0005904
name: normal rate of protein exchange in actomyosin contractile ring
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate, or speed, of protein exchange in the actomyosin contractile ring is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Normally, proteins including actin and myosin are turned over between the contractile ring and elsewhere in the cytoplasm; exchange is faster during than before ring constriction." [PMID:19570908, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "normal rate of protein exchange in actomyosin contractile ring during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal rate of protein exchange in actomyosin contractile ring during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
