[Term]
id: FYPO:0005935
name: normal meiotic recombination frequency
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the frequency of occurrence of meiotic recombination is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Meiotic recombination is a cellular process in which double strand breaks are formed and repaired through a double Holliday junction intermediate, resulting in the equal exchange of genetic material between non-sister chromatids in a pair of homologous chromosomes." [GO:0007131, PMID:19470480, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal occurrence of meiotic recombination" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0007078 ! normal meiotic cell cycle process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2017-02-20T15:13:46Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005936
name: normal intragenic meiotic recombination frequency
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the frequency of occurrence of intragenic meiotic recombination is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Intragenic meiotic recombination can result in gene conversion events." [PMID:19470480, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal meiotic intragenic recombination frequency" EXACT [PomBase:al]
is_a: FYPO:0007078 ! normal meiotic cell cycle process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2017-02-20T15:18:45Z

