[Term]
id: FYPO:0005939
name: decreased replicative lifespan
def: "A cell population phenotype in which the replicative lifespan of a cell population, i.e. the number of divisions cells in the population undergo before death, is lower than normal." [PMID:28139976, PomBase:mah]
comment: Although each cell has a replicative lifespan in that it divides a certain number of times and then dies, replicative lifespan is often measured at the population level, where it is defined by the number of generations at which 50% of the starting cells are dead.
synonym: "decreased cell population replicative lifespan" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased population replicative lifespan" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced replicative lifespan" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000003 ! cell population phenotype
is_a: FYPO:0001985 ! abnormal phenotype
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2017-02-20T16:04:56Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005940
name: increased replicative lifespan
def: "A cell population phenotype in which the replicative lifespan of a cell population, i.e. the number of divisions cells in the population undergo before death, is higher than normal." [PMID:28139976, PomBase:mah]
comment: Although each cell has a replicative lifespan in that it divides a certain number of times and then dies, replicative lifespan is often measured at the population level, where it is defined by the number of generations at which 50% of the starting cells are dead.
