[Term]
id: FYPO:0005941
name: normal meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Meiotic DNA double-strand break clipping is the process by which SPO11/Rec12-oligonucleotide complexes are removed from 5' DNA double-strand breaks induced during meiosis." [GO:1990898, PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0007078 ! normal meiotic cell cycle process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2017-03-09T14:34:21Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005942
name: normal intergenic meiotic recombination frequency
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the frequency of occurrence of intergenic meiotic recombination is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Intergenic meiotic recombination reflects crossovers between homologous chromosomes." [PMID:19752195, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal meiotic intergenic recombination frequency" EXACT [PomBase:al]
is_a: FYPO:0007078 ! normal meiotic cell cycle process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2017-03-09T14:49:08Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005943
name: decreased break-induced loss of heterozygosity via chromosomal translocation
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromosomal translocation that would result in the loss of one of two different alleles of a gene occurs to a lower extent than normal." [PMID:19798055, PomBase:mah]
comment: This phenotype may be observed in diploid cells, or in cells that have two copies of one or more reporter loci but are otherwise haploid. Loss of heterozygosity associated with chromosomal translocation may result from allelic crossover or break-induced replication. In cells with this phenotype, loss of heterozygosity may or may not occur via a different mechanism, such as chromosomal truncation.
synonym: "decreased break-induced loss of heterozygosity via chromosomal translocation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased break-induced loss of heterozygosity via chromosomal translocation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced break-induced loss of heterozygosity via chromosomal translocation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0005451 ! decreased break-induced loss of heterozygosity
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2017-03-09T15:01:56Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005944
name: increased break-induced loss of heterozygosity via chromosomal truncation
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromosomal truncation that would result in the loss of one of two different alleles of a gene occurs to a greater extent than normal." [PMID:19798055, PomBase:mah]
comment: This phenotype may be observed in diploid cells, or in cells that have two copies of one or more reporter loci but are otherwise haploid. Loss of heterozygosity associated with chromosomal translocation may result from allelic crossover or break-induced replication. In cells with this phenotype, loss of heterozygosity may or may not occur via a different mechanism, such as chromosomal truncation.
synonym: "increased break-induced loss of heterozygosity via chromosomal truncation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased break-induced loss of heterozygosity via chromosomal truncation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
