is_a: FYPO:0007424 ! increased chromosomal truncation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2017-03-09T15:04:12Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005945
name: normal frequency of break-induced loss of heterozygosity
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromosomal truncation that would result in the loss of one of two different alleles of a gene occurs at a normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) frequency." [PMID:19798055, PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001319 ! normal cellular process during vegetative growth
