[Term]
id: FYPO:0005976
name: increased rate of mitotic spindle elongation during anaphase B
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate, or speed, of mitotic spindle elongation is increased during anaphase B." [PMID:27872152, PomBase:mah]
