[Term]
id: FYPO:0005977
name: prion formation
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a soluble protein forms prions, by refolding and assembling into highly ordered, self-propagating detergent- and protease-resistant polymers. Phenotypes associated with prions are inherited in a non-Mendelian manner." [PMID:24021964, PMID:28191457, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "prion formation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "prion formation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
