[Term]
id: FYPO:0005984
name: sensitive to Congo Red
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to the dye Congo Red. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of Congo Red that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "hypersensitive to Congo Red" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to Congo Red during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to Congo Red during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
