[Term]
id: FYPO:0005988
name: abolished microtubule anchoring at cell cortex of cell tip during meiotic cell cycle
def: "A cell phenotype in which microtubule anchoring at the cell cortex of the cell tip does not occur during the meiotic cell cycle. Normally, anchoring maintains the localization of microtubules with their plus ends at the cell cortex." [PMID:25736293, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished microtubule anchoring at cell tip cortex during meiotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished microtubule cortical anchoring at cell tip during meiotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
