creation_date: 2017-04-13T14:51:40Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0005989
name: abnormal protein localization during mating
def: "A cell phenotype that affects the localization of a protein in a cell during conjugation with cellular fusion. A protein may be observed in a place where it is not normally found, absent from a place where it is normally found, or both." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend using one of the more specific terms instead of annotating to this term directly, if possible. If this term is used, we recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay.
