[Term]
id: FYPO:0005993
name: normal cytoplasmic translation
def: "A metabolism phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which translation in the cytoplasm is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Translation is the synthesis of a protein using the sequence of a mature mRNA molecule to specify the sequence of amino acids in a polypeptide chain." [GO:0002181, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term should be used only when an experiment measures protein synthesis directly, e.g. by measuring incorporation of a radiolabeled amino acid. Consider annotating to 'normal protein level' (FYPO:0004083) or one of its descendants.
synonym: "normal cytoplasmic protein biosynthesis" EXACT [GO:0006412, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cytoplasmic protein synthesis" EXACT [GO:0006412, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cytoplasmic translation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cytoplasmic translation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000291 ! translation phenotype
is_a: FYPO:0001319 ! normal cellular process during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2017-04-13T15:56:48Z

