[Term]
id: FYPO:0006010
name: abolished shmoo contact with partner cell
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which a mating projection is assembled but does not meet a cell of the opposite mating type." [PMID:28410370, PomBase:mah]
comment: The difference between this term and FYPO:0001873 is that the former describes failure to make contact with available cells of the opposite mating type, whereas the latter describes shmoo formation when no compatible cells are present.
