[Term]
id: FYPO:0006024
name: normal actin filament binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of a protein to one or more actin filaments is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). The relevant actin-binding protein may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any interaction with actin filaments that is assayed in a mutant, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "normal F-actin binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal filamentous actin binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000703 ! normal protein-protein interaction
