name: normal protein localization to chromatin during mitotic DNA replication
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of a protein to chromatin is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during mitotic DNA replication." [PMID:28481910, PomBase:mah]
