creation_date: 2017-06-05T16:29:49Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006039
name: incomplete mitotic metaphase chromosome recapture
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which mitotic metaphase chromosome recapture does not proceed until the kinetochore has moved all the way to the spindle pole body (SPB), but kinetochores instead pause abnormally near the SPB." [PMID:27146110, PomBase:mah]
