[Term]
id: FYPO:0006047
name: decreased interkinetochore distance before mitotic anaphase
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the distance between sister kinetochores is smaller than normal before the onset of mitotic anaphase." [PMID:27146110, PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term in cases where "stretching" refers to the distance between sister kinetochores of duplicated chromosomes that are bioriented on the spindle during mitosis. Also see 'abnormal kinetochore localization' (FYPO:0001778) and 'abnormal mitotic sister chromatid segregation' (FYPO:0000141).
synonym: "decreased distance between mitotic kinetochores" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
