[Term]
id: FYPO:0006049
name: fluctuating mitotic spindle length
def: "A cell phenotype in which a mitotic spindle assembles, but then undergoes large changes in length, instead of remaining at a constant length or gradually elongating." [PMID:27146110, PomBase:mah]
