[Term]
id: FYPO:0006066
name: abolished tubulin heterodimer binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of a protein to one or more alpha/beta tubulin heterodimers does not occur. The affected protein may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any interaction with tubulin dimers that is affected by a mutation, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "abolished protein-protein interaction with tubulin dimer" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished protein-protein interaction with tubulin heterodimer" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished tubulin dimer binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "tubulin heterodimer binding abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
