[Term]
id: FYPO:0006086
name: increased mitotic sister chromatid bridge formation during replication fork processing
def: "A cell phenotype in which one or more bridges consisting of unresolved intertwined sister chromatids form following replication fork arrest, and persist until mitotic anaphase. Bridges contain dsDNA and RPA-bound ssDNA, and may break, resulting in unequal sister chromatid segregation." [PMID:28475874, PomBase:mah]
