[Term]
id: FYPO:0006165
name: branched, swollen, elongated, multinucleate vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is branched, has more than one nucleus, and has a larger volume and is longer, than normal. In a swollen cell, both length and diameter may be greater than normal, although the cell is only considered elongated if the length:diameter ratio is also greater than normal." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "branched, elongated, swollen, multinucleate vegetative cell" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "branched, swollen, elongated, multinucleate cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
