[Term]
id: FYPO:0006171
name: mitotic spindle elongation during anaphase A
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which mitotic spindle elongation takes place during anaphase A. Normally, the spindle elongates immediately following assembly during prophase, remains at a static length during metaphase and anaphase A, and elongates further during anaphase B." [PMID:21920317, PMID:9802907, PomBase:mah]
