[Term]
id: FYPO:0006195
name: decreased number of elongated microtubule bundles curved around cell end
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which all detectable microtubules are present in fewer bundles than normal (usually only one or two), and bundles are longer than normal and curved around one or both ends of the cell." [PMID:14742702, PMID:16481403, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: Curved microtubules follow a smooth bend rather than a straight line. This phenotype is observed during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle.
synonym: "decreased number of elongated interphase microtubule bundles curved around cell end" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased number of elongated microtubule bundles curved around cell end during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
