[Term]
id: FYPO:0006198
name: inviable binucleate vegetative cell, with normal cell length and increased cell diameter
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is inviable, has two nuclei, and has normal length but a greater diameter than normal." [PMID:20805322, PomBase:mah]
comment: When using this term, also consider annotating to a cell cycle arrest term, such as 'abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic telophase' (FYPO:0000622); 'abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic anaphase' (FYPO:0000619) may be applicable if the assay detects DNA masses. Binucleate cells often arise as a result of cell cycle arrest.
