[Term]
id: FYPO:0006199
name: inviable stubby multinucleate vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a vegetatively growing cell is inviable and has more than one nucleus, and the cell diameter is larger than normal and the cell length is shorter than normal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that if you have done an experiment that assays the viability of a population of cells, such as looking at colony growth or growth in liquid culture, you should also annotate to 'inviable cell population' (FYPO:0002059) or one of its descendants.
