[Term]
id: FYPO:0006211
name: inviable after spore germination, before germ tube formation
def: "A phenotype in which a spore germinates but dies before forming a germ tube or dividing. Such spores exit dormancy and undergo isotropic swelling but the spore wall does not rupture and no germ tube emerges." [PMID:28572514, PomBase:mah]
comment: Spores with this phenotype can be identified by loss of spore refractility that can be observed by light microscopy or by a decrease in optical absorbance of the spore suspension.
synonym: "inviable following spore germination, before germ tube formation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable germinated spore, without germ tube formation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "lethal after spore germination, before germ tube formation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
