creation_date: 2017-10-18T14:53:22Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006254
name: abnormal ribosome footprint size distribution
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the distribution of ribosomal footprint lengths in a cell differs from wild type. Ribosomal footprints are RNA fragments protected by the ribosome, and normally range from 28-31 nucleotides long." [PMID:28945192, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal ribosome footprint length distribution" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal ribosome footprint size distribution during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal ribosome footprint size distribution during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
