[Term]
id: FYPO:0006315
name: abolished homologous chromosome segregation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which homologous chromosome segregation does not occur. Homologous chromosome segregation is the process in which replicated homologous chromosomes are organized and then physically separated and apportioned to two sets during the first division of the meiotic cell cycle." [GO:0045143, PMID:29259000, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished chromosome segregation during meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "homologous chromosome segregation abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0004159 ! abnormal homologous chromosome segregation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-05T11:30:51Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006316
name: spindle pole bodies present in increased numbers during meiosis II
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which cells contain more spindle pole bodies (SPBs) than normal during the second meiotic nuclear division." [PMID:29259000, PomBase:mah]
