[Term]
id: FYPO:0006318
name: decreased DNA resection during replication fork processing
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the extent of DNA resection upstream of a stalled replication fork is lower than normal. DNA resection is the 5'-to-3' degradation of one strand of DNA, leaving a stretch of single-stranded DNA." [PMID:29215009, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DNA resection during replication fork processing during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DNA resection during replication fork processing during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
