[Term]
id: FYPO:0006319
name: normal extent of DNA resection during replication fork processing
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the extent of DNA resection upstream of a stalled replication fork is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). DNA resection is the 5'-to-3' degradation of one strand of DNA, leaving a stretch of single-stranded DNA." [PMID:29215009, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal DNA resectioning during replication fork processing" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal extent of DNA resection during replication fork processing during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
