[Term]
id: FYPO:0006320
name: normal replication slippage during replication fork processing
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the increase in small deletions or duplications (\"replication slippage\") that normally results from processing arrested replication forks is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PMID:29215009, PomBase:mah]
