[Term]
id: FYPO:0006323
name: loss of viability following replication fork stalling
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable after stalled replication forks accumulate." [PMID:29215009, PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term to annotate experiments in which a culture is grown under conditions that cause replication fork stalling, and then the number of cells viable enough to form a colony upon return to conditions supporting vegetative growth (without fork stalling) is measured and compared to wild type.
synonym: "decreased viability following replication fork stalling" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of cell population viability following replication fork stalling" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced viability following replication fork stalling" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
