[Term]
id: FYPO:0006327
name: abnormal rate of protein exchange in medial cortical node
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate, or speed, of protein exchange in the medial cortical nodes is abnormal. Normally, myosin and other node proteins are turned over between the nodes and elsewhere at rates consistent for each protein." [PMID:21422229, PomBase:mah]
