created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-23T15:13:12Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006340
name: endocytosis restricted to old cell end
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which endocytosis occurs only at the old end of the cell during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle. Normally, endocytosis takes place at the old cell end throughout interphase, and also at the new end after NETO." [PMID:16141239, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "endocytosis abolished at new cell end" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "endocytosis restricted to old cell end during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "endocytosis restricted to old cell end during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "endocytosis restricted to old cell end during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "endocytosis restricted to old cell tip" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000034 ! abnormal endocytosis during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-23T15:30:42Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006341
name: abolished equatorial endocytosis during mitosis
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which endocytosis does not occur in the equatorial region of the cell during mitosis as in wild-type cells." [PMID:16141239, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished endocytosis to cell division site" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abolished equatorial endocytosis during cell division" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished equatorial endocytosis during M phase of mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished equatorial endocytosis during mitosis during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished equatorial endocytosis during mitotic M phase" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "endocytosis restricted to cell end during mitosis" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "equatorial endocytosis abolished during mitosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000034 ! abnormal endocytosis during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-23T15:32:38Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006342
name: decreased microtubule binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of a protein to one or more microtubules occurs to a lower extent than normal. The affected protein may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any interaction with actin filaments that is affected by a mutation, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "reduced microtubule binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001943 ! abnormal microtubule binding
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-26T11:11:38Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006343
name: abolished microtubule bundle formation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which microtubule bundle formation, which normally results in a parallel arrangement of microtubules, does not occur." [GO:0001578, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished microtubule array formation" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abolished microtubule bundling" EXACT [GO:0001578]
synonym: "microtubule bundle formation abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002761 ! abnormal microtubule bundle formation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-26T11:19:54Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006344
name: protein mislocalized to plasma membrane during vegetative growth
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a protein that is not normally found at the plasma membrane is observed there." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term can be used to annotate any case where a protein is found in the medial cortex in a mutant, but not in wild type. In some cases, there may be enough additional information to annotate to 'abnormal protein localization' (FYPO:0000443) or one of its descendants. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "ectopic protein localization to plasma membrane during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "protein mislocalised to plasma membrane during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein mislocalized to plasma membrane during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000782 ! mislocalized protein during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-26T11:41:52Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006345
name: increased duration of protein phosphorylation during nitrogen starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the duration of protein phosphorylation is longer than normal the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation. All phosphorylation may be affected, or only phosphorylation of specific proteins, or even specific sites within specific proteins." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased duration of protein phosphorylation during cellular response to nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "prolonged protein phosphorylation during nitrogen starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0005033 ! abnormal protein phosphorylation during nitrogen starvation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-26T11:49:06Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006346
name: bipolar mitotic spindle with decreased, irregular thickness
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the mitotic spindle has two poles and can elongate during anaphase, but has decreased and non-uniform thickness along its length." [PMID:12951601, PomBase:mah]
comment: In images of thin spindles, polar microtubules may appear not to reach continuously from pole to pole.
synonym: "bipolar mitotic spindle with decreased, irregular thickness during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "bipolar mitotic spindle with decreased, irregular thickness during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased, irregular bipolar mitotic spindle thickness" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "thin, discontinuous bipolar mitotic spindle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001574 ! abnormal bipolar mitotic spindle
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-26T11:59:01Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006347
name: sensitive to mechlorethamine
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to mechlorethamine. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of mechlorethamine that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "hypersensitive to mechlorethamine" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to 2-chloro-N-(2-chloroethyl)-N-methylethanamine" EXACT [CHEBI:28925]
synonym: "sensitive to bis(2-chloroethyl)methylamine" EXACT [CHEBI:28925]
synonym: "sensitive to HN2" EXACT [PMID:24192486]
synonym: "sensitive to mechlorethamine during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to mechlorethamine during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000127 ! increased sensitivity to chemical during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-01-29T15:23:41Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006348
name: normal growth on mechlorethamine
def: "A phenotype in which vegetative cell population growth is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) in a medium containing mechlorethamine." [PomBase:mah]
