[Term]
id: FYPO:0006352
name: normal F-actin level in actomyosin contractile ring during early mitosis
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of filamentous actin (F-actin) in the actomyosin contractile ring is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during early mitosis (before anaphase)." [PMID:29343550, PomBase:mah]
