name: abolished histone RNA level oscillation during mitotic cell cycle
def: "A gene expression phenotype in which the levels of RNAs that encode histones, which normally vary over the course of the mitotic cell cycle, remain constant. All RNAs encoding histones, or one or more specific histone RNA, may be affected." [PMID:17452352, PomBase:mah]
