comment: This term can be used for protein transport or for the movement of other substances (e.g. lipids or ions) via vesicles. If it is used for a protein transport phenotype, we recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay.
synonym: "normal vesicle-mediated protein transport during vegetative growth" NARROW [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal vesicle-mediated transport during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001071 ! normal transport
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-03-09T13:19:53Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006433
name: abnormal tubular endoplasmic reticulum morphology
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the size, shape, or structure of the tubular endoplasmic reticulum (ER) is abnormal. The tubular ER is the portion of the ER that consists of tubules having membranes with high curvature in cross-section." [GO:0071782, PomBase:mah]
