created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-03-09T13:20:19Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006434
name: decreased protein localization to medial cortical node, with protein distributed in cell cortex, during vegetative growth
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of a protein to the medial cortical node of a cell is decreased, and the protein is instead detected distributed throughout the cell cortex. There may be little or no protein detected at the medial cortical node." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "cortical drift" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
