[Term]
id: FYPO:0006435
name: increased FAD binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which occurrence of FAD binding by a gene product (usually a protein) in a mutant is increased. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can mean that the mutated gene product itself binds FAD more than wild type, or that a mutation in one gene increases FAD binding by a second gene product. When using this term, it is therefore recommended to note the specific protein(s) affected.
synonym: "increased oxidized flavin adenine dinucleotide binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
