[Term]
id: FYPO:0006475
name: mitotic spindle collapse
def: "A cell phenotype in which a short mitotic spindle assembles, and may begin elongation, but does not elongate normally or completely, and eventually collapses. Upon collapse the spindle may break or shrink." [PMID:15147872, PMID:23885124, PMID:25375240, PMID:27697865, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "broken mitotic spindle" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
