[Term]
id: FYPO:0006478
name: decreased mitotic cohesin dsDNA (leading strand) loading
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cohesin dsDNA (leading strand) loading is decreased during the mitotic cell cycle. Cohesin dsDNA (leading strand) loading is the topological linking of a cohesin ring complex to double-stranded DNA, i.e. the leading strand, in chromatin." [GO:0062021, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cohesin dsDNA (leading strand) loading during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cohesin dsDNA (leading strand) loading during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
