def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the number of ribosomal DNA (rDNA) repeats present in the rDNA arrays on chromosome III is significantly lower than the range in wild type cells." [PMID:19205745, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased copy number of rDNA repeats" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "decreased copy number of rDNA repeats during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "decreased rDNA copy number during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased ribosomal DNA copy number during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "shortened rDNA during vegetative growth" RELATED [PomBase:al]
is_a: FYPO:0004823 ! abnormal rDNA copy number
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-04-09T15:44:54Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006495
name: increased number of R-loops at tRNA genes
