[Term]
id: FYPO:0006500
name: premature cell wall disassembly at cell fusion site
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which disassembly of the cell wall at the site of cell-cell fusion during mating begins earlier than normal, e.g. before pairing with a partner cell. Premature cell wall breakdown often results in cell lysis." [PMID:29453312, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "advanced cell wall disassembly at cell fusion site" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "premature cell wall disassembly at cell fusion site during conjugation with cellular fusion" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "premature cell wall disassembly at cell fusion site during mating" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
