created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-04-18T11:36:26Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006501
name: premature actin fusion focus assembly
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which actin fusion focus assembly begins earlier than normal. An actin fusion focus normally forms during mating at the site where the two cells will fuse." [PMID:29453312, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "advanced actin fusion focus assembly" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "premature actin fusion focus formation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0006108 ! abnormal actin fusion focus assembly
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-04-18T11:43:05Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006502
name: abolished protein localization to cell cortex of cell tip during vegetative growth
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of a protein to the cell cortex of one or both cell tips does not occur." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
