[Term]
id: FYPO:0006518
name: loss of viability in G0
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable after entering G0 phase." [PMID:29167439, PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term to annotate experiments in which a culture is grown under nitrogen-depleted conditions until cells enter G0, and then the number of cells viable enough to form a colony upon return to conditions supporting vegetative growth is measured and compared to wild type.
synonym: "loss of viability in cell quiescence" EXACT [GO:0044838, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of viability in quiescence" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001178 ! loss of viability upon nitrogen starvation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-04-25T14:18:53Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006519
name: decreased protein degradation during mitotic G1 phase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the occurrence of protein degradation is decreased during G1 phase of the mitotic cell cycle." [PomBase:mah]
