is_a: FYPO:0002737 ! abnormal mitotic cell cycle process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-04-25T15:02:09Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006522
name: loss of viability following cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable after arrest at the mitotic G2/M phase transition of the mitotic cell cycle." [PMID:11598020, PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term to annotate experiments in which a culture is grown under conditions that arrest at the G2/M phase transition (e.g. restrictive temperature for a cdc mutant), and then the number of cells viable enough to form a colony upon return to conditions supporting vegetative growth is measured and compared to wild type.
synonym: "decreased viability following cell cycle arrest in mitotic G2 phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of cell population viability following cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of viability following mitotic G2/M arrest" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of viability of mitotic G2-arrested cells" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "reduced viability following cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001985 ! abnormal phenotype
is_a: FYPO:0002057 ! cell population viability
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-04-25T15:17:55Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006523
name: loss of viability in stationary phase following entry from mitotic G2 phase
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable after entering stationary phase following arrest at the mitotic G2/M phase transition of the mitotic cell cycle." [PMID:11598020, PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term to annotate experiments in which a culture is grown under conditions that induce stationary phase entry from G2 phase (e.g. minimal medium lacking either glucose or sulfate), and then the number of cells viable enough to form a colony upon return to conditions supporting vegetative growth is measured and compared to wild type.
synonym: "decreased viability in stationary phase following entry from mitotic G2 phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of cell population viability in stationary phase following entry from mitotic G2 phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of viability following mitotic G2 arrest and stationary phase entry" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of viability in stationary phase following entry from mitotic G2/M phase transition" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of viability of following entry into stationary phase from mitotic G2 phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced viability in stationary phase following entry from mitotic G2 phase" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000245 ! loss of viability in stationary phase
is_a: FYPO:0006522 ! loss of viability following cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-04-25T15:20:18Z

