[Term]
id: FYPO:0006537
name: loss of viability following cellular response to pheromone
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable after exposure to a pheromone." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term to annotate experiments in which a culture is grown in the presence of hydroxyurea, and then the number of cells viable enough to form a colony upon hydroxyurea removal is measured and compared to wild type.
