[Term]
id: FYPO:0006564
name: sensitive to ethanol in stationary phase
def: "A phenotype in which cells show increased sensitivity to ethanol when the cell population is in stationary phase. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of ethanol that allows wild type cells to grow." [PMID:9372444, PomBase:mah]
