[Term]
id: FYPO:0006565
name: normal viability upon phosphate starvation
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable under conditions of phosphate starvation." [PMID:9372444, PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term to annotate experiments in which a culture is grown to stationary phase under phosphate-depleted conditions, and then the number of cells viable enough to form a colony upon return to conditions supporting vegetative growth is measured and compared to wild type.
synonym: "normal cell population viability upon phosphate starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000257 ! normal phenotype
is_a: FYPO:0002057 ! cell population viability
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-06-08T13:58:06Z

