[Term]
id: FYPO:0006578
name: normal mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint
def: "A cell cycle checkpoint phenotype in which the mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). The mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint negatively regulates progression through the G2/M transition of the mitotic cell cycle in response to DNA damage." [PomBase:mah]
