[Term]
id: FYPO:0006633
name: increased cell length
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which cell length, i.e. the maximum distance between the cell ends, is greater than normal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term includes both elongated cells, in which both the length and length:diameter ratio are increased relative to wild type, and cells that have increased length but a wild-type length:diameter ratio.
