[Term]
id: FYPO:0006636
name: mislocalized protein distributed in cell cortex
def: "A cell phenotype in which a protein is detected abnormally distributed throughout the cell cortex. The protein may normally be restricted to part of the cell cortex, or not normally located in the cell cortex at all." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for protein that do not normally localize to discrete cytoplasmic regions, or for proteins that do normally show punctate localization but with such localization increased in a mutant. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "mislocalised protein distributed in cell cortex" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mislocalized protein distributed at cell surface" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mislocalized protein distributed in cell cortex during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
