[Term]
id: FYPO:0006660
name: loss of viability upon G0 to G1 transition
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable upon exiting G0 phase." [PMID:30116786, PomBase:mah]
comment: Also see the cell-level term 'inviable cell upon G0 to G1 transition' (FYPO:0000238). Use this term to annotate experiments in which a culture is grown under nitrogen-depleted conditions until cells have entered and remained for some time in G0, and then the number of cells that can exit G0 and form a colony upon return to conditions supporting vegetative growth is measured and compared to wild type.
synonym: "loss of mitotic competence upon recovery from cell quiescence" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
