[Term]
id: FYPO:0006672
name: transient cell fusion during mating followed by meiotic cell cycle entry and sporulation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which mating cells undergo transient cell fusion (cytogamy), and then one or both cells undergo haploid meiosis and sporulation. In transient cytogamy, cells fuse for a much shorter time than normal during mating, separate with incomplete exchange of cytosol contents, and the conjugation pore then reseals." [PMID:30089908, PomBase:mah]
