[Term]
id: FYPO:0006686
name: decreased DNA double-strand break processing
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which DNA double-strand break resection is decreased. DNA double-strand break resection is the process by which long-tract single-stranded 3'-end DNA is generated by removal of bases from a 5' end from which SPO11/Rec12-oligonucleotide complexes have been removed." [GO:0000729, PMID:21931565, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DNA double-strand break resection" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DNA double-strand break resectioning" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DSB processing" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced DNA double-strand break processing" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000063 ! abnormal DNA recombination
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-09-28T14:33:13Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006687
name: decreased DNA double-strand break processing during double-strand break repair via homologous recombination
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which DNA double-strand break resection that occurs as part of double-strand break repair via homologous recombination is decreased. DNA double-strand break resection is the process by which long-tract single-stranded 3'-end DNA is generated by removal of bases from a 5' end from which SPO11/Rec12-oligonucleotide complexes have been removed." [PMID:21931565, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DNA double-strand break resection during double-strand break repair via homologous recombination" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DNA double-strand break resectioning during double-strand break repair via homologous recombination" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DSB processing during double-strand break repair via homologous recombination" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced DNA double-strand break processing during double-strand break repair via homologous recombination" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0006686 ! decreased DNA double-strand break processing
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-09-28T14:46:18Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006688
name: increased transversion frequency
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which transversion mutations occur at a higher frequency than normal." [PMID:14599746, PomBase:mah]
comment: See SO:1000017.
is_a: FYPO:0000256 ! mutator
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-10-10T10:31:10Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006689
name: increased insertion/deletion frequency
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which insertion or deletion mutations occur at a higher frequency than normal." [PMID:14599746, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased indel frequency" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased insertion or deletion frequency" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000256 ! mutator
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-10-10T10:42:11Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006690
name: obsolete mitotic catastrophe with abnormal chromosome segregation
def: "OBSOLETE. A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell proceeds through the mitotic metaphase/anaphase transition in the presence of an uncorrected problem (such as chromosome structure or kinetochore attachment), and as a result undergoes abnormal chromosome segregation and subsequently dies." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because "mitotic catastrophe" has not been clearly defined for fission yeast.
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe with abnormal chromosome segregation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe with abnormal chromosome segregation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_obsolete: true
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-10-16T13:32:39Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006691
name: obsolete mitotic catastrophe with abnormal nuclear envelope partitioning
def: "OBSOLETE. A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell proceeds through the mitotic metaphase/anaphase transition in the presence of an uncorrected problem (such as chromosome structure or kinetochore attachment), and as a result undergoes abnormal nuclear envelope partitioning and subsequently dies." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This term was made obsolete because "mitotic catastrophe" has not been clearly defined for fission yeast.
synonym: "cut-like" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe with abnormal nuclear envelope partitioning during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic catastrophe with abnormal nuclear envelope partitioning during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_obsolete: true
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-10-16T13:38:48Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006692
name: cut with septum between unequally sized nuclei
def: "An inviable phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell undergoes septation despite abnormal mitotic sister chromatid separation, producing inviable daughter cells, and in which the septum forms so as to separate the nucleus into two unequal masses, each in one compartment." [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: In cells with this phenotype, septation has proceeded despite chromosome segregation failing to complete normally. Chromosome separation is entirely abolished. Consider also annotating to 'cut' (FYPO:0003155) or its descendants, because these phenotypes often co-occur.
synonym: "cut with septum between unequally sized nuclei during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cut with septum between unequally sized nuclei during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cut with unequally sized nuclei, one either side of septum" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "septation following abnormal mitotic sister chromatid segregation, with septum between unequally sized nuclei" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000229 ! cut
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-10-16T14:20:39Z

