[Term]
id: FYPO:0006708
name: abolished protein phosphorylation during glucose starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the phosphorylation of one or more specific proteins, or of specific protein sites, does not occur when the cell is subject to glucose starvation." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term. Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.
synonym: "abolished protein phosphorylation during cellular response to glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished protein phosphorylation during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein phosphorylation abolished during glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002678 ! abolished protein phosphorylation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-10-30T12:46:35Z

