[Term]
id: FYPO:0006715
name: large and small daughter nuclei
def: "A mitosis phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the nucleus divides unequally to produce one daughter nucleus that is larger than the other." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: This phenotype does not necessarily reflect a chromosome segregation defect. It may instead arise from abnormal nuclear envelope assembly, following normal chromosome segregation.
synonym: "large and small daughter nuclei during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "large and small daughter nuclei during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000062 ! abnormal nuclear morphology during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-10-30T13:23:50Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006716
name: large and small daughter nuclei, with unequal nuclear envelope distribution
def: "A mitosis phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromosomes segregate equally (i.e. normally), but the nuclear envelope is not distributed equally between daughter nuclei. As a result, the nucleus divides unequally to produce one daughter nucleus that is larger than the other." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "large and small daughter nuclei, with unequal nuclear envelope and equal mitotic sister chromatid segregation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "large and small daughter nuclei, with unequal nuclear envelope distribution, during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "large and small daughter nuclei, with unequal nuclear envelope distribution, during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "large and small daughter nuclei, with unequal nuclear envelope partitioning" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0006715 ! large and small daughter nuclei
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-10-30T13:23:56Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006717
