[Term]
id: FYPO:0006763
name: abolished meiotic cell cycle DNA replication checkpoint
def: "A cell cycle checkpoint phenotype in which cell cycle regulation mediated by the meiotic cell cycle DNA replication checkpoint does not occur under conditions that normally trigger the checkpoint signaling and response. The meiotic DNA replication checkpoint normally prevents the initiation of meiotic nuclear division until pre-meiotic DNA replication is complete." [GO:0033315, PMID:10521402, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished meiotic DNA replication checkpoint" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished meiotic G2/MI DNA replication checkpoint" EXACT [GO:0033315]
is_a: FYPO:0005511 ! meiotic cell cycle checkpoint phenotype
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-11-21T15:02:02Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006764
name: normal activation of meiotic cell cycle DNA replication checkpoint
def: "A cell cycle checkpoint phenotype in which the meiotic cell cycle DNA replication checkpoint is activated at a normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) frequency, under conditions that cause checkpoint activation in wild-type cells. The meiotic DNA replication checkpoint delays the meiotic nuclear division until pre-meiotic DNA replication is complete." [PMID:10521402, PomBase:mah]
comment: Checkpoint activation in a mutant usually implies that the mutation is causing problems that the checkpoint detects.
synonym: "normal activation of meiotic DNA replication checkpoint" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal activation of meiotic G2/MI DNA replication checkpoint" EXACT [GO:0033315]
synonym: "normal meiotic DNA replication checkpoint activation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0005511 ! meiotic cell cycle checkpoint phenotype
is_a: FYPO:0006915 ! normal cell cycle process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-11-21T15:13:22Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006765
