[Term]
id: FYPO:0006772
name: dispersed actin cortical patch localization during mating
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which actin cortical patches are localized throughout the cell cortex during mating. Normally, actin cortical patches concentrate in the mating projection tip and conjugation bridge during cell fusion, and then disperse after karyogamy." [PMID:20123972, PomBase:mah]
