[Term]
id: FYPO:0006782
name: decreased protein level in large ribosomal subunit precursor
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of a protein measured in a complex that is a precursor of the large ribosomal subunit is lower than normal." [PMID:27667686, PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term for cases where the relative abundance of one or more specific proteins in the proteasome is decreased, altering the proteasome stoichiometry. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "decreased large ribosomal subunit precursor complex protein level during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
