is_a: FYPO:0001324 ! decreased protein level during vegetative growth
is_a: FYPO:0005003 ! abnormal protein complex composition
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2018-11-30T09:52:16Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006783
name: increased level of carbohydrate metabolism gene mRNA during vegetative growth
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of one or more carbohydrate metabolism RNAs measured in a cell is higher than normal (i.e. higher than observed in wild-type cells). Carbohydrate metabolism RNAs are transcribed from genes whose products are involved in metabolism of one or more carbohydrates." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Consider annotating to a term describing abnormal transcription or abnormal regulation of transcription, but note that changes in RNA levels may result from changes in RNA stability as well as changes in transcription.
synonym: "increased carbohydrate metabolism gene mRNA accumulation during vegetative growth" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased level of carbohydrate metabolism gene mRNA during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased level of carbohydrate metabolism gene RNA during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased level of carbohydrate metabolism gene transcripts during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
