created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-01-04T14:16:29Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006799
name: abolished nuclear MIS12/MIND complex binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which nuclear MIS12/MIND complex binding by a gene product (usually a protein) in a mutant does not occur. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PMID:29180432, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any interaction with a protein complex that is assayed in a mutant, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
