created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-01-04T14:18:57Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006800
name: decreased centromere clustering at nuclear periphery during mitotic interphase
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of centromeres and associated kinetochores into a cluster at the nuclear periphery is decreased during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle. Centromere-kinetochore complexes normally cluster near the old spindle pole body during mitotic interphase." [PMID:29180432, PomBase:mah]
