[Term]
id: FYPO:0006819
name: normal vegetative cell growth rate
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which cells elongate at a normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) rate during the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle. Cell growth is the process in which a cell irreversibly increases in size over time by accretion and biosynthetic production of matter similar to that already present." [GO:0016049, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term refers to growth at the level of any individual cell, and that it specifies only that the rate of increase in cell size due to metabolism is normal. Other aspects of the cell's biology may be abnormal, and other abnormalities may affect increase in cell number (population growth). Also see 'cell population growth phenotype' (FYPO:0000139) and its descendants.
is_a: FYPO:0000627 ! normal cellular process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-02-01T13:09:35Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006820
name: abnormal cell growth rate
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the rate of cell growth is abnormal. Cell growth is the irreversible increase in size over time by accretion and biosynthetic production of matter similar to that already present." [GO:0016049, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term refers to growth, i.e. increase in size, of an individual cell. If you have measured the rate or extent of growth of a culture in liquid medium or on plates, use one of the 'cell population growth' terms.
is_a: FYPO:0002862 ! abnormal cell growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-02-01T13:17:19Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006821
name: slow vegetative cell growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which cells elongate more slowly than normal in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term refers to growth, i.e. increase in size, of an individual cell. If you have measured the rate or extent of growth of a culture in liquid medium or on plates, use one of the 'cell population growth' terms.
is_a: FYPO:0006820 ! abnormal cell growth rate
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-02-01T13:19:17Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0006822
name: viable small vegetative cell with normal cell growth rate
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a vegetatively growing cell is viable and elongates at a normal rate, but divides when a shorter time than normal has elapsed since the previous cell division. Daughter cells therefore have an abnormally low volume. Note that these small viable cells result from a cell cycle size regulation defect." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that if you have done an experiment that assays the viability of a population of cells, such as looking at colony growth or growth in liquid culture, you should also annotate to 'viable cell population' (FYPO:0002058) or one of its descendants.
synonym: "mitosis with small cell size and normal cell growth rate" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "reduced size at cell division with normal cell growth rate" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "small viable vegetative cell with normal cell growth rate" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "viable small cell with normal cell growth rate during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "viable small vegetative cell with normal cell growth rate" BROAD []
synonym: "viable small vegetative cell with normal cell growth rate during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "viable small vegetative cell with premature mitosis" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "wee" EXACT [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000648 ! viable small vegetative cell
relationship: has_part FYPO:0001046 ! premature mitosis
relationship: has_part FYPO:0006819 ! normal vegetative cell growth rate
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-02-01T13:31:57Z

[Term]
