def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which nucleosomes containing the histone H3 variant CenH3 (also called CENP-A; Cnp1 in S. pombe) are assembled over a normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) portion of the centromeric region of the chromosome. CENP-A-containing nucleosomes are assembled into chromatin around centromeres, encompassing the central core and centromeric inner repeat regions." [GO:0000729, PMID:28904333, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal extent of CENP-A containing nucleosome" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of CenH3-containing nucleosome assembly at centromere" RELATED [GO:0034080]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of CENP-A containing nucleosome assembly at centromere" EXACT [GO:0034080]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of CENP-A containing nucleosome assembly during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of CENP-A containing nucleosome assembly during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of CENP-A deposition" RELATED [GO:0034080]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of CENP-A loading" RELATED [GO:0034080]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of centromere-specific histone exchange" EXACT [GO:0034080]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of centromere-specific nucleosome assembly" EXACT [GO:0034080]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of centromeric DNA replication-independent nucleosome assembly" EXACT [GO:0034080]
synonym: "normal spatial extent of DNA replication-independent nucleosome assembly at centromere" EXACT [GO:0034080]
is_a: FYPO:0001319 ! normal cellular process during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-03-04T15:09:53Z

