[Term]
id: FYPO:0006866
name: increased rate of protein exchange in actomyosin contractile ring
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate, or speed, of protein exchange in the actomyosin contractile ring is increased. Normally, proteins including actin and myosin are turned over between the contractile ring and elsewhere in the cytoplasm; exchange is faster during than before ring constriction." [PMID:30928696, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased rate of protein exchange in actomyosin contractile ring during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased rate of protein exchange in actomyosin contractile ring during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
