[Term]
id: FYPO:0006902
name: loss of viability following cellular response to 4-nitroquinoline N-oxide
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable after exposure to 4-nitroquinoline N-oxide." [PomBase:mah]
