[Term]
id: FYPO:0006915
name: normal cell cycle process
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which a cell executes a cell cycle process normally (i.e. indistinguishably from wild type). A cell cycle process is any of the processes that form part of the cell cycle, and thereby ensures successive accurate and complete genome replication and chromosome segregation." [GO:0022402, PomBase:mah]
comment: This is a high-level term whose primary purpose is to organize terms beneath it in the ontology, and we expect that it will not be used for direct annotations. Please consider using a more specific term to annotate each phenotype.
subset: qc_do_not_manually_annotate
is_a: FYPO:0003832 ! normal cell cycle
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-06-10T15:23:05Z

[Term]
