[Term]
id: FYPO:0007010
name: secondary siRNA absent from cell
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of secondary siRNA measured in a cell is too low to detect. Secondary siRNAs are sequences homologous to regions 5' and 3' to the initial siRNA, and their production amplifies the primary siRNA signal." [PMID:20062003, PMID:22542102, PomBase:al, PomBase:mah]
