[Term]
id: FYPO:0007032
name: increased protein glycosylation during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the glycosylation of one or more specific proteins, or of specific protein sites, occurs to a greater extent than normal. Protein glycosylation is the addition of a carbohydrate or carbohydrate derivative unit to a protein amino acid." [GO:0006486, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased protein glycosylation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
