[Term]
id: FYPO:0007078
name: normal meiotic cell cycle process
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which a cell executes a meiotic cell cycle process normally (i.e. indistinguishably from wild type). A meiotic cell cycle process is any of the processes that form part of the meiotic cell cycle, and thereby ensures successive accurate and complete genome replication and meiotic chromosome segregation." [GO:0022402, PomBase:mah]
comment: This is a high-level term whose primary purpose is to organize terms beneath it in the ontology, and we expect that it will not be used for direct annotations. Please consider using a more specific term to annotate each phenotype.
