[Term]
id: FYPO:0007097
name: ectopic actin fusion focus assembly
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which actin fusion focus assembly takes place in one or more abnormal locations. An actin fusion focus normally forms during mating at the site where the two cells will fuse. Ectopic fusion foci often form near actin cortical patches, and may also have abnormal composition." [PMID:31495586, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "ectopic actin fusion focus formation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mislocalized actin fusion focus assembly" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0006108 ! abnormal actin fusion focus assembly
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-10-11T12:12:09Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007098
name: normal growth on vanadate
def: "A phenotype in which vegetative cell population growth is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) in a medium containing vanadate ions (VO4(3-))." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell population growth in presence of vanadate" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell population growth on vanadate" EXACT [PomBase:al, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
