creation_date: 2019-10-11T13:43:34Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007099
name: normal spindle elongation in meiosis I
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the lengthening of the distance between poles of the meiotic spindle that occurs as part of the first meiotic nuclear division is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PomBase:mah]
comment: This is a high-level term whose primary purpose is to organize terms beneath it in the ontology, and we expect that it will not be used for direct annotations. Please consider using a more specific term to annotate each phenotype.
synonym: "normal meiotic spindle elongation in first meiotic nuclear division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal meiotic spindle elongation in meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0002739 ! abnormal meiotic cell cycle process
is_a: FYPO:0007078 ! normal meiotic cell cycle process
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-10-11T13:55:16Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007100
name: abnormal cell cycle arrest in meiotic prophase I with clustered telomeres
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the first meiotic nuclear division is arrested in prophase I under conditions where arrest does not normally occur, and with telomeres clustered at the spindle pole body. Telomere clustering at the SPB indicates that the cell has reached or passed the pachytene stage." [PMID:21449049, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal cell cycle arrest in meiotic prophase I at or after pachytene" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal cell cycle arrest in meiotic prophase I with telomeres clustered at SPB" EXACT [PomBase:al]
synonym: "abnormal cell cycle arrest in meiotic prophase I with telomeres clustered at spindle pole bodies" EXACT [PomBase:al]
is_a: FYPO:0002817 ! abnormally arrested meiosis I
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-10-11T14:08:51Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007101
name: bent spindle during meiosis I
def: "A spindle phenotype in which the meiotic spindle is not straight, but instead forms an angle where microtubules from opposite poles interdigitate, during meiosis I." [PMID:22292001, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "bent bipolar spindle during meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "bent meiotic spindle during meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "bent spindle during first meiotic nuclear division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "V-shaped bipolar spindle during meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0000734 ! abnormal meiotic spindle
is_a: FYPO:0003607 ! abnormal spindle morphology
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-10-16T14:41:07Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007102
name: multiple spindles during meiosis II
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which a cell contains more than one meiotic spindle per nucleus during the second meiotic nuclear division." [PMID:22292001, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "additional spindles present during meiosis II" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "extra spindles during meiosis II" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased number of spindles during meiosis II" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "multiple meiotic spindles during meiosis II" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "spindles present in greater numbers during meiosis II" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0006390 ! multiple meiotic spindles
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-10-16T14:43:31Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007103
name: spindle collapse during meiosis I
def: "A cell phenotype in which a short meiotic spindle assembles during meiosis I, and may begin elongation, but does not elongate normally or completely, and eventually collapses. Upon collapse the spindle may break or shrink." [PMID:22292001, PomBase:mah]
comment: Sister chromatids may separate in meiosis I due to problems with either cohesion or kinetochore attachment to microtubules. Therefore consider also annotating to 'abnormal attachment of spindle microtubules to kinetochore involved in homologous chromosome segregation' (FYPO:0000209), 'decreased meiotic sister chromatid cohesion' (FYPO:0002093), or 'merotelic kinetochore attachment during meiosis I' (FYPO:0005638).
synonym: "broken spindle during meiosis I" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "meiotic spindle collapse during meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "spindle breakage during meiosis I" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "spindle collapse during first meiotic nuclear division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0007083 ! meiotic spindle collapse
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-10-16T14:50:27Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007104
name: abnormal homologous chromosome arm segregation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which homologous chromosome segregation is abnormal along the chromosome arms." [PMID:22292001, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal homologous chromosome arm segregation during first meiotic nuclear division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal homologous chromosome arm segregation during meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal homologous chromosome arm separation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0004159 ! abnormal homologous chromosome segregation
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-10-16T15:06:11Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007105
name: increased duration of Rad52 focus presence during meiotic cell cycle
def: "A cell phenotype in which sites at which the protein Rad52 accumulates remain present for a longer time than normal during the meiotic cell cycle. Normally, Rad52 foci form during prophase I but disappear before metaphase I." [PMID:22292001, PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0004638 ! abnormal cellular physical quality phenotype
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2019-10-16T15:13:59Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007106
name: normal mitotic spindle morphology
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the size, shape, or structure of all or part of the mitotic spindle is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that an abnormal nuclear envelope organization process may, but does not necessarily, result in abnormal nuclear envelope morphology.
synonym: "normal mitotic spindle morphology during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal spindle morphology during mitosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal spindle morphology during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001313 ! normal subcellular component during vegetative growth
