creation_date: 2019-10-16T15:17:00Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007107
name: normal microtubule cytoskeleton organization during meiosis I
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which microtubule cytoskeleton organization is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during meiosis I. Microtubule cytoskeleton organization is the assembly, arrangement of constituent parts, or disassembly of cytoskeletal structures comprising microtubules and their associated proteins." [GO:0000226, PomBase:mah]
