def: "A phenotype that affects the organization of the microtubule cytoskeleton during all or part of the meiotic cell cycle. Microtubule cytoskeleton organization is a cellular process that results in the assembly, arrangement of constituent parts, or disassembly of cytoskeletal structures comprising microtubules and their associated proteins." [GO:0000226, PomBase:mah]
