[Term]
id: FYPO:0007119
name: loss of viability upon amino acid starvation
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable when cells the population are subject to starvation for one or more amino acids." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term to annotate experiments in which a culture is grown under glucose-depleted conditions, and then the number of cells viable enough to form a colony upon return to conditions supporting vegetative growth is measured and compared to wild type.
synonym: "decreased viability upon amino acid starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of cell population viability upon amino acid starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "loss of viability upon amino acid depletion" EXACT [PomBase:al]
