[Term]
id: FYPO:0007120
name: abolished cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase in response to leucine starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the occurrence of cell cycle arrest in response to leucine starvation does not occur; arrest normally occurs in G1 phase." [PMID:31456006, PomBase:mah]
comment: This term can be used for any circumstances in which cells are starved for nitrogen. Note that cells may enter G0 (quiescence) when subjected to prolonged nitrogen starvation; this term is not restricted to G0.
synonym: "abolished cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase during cellular response to leucine starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
