[Term]
id: FYPO:0007171
name: normal cell cortex morphology during meiotic prophase I
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which the size, shape, and structure of the cell cortex are normal during prophase of the first meiotic nuclear division. The cell cortex is the region of a cell that lies just beneath the plasma membrane." [GO:0005938, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that an abnormal cell cortex organization process may, but does not necessarily, result in abnormal cell cortex morphology. This term can be used for any circumstances in which cells are starved for nitrogen. Note that cells may enter G0 (quiescence) when subjected to prolonged nitrogen starvation; this term is not restricted to G0.
synonym: "normal cell cortex morphology during prophase I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell cortex morphology during prophase of meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
