[Term]
id: FYPO:0007241
name: abolished NETO in cell derived from growing end and premature NETO in cell derived from non-growing end
def: "A cell polarity phenotype in which the switch from the monopolar to bipolar mode of cell growth (new end take-off; NETO) is abnormal in both of the daughter cells formed as a result of the division of a mother cell in which NETO did not occur, such that NETO is abolished in the daughter cell that inherits the parent cell's old end, and begins earlier than normal in the daughter cell that inherits parent cell's new end. Normally, growth begins at the old end and then becomes bipolar with similar timing in both daughter cells." [PMID:31719163, PomBase:mah]
