[Term]
id: FYPO:0007249
name: normal level of X-shaped replication intermediates
def: "A cell phenotype in which the level of X-shaped DNA replication intermediates is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). X-shaped intermediates may be formed by replication forks moving bidirectionally from outside the region, or by the increased formation or persistence of Holliday junctions or similar recombination intermediates." [PMID:23071723, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal level of X-shaped DNA replication intermediates" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal level of X-shaped replication intermediates during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
