[Term]
id: FYPO:0007319
name: decreased stress granule assembly during glucose starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which stress granule assembly occurs to a lower extent than normal when the cell is subject to glucose starvation." [PMID:32071154, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that FYPO uses "glucose starvation" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies "during vegetative growth" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.
synonym: "decreased stress granule assembly during cellular response to glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased stress granule assembly during glucose depletion" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased stress granule assembly during glucose deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased stress granule assembly during glucose limitation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced stress granule assembly during glucose starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
