[Term]
id: FYPO:0007328
name: normal number of Rad52 foci during vegetative growth
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the number of sites at which the protein Rad52 (also called Rad22) accumulates is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PMID:31833215, PomBase:mah]
