[Term]
id: FYPO:0007329
name: increased DNA damage at tRNA genes
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of DNA damage measured at transfer RNA genes in a cell is greater than normal. The number, extent, or both of damage sites may be increased." [PMID:31833215, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA damage at transfer RNA genes" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA damage at tRNA genes during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA damage at tRNA genes during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
