creation_date: 2020-04-17T16:01:49Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007330
name: sensitive to formaldehyde
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to formaldehyde. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of formaldehyde that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "hypersensitive to formaldehyde" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to formaldehyde during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to formaldehyde during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000127 ! increased sensitivity to chemical during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-04-17T16:27:55Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007331
name: normal growth on formaldehyde
def: "A phenotype in which vegetative cell population growth is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) in a medium containing formaldehyde." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell population growth in presence of formaldehyde" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell population growth on formaldehyde" EXACT [PomBase:al, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "normal vegetative cell population growth on formaldehyde" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001357 ! normal vegetative cell population growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-04-17T16:29:25Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007332
name: abolished increase in protein phosphorylation during cellular response to stress in presence of small molecule
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which an increase in the phosphorylation of one or more specific proteins that would normally occur when cells are subjected to a stress in the presence of a specific small molecule does not occur under the same circumstances." [PMID:31932483, PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term when a difference between wild type and a mutant is seen only when both the stress and the small molecule are present. An example is protein phosphorylation under oxidative stress in the presence of the small molecule INR119. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "abolished increase in protein phosphorylation by small molecule" RELATED [PMID:31932483]
synonym: "abolished increase in protein phosphorylation during cellular response to stress in presence of small molecule during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished increase in protein phosphorylation during cellular response to stress in presence of small molecule during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002033 ! abolished protein phosphorylation during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-04-17T16:44:48Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007333
name: abolished chromatin silencing
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromatin silencing does not occur. Chromatin silencing is the observed effect of processes that repress transcription in a region of the genome that is normally assembled into heterochromatin or CENP-A-containing chromatin (the latter is found at the centromere central core)." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Chromatin silencing phenotypes may reflect the assembly or maintenance of heterochromatin. See the GO cellular component term 'heterochromatin' (GO:0000792), and the biological process term 'heterochromatin organization' (GO:0070828).
synonym: "abolished chromatin silencing during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "chromatin silencing abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "chromatin silencing abolished during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000575 ! abolished gene silencing
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-04-21T13:38:04Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007334
name: abolished chromatin silencing at centromere outer repeat
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromatin silencing does not occur at centromere outer repeat regions." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Chromatin silencing phenotypes may reflect the assembly or maintenance of heterochromatin. See the GO cellular component term 'heterochromatin' (GO:0000792), and the biological process term 'heterochromatin organization' (GO:0070828).
synonym: "abolished chromatin silencing at centromere otr" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished chromatin silencing at centromere outer repeat during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
