[Term]
id: FYPO:0007346
name: normal growth during cellular response to DNA damage
def: "A cell population growth phenotype in which vegetative cells grow normally (i.e. indistinguishably from wild type) during a cellular response to DNA damage." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Use this term if you have assayed growth of cells exposed to DNA damage in culture. If you have assayed the response to DNA damage at the subcellular or molecular level, consider annotating to a more specific term (e.g. normal protein phosphorylation during cellular response to DNA damage FYPO:0002899). Also consider specific phenotype terms for growth upon exposure to substances or other stimuli that can damage DNA, e.g. 'normal growth on methyl methanesulfonate' (FYPO:0000957), 'normal growth during cellular response to UV' (FYPO:0000969), etc.
synonym: "normal cell population growth during cellular response to DNA damage" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cellular response to DNA damage" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal sensitivity to DNA damage" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
