def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of fructose 1,6-bisphosphate measured in a cell is higher than normal." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased cellular D-fructose 1,6-bisphosphate level" EXACT [CHEBI:78682]
synonym: "increased cellular fructose 1,6-bisphosphate level during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased cellular fructose 1,6-bisphosphate level during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased fructose 1,6-bisphosphate accumulation" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001330 ! increased level of substance in cell during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-06T15:29:39Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007368
name: increased energy charge
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell's energy charge higher than normal. Energy charge is a measure of energy available to the cell, as reflected in the ATP-ADP-AMP balance and defined as (ATP + 1/2 ADP)/(AMP + ADP + ATP)." [PMID:32319721, PMID:6027798, PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003755 ! abnormal vegetative cell phenotype
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-06T15:36:42Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007369
name: altered cellular redox status
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell's redox status differs from normal, as measured by the ratios of reduced to oxidized forms of one or more metabolites (e.g. NAD+:NADH)." [PMID:32319721, PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003755 ! abnormal vegetative cell phenotype
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-06T15:38:29Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007370
name: increased cell population growth rate on fructose carbon source
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a cell population in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle grows at a faster rate than normal in a medium containing fructose as the carbon source." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that cell growth terms refer to growth under aerobic conditions unless stated otherwise.
synonym: "enhanced growth on fructose" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "fast cell population growth on fructose carbon source" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased cell population proliferation on fructose carbon source" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased cell proliferation on fructose carbon source" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased vegetative cell population growth rate on fructose carbon source" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000636 ! increased cell population growth rate
is_a: FYPO:0004557 ! increased vegetative cell population growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-06T15:40:14Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007371
name: increased cell population growth rate on sucrose carbon source
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a cell population in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle grows at a faster rate than normal in a medium containing sucrose as the carbon source." [PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that cell growth terms refer to growth under aerobic conditions unless stated otherwise.
synonym: "enhanced growth on sucrose" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "fast cell population growth on sucrose carbon source" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased cell population proliferation on sucrose carbon source" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased cell proliferation on sucrose carbon source" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased vegetative cell population growth rate on sucrose carbon source" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000636 ! increased cell population growth rate
is_a: FYPO:0009076 ! increased cell population growth on sucrose carbon source
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-06T15:41:15Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007372
name: resistance to chlorpromazine
def: "An increased chemical resistance phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells grow in the presence of a higher concentration of chlorpromazine than normal." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistance to chlorpromazine during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistance to chlorpromazine during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistant to chlorpromazine" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000126 ! increased resistance to chemical during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-06T15:42:29Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007373
name: abnormal histone methylation at silent mating-type cassette during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the methylation of histones in silent mating-type cassettes is abnormal. All histone methylation may be affected, or methylation of specific sites on specific histones may be altered." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal histone methylation at mating-type region heterochromatin during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal histone methylation at silent mating-type cassette during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000457 ! abnormal histone methylation during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-12T13:29:47Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007374
name: abnormal histone methylation at centromere during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the methylation of histones in centromeric regions is abnormal. All histone methylation may be affected, or methylation of specific sites on specific histones may be altered." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal centromeric histone methylation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal histone methylation at centromere during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000457 ! abnormal histone methylation during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-12T13:42:20Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007375
name: abnormal histone methylation at telomere during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the methylation of histones in telomeric regions is abnormal. All histone methylation may be affected, or methylation of specific sites on specific histones may be altered." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal histone methylation at telomere during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal telomeric histone methylation during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000457 ! abnormal histone methylation during vegetative growth
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-12T13:43:33Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007376
name: abolished epigenetic heterochromatin inheritance
def: "A phenotype in which a region of the genome that is normally stably assembled and maintained as heterochromatin over successive generations entirely loses heterochromatic structure." [PMID:29899117, PMID:31278118, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished epigenetic heterochromatin propagation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished epigenetic inheritance of heterochromatin" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished PEV" RELATED [PMID:31278118]
is_a: FYPO:0007477 ! abnormal epigenetic heterochromatin inheritance
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2020-05-12T13:57:00Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007377
name: protein mislocalized to medial cortex during mitotic interphase
def: "A  cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a protein that is not normally found at the medial cortex is observed there during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle." [PMID:9679144, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "ectopic protein localization to medial cortex during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein mislocalised to medial cortex during mitotic interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein mislocalized to medial cortex during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003390 ! protein mislocalized to medial cortex during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-05-19T12:21:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007378
name: normal spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which rapid, back-and-forth movement of the mitotic spindle pole body (SPB), and associated chromosome movement, is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). SPB oscillation occurs during mitotic interphase (as well as prophase) and is restricted to a small space." [GO:0140405, PMID:18495844, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal mitotic spindle pole body movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal mitotic spindle pole body oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001319 ! normal cellular process during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-05-27T10:33:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007379
name: T-shaped vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a new growth zone forms along the lateral portion of the cell (often in the middle) before septation, such that a single cell grows in the form of the letter T." [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: One distinction between T-shaped and other branched cells is that in T-shaped cells the new growth zone forms before NETO. A T-shaped cell may septate perpendicular to the normal septation axis, and divide to form normal-shaped daughter cells. Note that if you have done an experiment that assays the viability of a population of cells, such as looking at colony growth or growth in liquid culture, you should also annotate to 'viable cell population' (FYPO:0002058) or one of its descendants.
synonym: "T-shaped cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "T-shaped vegetative cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000015 ! branched vegetative cell
is_a: FYPO:0002197 ! viable vegetative cell with abnormal cell shape
is_a: FYPO:0005566 ! T-shaped cell
relationship: output_of FYPO:0000026 ! abnormal vegetative cell polarity
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-05-27T11:17:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007380
name: elongated T-shaped vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is longer than normal, and a new growth zone forms along the lateral portion of the cell (often in the middle) before septation, such that a single cell grows in the form of the letter T." [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: One distinction between T-shaped and other branched cells is that in T-shaped cells the new growth zone forms before NETO. A T-shaped cell may septate perpendicular to the normal septation axis, and divide to form normal-shaped daughter cells.
synonym: "elongated T-shaped cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "elongated T-shaped vegetative cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "long T-shaped vegetative cell" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001122 ! elongated vegetative cell
is_a: FYPO:0007379 ! T-shaped vegetative cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-05-27T11:24:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007381
name: Ssb1 megafocus present
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the protein Ssb1 accumulates in a large focus, or occasionally two foci, in the nucleus." [PMID:26246602, PMID:32341083, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "RPA megafocus present" EXACT [PMID:32341083, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "single enlarged Ssb1 focus present" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "Ssb1 megafocus present during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "Ssb1 megafocus present during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0004639 ! abnormal cellular physical quality phenotype during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-05-27T12:58:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007382
name: normal transcription regulatory region sequence-specific DNA binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which occurrence of DNA binding at a transcription regulatory region by a gene product is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). The relevant gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal promoter binding" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal sequence-specific DNA binding at transcription regulatory region" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal transcription regulatory region binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000655 ! normal DNA binding
