[Term]
id: FYPO:0007384
name: normal protein distribution along RNA polymerase II-transcribed genes during cellular response to oxidative stress
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the distribution of a protein localized to chromatin along the length of genes that can be transcribed by RNA polymerase II is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during a cellular response to oxidative stress." [PMID:28652406, PomBase:mah]
comment: Usually assayed for RNA polymerase, transcription factors, or other components of the transcription machinery. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "normal protein distribution across RNA polymerase II-transcribed genes during cellular response to oxidative stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein distribution along RNA polymerase II-regulated genes during cellular response to oxidative stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein distribution along RNA polymerase II-transcribed genes during cellular response to oxidative stress during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein distribution along RNA polymerase II-transcribed genes during cellular response to oxidative stress during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein distribution in chromatin along RNA polymerase II-transcribed genes during cellular response to oxidative stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein localization to chromatin along RNA polymerase II-transcribed genes during cellular response to oxidative stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0006021 ! normal protein distribution along RNA polymerase II-transcribed genes
