[Term]
id: FYPO:0007386
name: decreased histone H2B-K119 ubiquitination during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which ubiquitination of lysine at position 119 of histone H2B occurs to a lower extent than normal. Lysine 119 corresponds to the conserved C-terminal lysine of H2B." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased histone H2B conserved C-terminal lysine ubiquitination during vegetative growth" EXACT [GO:0071894]
synonym: "decreased histone H2B-K119 ubiquitination during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced histone H2B-K119 ubiquitination during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
