[Term]
id: FYPO:0007387
name: abolished NETO, with growth from new end
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the switch from the monopolar to bipolar mode of cell growth (new end take-off; NETO) does not occur, and the cell grows only from the new end." [PMID:12007420, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished cell growth mode switching, monopolar to bipolar, with growth from new end" EXACT [GO:0051523]
synonym: "abolished NETO during vegetative growth, with growth from new end" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished NETO, with cell growth from new end" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished NETO, with growth from new end during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished NETO, with growth from new end during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished NETO, with monopolar growth from new end" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished new end take-off, with growth from new end" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished switch from monopolar to bipolar cell growth, with cell growth from new end" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished switch from monopolar to bipolar cell growth, with growth from new end" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "NETO abolished, with growth from new end" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001018 ! abolished NETO
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-06-11T14:49:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007388
name: misoriented mitotic spindle
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the mitotic spindle is assembled in an incorrect orientation. Normally, the spindle is parallel to the long axis of the cell." [PMID:18495844, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal angle of mitotic spindle orientation" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic spindle orientation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "misoriented mitotic spindle during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "misoriented mitotic spindle during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000338 ! abnormal mitotic spindle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-06-15T10:14:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007389
name: abnormal angle of spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which spindle pole body (SPB)-led chromosome movement in mitotic interphase takes place at an abnormal angle relative to the long axis of the cell. Normally, the SPB oscillation angle remains nearly parallel to the long axis." [PMID:18495844, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal angle of mitotic SPB oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal angle of mitotic spindle pole body movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal angle of mitotic spindle pole body oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal angle of SPB-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal angle of spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal angle of spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased angle of spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase" NARROW [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased trajectory angle of SPB oscillation" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase at abnormal angle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0005348 ! abnormal spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-06-15T10:41:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007390
name: increased variability of angle of spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which spindle pole body (SPB)-led chromosome movement in mitotic interphase takes place at an angle that varies more than normal. Normally, the SPB oscillation angle remains nearly parallel to the long axis of the cell." [PMID:18495844, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased variability of angle of mitotic SPB oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased variability of angle of mitotic spindle pole body movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased variability of angle of mitotic spindle pole body oscillation during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased variability of angle of SPB-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased variability of angle of spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during interphase of mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased variability of angle of spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "variable trajectory angle of SPB oscillation" RELATED [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0005348 ! abnormal spindle pole body-led chromosome movement during mitotic interphase
