[Term]
id: FYPO:0007391
name: inviable aneuploid spore
def: "A viability phenotype in which an aneuploid spore is unable to survive under conditions in which wild type spores survive. An inviable spore does not germinate." [PMID:22737087, PomBase:mah]
comment: Thes phenotype can be observed after a polyploid meiosis, where aneuploid spores no longer form small colonies. This results in an increase of large to small colonies and decreased spore viability.
synonym: "abolished aneuploid spore germination" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "aneuploid spore germination abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased aneuploid spore viability" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased viability of aneuploid cells" RELATED [PomBase:jh, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "decreased viability of aneuploid spores" RELATED [PomBase:jh, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "lethal in aneuploid spore" RELATED [PomBase:jh, PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0002151 ! inviable spore
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-06-15T13:11:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007392
name: increased loss of disomic chromosome 3
def: "A cell phenotype in which that are aneuploid due to the presence of an extra copy of chromosome 3 lose the extra chromosome, producing haploid daughter cells, at a higher frequency than in otherwise wild-type cells." [PMID:22737087, PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
comment: This phenotype results from increased chromosome instability in aneuploid cells, restores the cells to euhaploid, and causes haploid colonies to arise at a higher frequency.
synonym: "increased haploidisation in presence of chromosome 3 disomy" RELATED [PomBase:jh, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased loss of disomic chromosome 3 during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:jh, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased loss of disomic chromosome 3 during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003755 ! abnormal vegetative cell phenotype
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-06-15T13:21:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007393
name: septum mislocalized to cell tip
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell has a septum with both ends at the cell tip(s). The normal location is at the midpoint of the long axis of the cell." [PMID:32101481, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
comment: Includes cells where both ends of the septum are found at the same end of the cell, and cells where one end of the septum is found at each end.
synonym: "septum mislocalized to cell tip during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "septum mislocalized to cell tip during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "tip septation" EXACT [PMID:32101481]
is_a: FYPO:0003210 ! mislocalized, misoriented septum
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-06-15T13:46:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007394
name: abnormal RNA structure
def: "A phenotype in which the structure of one or more RNA molecules differs from normal." [PMID:24793650, PomBase:mah]
