[Term]
id: FYPO:0007426
name: abolished new mitotic spindle pole body insertion into nuclear envelope
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the insertion of the newly assembled spindle pole body into the nuclear envelope does not occur." [PMID:19487457, PMID:22042620, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal establishment of old mitotic spindle pole body localization to nuclear envelope" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished new mitotic SPB insertion into nuclear envelope" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
