[Term]
id: FYPO:0007462
name: increased filamentous actin level
def: "A cell phenotype in which the amount of filamentous actin measured the cell is higher than normal when the cell is in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle. The total actin level (globular and filamentous actin) may be normal or abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
