[Term]
id: FYPO:0007464
name: increased RNA level during cellular response to hypoxia
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of RNA measured in a cell during a cellular response to hypoxia is higher than normal. Total RNA or a specific RNA may be affected." [PomBase:mah]
