[Term]
id: FYPO:0007471
name: abnormal heterochromatin organization during G0
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which any process of heterochromatin organization is abnormal during G0 phase. Heterochromatin organization results in the specification, formation or maintenance of the physical structure of eukaryotic heterochromatin, a compact and highly condensed form of chromatin." [GO:0070828, PomBase:mah]
