[Term]
id: FYPO:0007474
name: variable cell size at division
def: "A cell population phenotype in which cells in a population do not divide at a uniform size, although each cell divides to form equal-size daughter cells. Within one population, some cells may be larger and others smaller than normal (i.e. compared to wild-type cells under the same conditions)." [PMID:23333317, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased variability of cell size in a vegetative population" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
