[Term]
id: FYPO:0007478
name: decreased epigenetic heterochromatin inheritance
def: "A phenotype in which a region of the genome that is normally stably assembled and maintained as heterochromatin over successive generations retains heterochromatic structure for fewer generations than normal." [PMID:29899117, PMID:31278118, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased epigenetic heterochromatin propagation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased PEV" RELATED [PMID:31278118]
synonym: "epigenetic inheritance of heterochromatin" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced epigenetic heterochromatin inheritance" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
