[Term]
id: FYPO:0007479
name: normal epigenetic heterochromatin inheritance
def: "A phenotype in which the assembly and stable inheritance of heterochromatic structure is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) in regions of the genome where heterochromatin is normally maintained over successive generations." [PMID:29899117, PMID:31278118, PomBase:mah]
