[Term]
id: FYPO:0007509
name: increased histone H3-K9 trimethylation at silent mating-type cassette during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the trimethylation of lysine at position 9 of histone H3 in silent mating-type cassettes occurs to a greater extent than normal." [PMID:17434129, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased histone H3 K9 trimethylation at silent mating-type cassette during vegetative growth" EXACT [GO:0036124\,PomBase\:mah]
synonym: "increased histone H3-K9 trimethylation at mating-type region heterochromatin during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased histone H3-K9 trimethylation at silent mating-type cassette during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased histone H3K9 trimethylation at silent mating-type cassette during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased histone H3K9me3 at silent mating-type cassette during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased histone lysine H3 K9 trimethylation at silent mating-type cassette during vegetative growth" EXACT [GO:0036124\,PomBase\:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000879 ! increased histone H3-K9 trimethylation during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-05T14:50:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007510
name: cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition in absence of mitotic DNA replication checkpoint
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which progression through the mitotic cell cycle is abnormally arrested at the mitotic G2/M phase transition in the absence of the mitotic DNA replication checkpoint. The previous S phase is completed, no replication intermediates can be observed, and cells do not undergo rereplication." [PMID:17690116, PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cell cycle arrest at G2/M phase transition in absence of mitotic DNA replication checkpoint during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition in absence of mitotic DNA replication checkpoint during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic cell cycle arrest at the G2/M transition with completed S phase" RELATED [PomBase:jh]
is_a: FYPO:0000400 ! abnormal cell cycle arrest at mitotic G2/M phase transition
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-10T13:29:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007511
name: normal mitosis following cell cycle arrest in response to mitotic DNA replication checkpoint
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which a cell undergoes normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) mitosis upon release from a following release from a G2/M cell cycle block imposed by activation of the mitotic DNA replication checkpoint." [PMID:17690116, PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal mitosis following cell cycle arrest in response to DNA replication checkpoint during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal mitosis following cell cycle arrest in response to mitotic DNA replication checkpoint during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal mitosis following release from a mitotic DNA replication cell cycle block" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
is_a: FYPO:0001007 ! normal mitosis
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-10T13:35:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007512
name: abnormal chromosome III morphology
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the size, shape, or structure chromosome III is abnormal." [PMID:17690116, PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal chromosome III mobility" RELATED [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "abnormal chromosome III morphology during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal chromosome III morphology during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000848 ! abnormal chromosome morphology during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-10T13:38:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007513
name: increased rDNA copy number during vegetative growth
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the number of ribosomal DNA (rDNA) repeats present in the rDNA arrays on chromosome III is significantly greater than the range in wild type cells." [PMID:17690116, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased copy number of rDNA repeats" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "increased copy number of rDNA repeats during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "increased rDNA copy number during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0004823 ! abnormal rDNA copy number
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-10T14:03:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007514
name: sensitive to manumycin A
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to manumycin A. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of manumycin A that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "hypersensitive to manumycin A" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to manu-A" EXACT [PMID:25500221]
synonym: "sensitive to manumycin A during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to manumycin A during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000127 ! increased sensitivity to chemical during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-10T14:12:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007515
name: decreased RNA stability during cellular response to oxidative stress
def: "A cell phenotype in which RNA stability is decreased during a cellular response to oxidative stress. RNA molecules are more likely to degrade over a given time period than in wild type. Total RNA or a specific RNA, such as the mRNA transcribed from a gene of interest, may be affected." [PMID:14633985, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased RNA stability during cellular response to oxidative stress during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased RNA stability during cellular response to oxidative stress during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased RNA stability in response to oxidative stress" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "reduced RNA stability during cellular response to oxidative stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003038 ! abnormal RNA stability
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T14:18:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007516
name: decreased DNA volume
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which DNA occupies a smaller portion of the total nuclear volume than normal. The nuclear volume itself may be normal." [PMID:33153481, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DNA volume during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased DNA volume during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced DNA volume" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001322 ! abnormal subcellular component during vegetative growth
is_a: FYPO:0002403 ! abnormal nucleus
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T14:27:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007517
name: increased chromatin mobility
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromatin moves within the nucleus to a greater extent than normal." [PMID:33153481, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased chromatin mobility during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased chromatin mobility during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased chromatin motility" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased chromatin movement" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001352 ! abnormal chromatin organization during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T14:33:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007518
name: increased transcription-induced DNA damage
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of DNA damage occurring as a side effect of transcription in a cell is greater than normal. The number, extent, or both of damage sites may be increased." [PMID:33153481, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased DNA damage by transcription" EXACT [PMID:33153481]
synonym: "increased transcription-induced DNA damage during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased transcription-induced DNA damage during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003547 ! increased DNA damage during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T14:37:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007519
name: normal DNA volume
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which DNA occupies a normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) portion of the total nuclear volume. The nuclear volume itself is also normal." [PMID:33153481, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal DNA volume during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal DNA volume during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001313 ! normal subcellular component during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T14:47:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007520
name: normal growth on beta-glucanase
def: "A phenotype in which vegetative cell population growth is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) in a medium containing  one or more enzymes that degrades cell wall polysaccharides by hydrolyzing beta-glucan linkages." [PMID:19625445, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell population growth in presence of beta-glucanase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell population growth on beta-glucanase" EXACT [PomBase:al, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "normal cellular response to beta-glucanase" RELATED [PomBase:al, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal vegetative cell population growth on beta-glucanase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001192 ! normal growth on cell wall-degrading enzymes
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T14:51:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007521
name: resistance to tacrolimus and magnesium chloride
def: "An increased chemical resistance phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells grow in the presence of higher concentrations of tacrolimus and magnesium chloride than normal." [PMID:19625445, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "hypersensitive to tacrolimus and magnesium chloride" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistance to FK506 and magnesium chloride" EXACT [CHEBI:61057, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistance to magnesium chloride and FK506" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistance to magnesium chloride and tacrolimus" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistance to tacrolimus and magnesium chloride during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistance to tacrolimus and magnesium chloride during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistance to tacrolimus and MgCl2" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "resistant to tacrolimus and magnesium chloride" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "viable in the presence of FK506 and chloride" EXACT [PMID:19625445]
synonym: "vic" RELATED [PMID:19625445]
is_a: FYPO:0000126 ! increased resistance to chemical during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T15:16:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007522
name: sensitive to tacrolimus and magnesium chloride
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to a combination of tacrolimus and magnesium chloride. Cells stop growing (and may die) at concentrations of tacrolimus and magnesium chloride that allow wild type cells to grow." [PMID:19625445, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "inviable in the presence of FK506 and chloride" EXACT [PMID:19625445]
synonym: "sensitive to FK506 and magnesium chloride" EXACT [CHEBI:61057, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to magnesium chloride and FK506" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to magnesium chloride and tacrolimus" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to tacrolimus and magnesium chloride during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to tacrolimus and magnesium chloride during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to tacrolimus and MgCl2" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "vic-negative" RELATED [PMID:19625445]
is_a: FYPO:0000127 ! increased sensitivity to chemical during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T15:22:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007523
name: decreased protein level during cellular response to oxidative stress
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of protein measured in a cell during a cellular response to oxidative stress is lower than normal. Total protein or a specific protein may be affected." [PMID:19625445, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "decreased protein accumulation during cellular response to oxidative stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein level during cellular response to oxidative stress during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein level during cellular response to oxidative stress during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced protein level during cellular response to oxidative stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001324 ! decreased protein level during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T15:25:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007524
name: delayed onset of protein import into nucleus
def: "A transport phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the import of protein into the nucleus begins later than normal. Import of all proteins or a specific protein may be affected." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "delayed onset of protein import into nucleus during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed onset of protein import into nucleus during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "delayed protein import into nucleus" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003188 ! abnormal protein import into nucleus during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T15:30:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007525
name: decreased ribosome binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which occurrence of ribosome binding by a gene product (usually a protein) in a mutant is decreased. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PMID:19625445, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced ribosome binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001092 ! binding phenotype
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T15:45:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007526
name: increased protein phosphorylation during cellular response to salt stress
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the phosphorylation of one or more specific proteins, or of specific protein sites, occurs to a greater extent than normal during a cellular response to salt stress." [PMID:19625445, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased protein phosphorylation during cellular response to salt stress during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased protein phosphorylation during cellular response to salt stress during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001038 ! increased protein phosphorylation during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-17T15:49:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007527
name: increased protein localization to cell tip during nitrogen starvation
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to the cell tip is increased when the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation." [PMID:27746023, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased protein localization to cell tip during nitrogen depletion" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased protein localization to cell tip during nitrogen deprivation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0005987 ! abnormal protein localization to cell tip
