[Term]
id: FYPO:0007532
name: decreased replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore complex
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which arrested replication forks do not colocalize with nuclear pore complexes (NPCs) longer than actively replicating forks. Normally, arrested replication forks relocate to NPCs as part of replication fork processing, and remain anchored at NPCs while recombination-dependent replication takes place." [PMID:33159083, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased replication fork colocalization with NPC" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore complex during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore complex during mitotic S phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore complex during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased replication fork relocation to nuclear pore complex" EXACT [PMID:33159083]
synonym: "decreased replication fork relocation to nuclear pore complex during mitotic S phase" EXACT [PMID:33159083]
synonym: "reduced replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore complex" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003586 ! abnormal replication fork processing
