[Term]
id: FYPO:0007533
name: normal replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore complex
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which arrested replication forks colocalize normally (i.e. indistinguishably from wild type) with nuclear pore complexes (NPCs). Normally, arrested replication forks relocate to NPCs as part of replication fork processing, and remain anchored at NPCs while recombination-dependent replication takes place." [PMID:33159083, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal replication fork colocalization with NPC" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore complex during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore complex during mitotic S phase" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal replication fork colocalization with nuclear pore complex during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal replication fork relocation to nuclear pore complex" EXACT [PMID:33159083]
synonym: "normal replication fork relocation to nuclear pore complex during mitotic S phase" EXACT [PMID:33159083]
is_a: FYPO:0007254 ! normal replication fork processing
