[Term]
id: FYPO:0007541
name: viable branched, swollen, elongated, multinucleate, multiseptate vegetative cell
def: "A cell morphology phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell is viable, branched, has more than one nucleus and more than one septum, and has a larger volume and is longer, than normal. In a swollen cell, both length and diameter may be greater than normal, although the cell is only considered elongated if the length:diameter ratio is also greater than normal." [PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "viable branched, elongated, swollen, multinucleate, multiseptate vegetative cell" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "viable branched, swollen, elongated, multinucleate, multiseptate cell during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "viable branched, swollen, elongated, multinucleate, multiseptate vegetative cell during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001252 ! multinucleate multiseptate vegetative cell
is_a: FYPO:0003500 ! viable branched, elongated, multiseptate vegetative cell
is_a: FYPO:0006167 ! viable branched, swollen, elongated, multinucleate vegetative cell
is_a: FYPO:0007436 ! swollen elongated multiseptate vegetative cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-11-30T12:10:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007542
name: normal double-stranded DNA binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which occurrence of double-stranded DNA binding by a gene product is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). The relevant gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal dsDNA binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000655 ! normal DNA binding
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-12-09T12:19:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007543
name: abolished double-stranded DNA binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which double-stranded DNA binding by a gene product does not occur, when a gene or the bound DNA sequence is mutated. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished dsDNA binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "double-stranded DNA binding abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000659 ! abolished DNA binding
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-12-09T13:46:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007544
name: normal cohesin complex binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of one protein to a cohesin complex is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). The protein whose binding to the cohesin complex is assayed may be encoded by the mutated gene, or may be encoded by a different gene." [PMID:33176147, PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0005232 ! normal protein complex binding
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-12-09T13:49:46Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007545
name: increased duration of protein localization to mitotic nuclear bridge
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which one or more proteins is localized to the mitotic nuclear bridge for a longer time than normal." [PMID:32502403, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased duration of protein localisation to mitotic nuclear bridge" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased duration of protein localization to mitotic nuclear bridge during mitotic anaphase B" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased duration of protein localization to mitotic nuclear bridge during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased duration of protein localization to mitotic nuclear bridge during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "prolonged protein localization to mitotic nuclear bridge" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001129 ! abnormal protein localization to nucleus during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-12-09T15:01:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007546
name: abolished nuclear envelope division
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which nuclear envelope division does not occur. Nuclear envelope division takes place at the end of mitosis; the nuclear envelope undergoes localized breakdown in the nuclear bridge midzone and the ends are sealed and retrieved into the envelopes of the separated daughter nuclei. When nuclear envelope division does not occur, the two DNA masses remain linked by the nuclear bridge, and may coalesce back into a single nucleus." [PMID:32502403, PMID:32848252, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abolished NE division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished nuclear envelope division during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished nuclear envelope division during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "failed nuclear envelope division" EXACT [PMID:32502403]
synonym: "nuclear envelope division abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000815 ! abnormal nuclear envelope organization
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-12-09T15:09:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007547
name: abnormal nuclear pore localization to mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane
def: "A localization phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which nuclear pore localization to the portion of the nuclear envelope enclosing the mitotic nuclear bridge is abnormal, resulting in an abnormal distribution of nuclear pores in the bridge envelope. The nuclear bridge is a narrow constricted region of the nucleus that forms around the mitotic spindle during anaphase. Normally, nuclear pores that lack baskets are found in the midzone of the nuclear bridge." [PMID:32502403, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal distribution of nuclear pores at nuclear bridge midzone membrane domain" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abnormal NPC localization to mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal nuclear pore complex localization to mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal nuclear pore distribution in mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal nuclear pore distribution in mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane domain" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal nuclear pore localization to mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal nuclear pore localization to mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003783 ! abnormal nuclear pore localization during mitosis
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2020-12-09T15:12:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007548
name: abnormal mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane domain organization
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which nuclear envelope organization is abnormal in the region of the nuclear envelope that surrounds the mitotic nuclear bridge during mitosis." [PMID:32502403, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic nuclear bridge midzone envelope organization" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane domain organization during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal mitotic nuclear bridge midzone membrane domain organization during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
