[Term]
id: FYPO:0007565
name: abolished DNA binding at MCB
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which DNA binding at an RNA polymerase II proximal promoter that contains a Mlu1 cell cycle box (MCB) by a gene product does not occur, when a gene or the bound DNA sequence is mutated. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PMID:8223442, PomBase:mah]
