[Term]
id: FYPO:0007598
name: abolished chromatin silencing at ectopic tethering site
def: "A transcription regulation phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromatin silencing does not occur at a site where silencing can normally be triggered by the ectopic tethering of a protein." [PMID:23613586, PomBase:mah]
comment: Note that this term incorporates some information about experimental tools, but is included to allow effects of tethering different (wild-type or mutated) proteins to the binding site to be represented. The tethering site is placed adjacent to a reporter gene that is expressed in the absence of a binding domain fusion (i.e. in a region not normally silenced).
synonym: "abolished chromatin silencing at ectopic tethering site during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished chromatin silencing at ectopic tethering site during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000144 ! abnormal chromatin silencing
