comment: Note that this term incorporates some information about experimental tools, but is included to allow effects of tethering different (wild-type or mutated) proteins to the binding site to be represented. The tethering site is placed adjacent to a reporter gene that is expressed in the absence of a binding domain fusion (i.e. in a region not normally silenced).
synonym: "increased chromatin silencing at ectopic tethering site" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased chromatin silencing at ectopic tethering site during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
