[Term]
id: FYPO:0007605
name: decreased outer prospore membrane breakdown
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which breakdown of the outer layer of the prospore membrane (forespore membrane; FSM) is decreased. Normally, the outer of the two FSM layers breaks down completely, producing a mature spore. When FSM breakdown does not occur normally, the outer FSM layers of two adjacent spores may be fused." [PMID:33202882, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased outer forespore membrane breakdown" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased outer membrane FSM breakdown" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
