[Term]
id: FYPO:0007617
name: sensitive to sodium azide
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to sodium azide (NaN3). Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of sodium azide that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to NaN3" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to sodium azide during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sensitive to sodium azide during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
