[Term]
id: FYPO:0007619
name: normal protein localization to chromatin during cellular response to oxidative stress
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of a protein to chromatin is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) when the cell is subject to oxidative stress." [PomBase:mah]
