[Term]
id: FYPO:0007621
name: increased protein-protein interaction during cellular response to oxidative stress
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of one protein to another occurs to a lower extent than normal when the cell is subject to oxidative stress. The relevant proteins may include the one encoded by the mutated gene, or may both be encoded by different genes." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased protein binding during cellular response to oxidative stress" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased protein-protein interaction during oxidative stress response" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
