[Term]
id: FYPO:0007659
name: variable cell size at division with subsequent division at normal size
def: "A cell population phenotype in which cells in a population do not divide at a uniform size, although each cell divides to form equal-size daughter cells, which then subsequently divide at a normal size. Within one population, some cells may be larger and others smaller than normal (i.e. compared to wild-type cells under the same conditions) upon the first division. Daughter cells that are larger than normal upon formation divide earlier, and smaller-formed daughter cells divide later, than cells formed at a normal size." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased variability of cell size in a vegetative population, with subsequent division at normal size" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "variable cell length at entry into mitosis followed by equal cell division" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "variable cell size at division with normal cell size homeostasis" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "variable cell size at division with subsequent division at normal size during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "variable cell size at division with subsequent division at normal size during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "variable vegetative cell size at division with subsequent division at normal size" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0007474 ! variable cell size at division
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-03-02T13:48:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007660
name: variable cell size at division with subsequent division at abnormal size
def: "A cell population phenotype in which cells in a population do not divide at a uniform size, although each cell divides to form equal-size daughter cells, which then subsequently divide at an abnormal size. Within one population, some cells may be larger and others smaller than normal (i.e. compared to wild-type cells under the same conditions) upon each division." [PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased variability of cell size in a vegetative population, with subsequent division at abnormal size" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
