[Term]
id: FYPO:0007680
name: increased ribonucleotide incorporation into DNA
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which more ribonucleotides than normal are incorporated into one or both strands during mitotic DNA replication." [PMID:33568651, PomBase:mah]
