[Term]
id: FYPO:0007687
name: normal protein localization to nuclear exosome focus during meiosis
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to nuclear exosome foci is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during meiosis. Nuclear exosome foci, also called Mmi1 foci, are small structures that form within the nucleus, and contain proteins involved in degrading meiosis-specific RNAs during the mitotic cell cycle." [PMID:33574613, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "normal protein localisation to nuclear exosome focus during meiosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein localization to Mmi1 focus during meiosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein localization to Mmi1 nuclear focus during meiosis" EXACT [GO:1990251]
synonym: "normal protein localization to nuclear exosome foci during meiosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein localization to nuclear exosome focus during meiotic nuclear division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003790 ! normal protein localization during meiosis
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-03-16T14:54:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007688
name: abolished protein localization to kinetochore during meiotic metaphase I
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to the kinetochore of a chromosome does not occur during metaphase of the first meiotic nuclear division." [PMID:16541024, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "abolished protein localisation to kinetochore during meiotic metaphase I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished protein localization to kinetochore during meiosis I metaphase" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "protein localization to kinetochore abolished during meiotic metaphase I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
