property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-03-16T16:17:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007689
name: normal cell growth polarization
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells can grow in a normally (i.e. as in wild type) polarized manner as in the presence of a polarity landmark. The landmark itself may be in a normal or abnormal location." [PMID:21148300, PomBase:mah]
comment: The difference between this term and 'normal cell polarity' (FYPO:0005456) is that this term can be used if a polarity landmark is in an abnormal place, but polar growth takes place at the landmark. FYPO:0005465 can be used only when all aspects of polar growth are normal.
synonym: "normal cell growth polarisation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell growth polarization during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal cell growth polarization during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal vegetative cell growth polarization" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001319 ! normal cellular process during vegetative growth
