[Term]
id: FYPO:0007751
name: spindle collapse during meiotic prometaphase I
def: "A cell phenotype in which a short spindle assembles during the first meiotic nuclear division, and may begin elongation, but does not elongate normally or completely, and collapses during prometaphase I. Upon collapse the spindle may break or shrink." [PMID:32723864, PomBase:mah]
