[Term]
id: FYPO:0007754
name: abolished mitotic spindle formation phase II
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which phase II of mitotic spindle assembly does not occur. During phase II, the spindle is normally maintained at a constant length during mitotic metaphase." [PMID:32723864, PomBase:mah]
