[Term]
id: FYPO:0007769
name: increased heterochromatin tethering at nuclear periphery during mitosis
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which heterochromatin tethering at the nuclear periphery persists after the onset of mitosis. Normally, heterochromatic parts of chromosomes, such as centromeres and telomeres, are maintained at the nuclear periphery during interphase and released during mitosis." [PMID:32109380, PomBase:mah]
