[Term]
id: FYPO:0007787
name: increased transcription during cell cycle arrest at meiotic G2/MI transition
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which transcription occurs to a greater extent than normal when the meiotic cell cycle is arrested at the G2/MI phase transition. All genes, or a specific subset of genes, may be affected." [PMID:28476936, PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased transcription during abnormal cell cycle arrest at G2/M1 transition" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased transcription during abnormal cell cycle arrest at G2/MI transition of meiotic cell cycle" EXACT [GO:0008315]
synonym: "increased transcription during abnormal cell cycle arrest at meiotic cell cycle G2/MI phase transition" EXACT [GO:0008315]
