[Term]
id: FYPO:0007795
name: two cell divisions prior to cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase without nutrient starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which progression through the mitotic cell cycle is arrested in G1 phase after the cells have undergone two rounds of cell division under nutrient-replete conditions. This arrest resembles that of wild-type cells under conditions of nitrogen starvation." [PMID:17121544, PMID:28476936, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "two cell divisions prior to mitotic cell cycle arrest in G1 phase without nutrient starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "two cell divisions prior to mitotic G1 arrest without nutrient starvation" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
