[Term]
id: FYPO:0007798
name: increased actin filament binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of a protein to one or more actin filaments occurs to a greater extent than normal. The affected protein may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased F-actin binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased filamentous actin binding" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
