[Term]
id: FYPO:0007858
name: mitotic DNA re-replication in absence of mitotic spindle
def: "A regulation phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell undergoes one or more rounds of rereplication of the entire genome without forming a mitotic spindle or undergoing cytokinesis." [PMID:20967237, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal negative regulation of mitotic DNA replication initiation resulting in complete rereplication in absence of mitotic spindle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal negative regulation of mitotic DNA replication initiation resulting in complete rereplication in absence of mitotic spindle during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal negative regulation of mitotic DNA replication initiation resulting in complete rereplication in absence of mitotic spindle during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "mitotic DNA re-replication in the absence of normal mitotic spindle assembly and cytokinesis" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
is_a: FYPO:0001425 ! abnormal negative regulation of mitotic DNA replication initiation resulting in complete rereplication
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-09-28T12:55:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007859
name: nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the nucleus divides into two or more fragments, each enclosed by nuclear envelope and containing a DNA mass, in a cell that does not form a mitotic spindle or undergo cytokinesis. In these cells, the nucleus does not elongate into a dumbbell shape, but instead the nuclear envelope takes on a ruffled aspect and then eventually pinches into two nuclear masses." [PMID:20967237, PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "nuclear fission" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "nuclear fission in absence of mitotic spindle" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "rel syn DNA segregation in absence of mitotic spindle" RELATED [PomBase:jh]
is_a: FYPO:0000337 ! abnormal mitosis
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-09-28T13:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007860
name: spindle pole body separation in absence of mitotic spindle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the spindle pole body (SPB) duplicates normally, and the SPBs separate, in a cell that does not form a mitotic spindle or undergo cytokinesis. The DNA and nucleus may go on to divide in the absence of a spindle, with each DNA mass associated with an SPB." [PMID:20967237, PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "SPB separation in absence of mitotic spindle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "spindle pole body separation in absence of mitotic spindle during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "spindle pole body separation in absence of mitotic spindle during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002734 ! abnormal cell cycle process
relationship: part_of FYPO:0007859 ! nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-09-28T13:02:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007861
name: sister chromatid separation during nuclear fission
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which sister chromatids become physically detached in a cell that does not form a mitotic spindle or undergo cytokinesis. The DNA and nucleus may go on to divide in the absence of a spindle, with sister chromatids segregated to separate DNA masses." [PMID:20967237, PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "chromosome separation during nuclear fission" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "sister chromatid separation during nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sister chromatid separation during nuclear fission during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "sister chromatid separation during nuclear fission during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0002734 ! abnormal cell cycle process
relationship: part_of FYPO:0007859 ! nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-09-28T13:06:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007862
name: centromere clustering at nuclear periphery during nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which centromeres and kinetochores remain associated with the spindle pole body during nuclear division in a that does not form a mitotic spindle or undergo cytokinesis." [PMID:20967237, PomBase:jh, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal centromere-SPB association at mitosis" RELATED [PomBase:jh]
synonym: "centromere clustering at nuclear periphery during nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "centromere clustering at nuclear periphery during nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "centromere clustering at nuclear periphery during nuclear fission" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "chromosome SPB attachment during nuclear fission" EXACT [PomBase:jh]
is_a: FYPO:0002734 ! abnormal cell cycle process
relationship: part_of FYPO:0007859 ! nuclear division in absence of mitotic spindle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-09-28T13:11:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007863
name: abnormal protein localization to spindle
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to the mitotic or meiotic spindle is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
subset: qc_do_not_manually_annotate
synonym: "abnormal protein localisation to spindle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001370 ! abnormal protein localization
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-09-28T14:06:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007864
name: abolished protein localization to meiotic spindle pole during meiosis I
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to one or both poles of the meiotic spindle does not occur during the first meiotic nuclear division." [PMID:34346498, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "abolished protein localisation to meiotic spindle pole during meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished protein localisation to spindle pole during meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished protein localization to meiosis I spindle pole" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished protein localization to spindle pole during first meiotic nuclear division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "protein localization to meiotic spindle pole during meiosis I abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0001375 ! abolished protein localization
is_a: FYPO:0006454 ! abnormal protein localization to meiotic spindle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-09-28T14:12:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007865
name: normal protein localization to spindle
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to the mitotic or meiotic spindle is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
subset: qc_do_not_manually_annotate
synonym: "normal protein localisation to spindle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
