[Term]
id: FYPO:0007866
name: normal protein localization to meiotic spindle
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to the meiotic spindle is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "normal protein localisation to meiotic spindle" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein localization to spindle during meiosis" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "normal protein localization to spindle pole during meiotic nuclear division" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
