[Term]
id: FYPO:0007867
name: normal protein localization to meiotic spindle pole during meiosis I
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to one or both poles of the meiotic spindle is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during the first meiotic nuclear division." [PMID:34346498, PomBase:mah]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "normal protein localisation to meiotic spindle pole during meiosis I" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
