[Term]
id: FYPO:0007878
name: decreased protein degradation during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the occurrence of protein degradation is decreased during a cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate. Protein degradation, also known as protein catabolism, is any metabolic process that results in the destruction of the native, active configuration of a protein, with or without the hydrolysis of peptide bonds." [GO:0030163, PMID:34608864, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein breakdown during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate" EXACT [GO:0030163, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein catabolic process during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate" EXACT [GO:0030163, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein catabolism during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate" EXACT [GO:0030163, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein degradation during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein degradation during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased protein degradation during cellular response to MMS" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced protein degradation during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0000845 ! abnormal protein degradation during vegetative growth
is_a: FYPO:0002797 ! decreased protein degradation
