[Term]
id: FYPO:0007883
name: decreased cleavage-dependent termination of RNA polymerase II transcription
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cleavage-dependent termination of transcription by RNA polymerase II is abnormal. In cleavage-dependent termination, co-transcriptional secondary structure-dependent endonucleolytic cleavage triggers RNA polymerase II transcription termination; transcripts are not polyadenylated, and are subsequently rapidly degraded in the nucleus. Termination of all transcripts, or a subset of transcripts, may be affected." [PMID:34352089, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cleavage-dependent premature transcription termination" NARROW [PMID:34352089]
synonym: "decreased cleavage-dependent RNA polymerase II transcription termination" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cleavage-dependent termination of RNA polymerase II transcription during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased cleavage-dependent termination of RNA polymerase II transcription during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "decreased Pac1-dependent termination of RNA polymerase II transcription" RELATED [PMID:34352089]
is_a: FYPO:0006613 ! decreased termination of RNA polymerase II transcription
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-11-03T15:06:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007884
name: abolished Lsm2-8 complex binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which Lms2-8 complex binding by a gene product (usually a protein) in a mutant does not occur. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PMID:33378677, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "Lsm2-8 complex binding abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003591 ! abnormal protein complex binding
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-11-15T13:15:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007885
name: decreased Lsm2-8 complex binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which occurrence of Lms2-8 complex binding by a gene product (usually a protein) in a mutant is decreased. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene." [PMID:33378677, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "reduced Lsm2-8 complex binding" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
is_a: FYPO:0003591 ! abnormal protein complex binding
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-11-15T13:15:41Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-11-15T13:16:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007886
name: abolished histone H3-K9 dimethylation during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which dimethylation of lysine at position 9 of histone H3 does not occur." [PMID:34524082, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished histone H3 K9 dimethylation during vegetative growth" EXACT [GO:0036123, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished histone H3-K9 dimethylation during mitotic cell cycle" RELATED [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished histone H3K9me2 during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abolished histone lysine H3 K9 dimethylation during vegetative growth" EXACT [GO:0036123, PomBase:mah]
synonym: "histone H3-K9 dimethylation abolished during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "histone H3-K9 dimethylation absent during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:al]
is_a: FYPO:0002566 ! abolished histone H3-K9 methylation during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "midori" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-11-18T08:08:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007890
name: normal protein localization to kinetochore during mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint signaling
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of a protein to the kinetochore of a chromosome is normal during mitotic spindle assembly checkpoint signaling." [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0002901 ! normal protein localization to kinetochore during vegetative growth

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007891
name: decreased spatial extent of mating-type region heterochromatin assembly
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which heterochromatin is assembled over a smaller portion of the mating-type region than normal." [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0005849 ! decreased spatial extent of heterochromatin assembly

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007892
name: increased histone exchange at subtelomeric heterochromatin {EXACT="increased histone exchange at subtelomeric heterochromatin"}
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which histone exchange at subtelomeric heterochromatin is increased. Histone exchange is replacement, within chromatin, of resident histones or histone subunits with alternative, sometimes variant, histones or subunits." [PMID:34731638, PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0007472 ! abnormal histone exchange

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007893
name: normal protein dephosphorylation during mitotic exit
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which protein dephosphorylation is normal during mitotic exit (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Protein dephosphorylation is the removal of a phosphate group from a protein amino acid." [PMID:12546793]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
is_a: FYPO:0001922 ! normal protein dephosphorylation during vegetative growth

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007894
name: increased histone H2B-K119 ubiquitination at subtelomeric heterochromatin during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which ubiquitination of lysine at position 119 of histone H2B is increased at subtelomeric heterochromatin. Lysine 119 corresponds to the conserved C-terminal lysine of H2B." [PMID:34731638]
is_a: FYPO:0008439 ! increased histone H2B-K119 ubiquitination during vegetative growth

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007895
name: increased histone H2B-K119 ubiquitination at pericentromeric heterochromatin during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which ubiquitination of lysine at position 119 of histone H2B is increased at pericentromeric heterochromatin. Lysine 119 corresponds to the conserved C-terminal lysine of H2B." [PMID:34731638]
is_a: FYPO:0008439 ! increased histone H2B-K119 ubiquitination during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-12-07T15:40:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007897
name: increased protein phosphorylation during mitotic exit
def: "A cellular process during mitosis in which the phosphorylation of one or more specific proteins, or of specific protein sites, occurs to a greater extent than normal during mitotic exit." []
is_a: FYPO:0004355 ! increased protein phosphorylation during mitosis
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-12-07T17:24:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007898
name: decreased actomyosin contractile ring actin filament length
def: "A cytokinesis phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the length of actin filaments in the contractile ring is shorter than normal." [PMID:34613787]
is_a: FYPO:0004736 ! abnormal actomyosin contractile ring
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-12-07T18:06:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007899
name: increased rate of protein localization to actomyosin contractile ring
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate, or speed, localization of a protein to the actomyosin contractile ring is increased." [PMID:34613787, PomBase:vw]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "increased rate of protein localisation to actomyosin contractile ring" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased rate of protein localization to actomyosin contractile ring during vegetative growth" EXACT [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "increased rate of protein localization to actomyosin contractile ring involved in mitotic cytokinesis" EXACT [GO:1904498]
synonym: "increased rate of protein localization to cytokinetic contractile ring" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "increased rate of protein localization to mitotic contractile ring" EXACT [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0002560 ! abnormal protein localization to actomyosin contractile ring
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2021-12-07T18:52:12Z" xsd:dateTime
created_by: midori
creation_date: 2015-10-30T15:25:35Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007901
name: increased number of R-loops
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of RNA-DNA hybrid molecules is greater than normal." [PMID:29622660]
synonym: "increased level of R-loops" EXACT []
synonym: "increased level of RNA-DNA hybrids" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0001323 ! altered level of substance in cell during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T15:14:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007902
name: normal onset of cytokinesis
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which mitotic cytokinesis begins at the same time as normal." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0001367 ! normal cytokinesis
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T16:59:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007903
name: cell lysis during mitotic interphase
def: "An inviable phenotype in which a cell lyses during mitotic interphase, i.e. the plasma membrane ruptures and cytoplasm is lost. Note that in fission yeast cell lysis, the integrity of the cell wall is also compromised." [PMID:19189958, PomBase:val]
synonym: "cell lysis during NETO" NARROW []
synonym: "vegetative cell lysis during interphase" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000647 ! vegetative cell lysis
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T17:13:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007904
name: abnormal glucan synthesis
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which glucan biosynthesis is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal glucan biosynthetic process" EXACT []
synonym: "beta-glucan synthesis defective" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000860 ! abnormal metabolic process
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T17:25:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007905
name: abnormal beta-glucan synthesis
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which beta-glucan biosynthesis is abnormal." [PomBase:mah]
synonym: "abnormal beta-glucan biosynthetic process" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0007904 ! abnormal glucan synthesis
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T17:25:24Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T17:33:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007906
name: increased cell population growth rate during amino acid starvation
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a cell population in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle grows at a faster rate than normal during amino acid starvation." [PMID:34805795, PomBase:val]
synonym: "increased cell proliferation during amino acid starvation" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000636 ! increased cell population growth rate
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T18:45:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007907
name: increased protein phosphorylation during amino acid starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the phosphorylation of one or more specific proteins, or of specific protein sites, occurs to a greater extent than normal when a cell is subject to amino acid starvation." [PMID:34805795\nPomBase\:val]
is_a: FYPO:0001038 ! increased protein phosphorylation during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T18:53:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007908
name: decreased protein phosphorylation during amino acid starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the phosphorylation of one or more specific proteins, or of specific protein sites, occurs to a lesser extent than normal when a cell is subject to amino acid starvation." [PMID:34805795, PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0001838 ! decreased protein phosphorylation during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T19:03:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007909
name: increased vacuolar pH
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the measured vacuolar pH is higher than normal." [PMID:34805795]
xref: PomBase:val
is_a: FYPO:0003755 ! abnormal vegetative cell phenotype
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-11T19:13:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007910
name: increased vegetative cell shrinkage
def: "A cell size phenotype in which a vegetative cell has a reduced volume or dimensions compared to a size previously observed for the same cell." [PMID:19189958, PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0001127 ! abnormal cell size
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-13T15:03:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007911
name: increased level of GTP-bound protein
def: "A cell phenotype in which the amount of GTP-bound protein measured in the cell is higher than normal when the cell is in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle. Total protein or a specific protein may be affected." [PMID:19189958, PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0001327 ! increased protein level during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-13T15:19:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007912
name: normal mitochondrial distribution
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which mitochondrial localization is normal." [PMID:10641037, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "normal mitochondrial localization" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0007913 ! normal organelle localization
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-13T15:35:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007913
name: normal organelle localization
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which organelle localization is normal." []
is_a: FYPO:0001319 ! normal cellular process during vegetative growth
is_a: FYPO:0001337 ! localization phenotype during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-13T15:38:42Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007914
name: mitotic sister chromatid separation during metaphase
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which mitotic sister chromatid separation occurs during mitotic metaphase." [PMID:10398680, PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0000416 ! premature mitotic sister chromatid separation
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-13T16:00:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007915
name: normal endoplasmic reticulum localization
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which Endoplasmic Reticulum localization is normal." [PMID:10641037, PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0007913 ! normal organelle localization
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-13T16:11:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007916
name: increased cellular dihydrosphingosine-1-phosphate level
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of  dihydrosphingosine-1-phosphate (DHS-1P) measured in a cell is higher than normal." [PMID:35008733]
synonym: "increased cellular level of DHS-1P" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0001330 ! increased level of substance in cell during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-20T11:33:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007917
name: decreased cellular dihydroceramide level
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of  dihydroceramide measured in the cell is lower than normal." []
synonym: "decreased cellular DH-cer level" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0001329 ! decreased level of substance in cell during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-20T11:44:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007918
name: abnormal RNA 3'-end processing {xref="PomBase:vw"}
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which RNA 3' end processing is abnormal." []
is_a: FYPO:0001553 ! abnormal RNA processing
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-20T11:56:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007919
name: abnormal RNA alternative polyadenylation
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which alternative polyadenylation of RNA is abnormal. RNA alternative polyadenylation generates RNA molecules with variable 3'-end lengths from a given RNA by differential use of cleavage and polyadenylation signals. Includes differences in the relative usage levels of alternative polyadenylation sites." []
is_a: FYPO:0001553 ! abnormal RNA processing
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-20T13:49:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007920
name: decreased ncRNA alternative polyadenylation
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which alternative polyadenylation of ncRNA is decreased. ncRNA alternative polyadenylation generates RNA molecules with variable 3'-end lengths from a given RNA by differential use of cleavage and polyadenylation signals. Includes differences in the relative usage levels of alternative polyadenylation sites." []
is_a: FYPO:0007919 ! abnormal RNA alternative polyadenylation
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-20T13:55:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007921
name: sensitive to benzamidine
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to benzamidine. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of benzamidine that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "sensitive to benzamidine during vegetative growth" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000127 ! increased sensitivity to chemical during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-20T16:14:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007922
name: sensitive to cysteine
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to cysteine  above normal physiological concentrations. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of cysteine that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:vw]
synonym: "sensitive to cysteine during vegetative growth" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000127 ! increased sensitivity to chemical during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
