id: FYPO:0007933
name: sensitive to 2,2′-dipyridyl
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to 2,2′-dipyridyl. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of 2,2′-dipyridyl that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0000127 ! increased sensitivity to chemical during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-20T18:56:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007934
name: dihydrouridine absent from cell
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of dihydrouridine measured in a cell is too low to detect." [PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0001208 ! substance absent from cell during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-20T19:01:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007936
name: increased number of DNA breakpoint junctions
def: "A cell phenotype in which the number of sites of  DNA breakpoint junctions is greater than normal." [PomBase:vw]
comment: DNA breakpooint junctions can be used to assess genome rearrangments.
is_a: FYPO:0003546 ! increased DNA damage
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-24T16:16:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007937
name: increased number of DNA breakpoint junctions during stationary phase
def: "A cell phenotype in which the number of sites of DNA breakpoint junctions is greater than normal during stationary phase." []
is_a: FYPO:0007936 ! increased number of DNA breakpoint junctions
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-24T16:21:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007938
name: sensitive to tea tree oil
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to tea tree oil. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of tea tree oil that allows wild type cells to grow." []
is_a: FYPO:0000127 ! increased sensitivity to chemical during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-01-31T17:32:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007939
name: normal chromatin loop formation during meiotic prophase I
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which any chromatin loop formation is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during  the meiotic prophase I." [PomBase:val]
synonym: "normal chromatin looping during meiotic prophase I" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0007941 ! normal chromatin organization during meiotic cell cycle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T12:48:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007940
name: normal chromatin organization
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which any process of chromatin organization is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Chromatin organization results in the specification, formation or maintenance of the physical structure of eukaryotic chromatin." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0001319 ! normal cellular process during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T12:53:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007941
name: normal chromatin organization during meiotic cell cycle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which any process of chromatin organization is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during  the meiotic cell cycle. Chromatin organization results in the specification, formation or maintenance of the physical structure of eukaryotic chromatin." []
synonym: "normal chromatin organisation during meiotic cell cycle" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0007940 ! normal chromatin organization
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T12:55:09Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007942
name: increased length of chromatin loops during meiotic prophase I
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which chromatin  loop  formation  during meiotic prophase I results in  chromatin loops of increased length." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0007944 ! abnormal chromatin loop formation during meiotic prophase I
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T13:16:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007943
name: abnormal chromatin organization during meiotic cell cycle
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which any process of chromatin organization is abnormal during the meiotic cell cycle. Chromatin organization results in the specification, formation or maintenance of the physical structure of eukaryotic chromatin." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0000642 ! abnormal chromatin organization
is_a: FYPO:0006759 ! abnormal meiotic chromosome organization
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T13:29:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007944
name: abnormal chromatin loop formation during meiotic prophase I
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which any process of chromatin loop formation is abnormal during meiotic prophase I." [PomBase:val]
synonym: "abnormal chromatin looping during meiotic prophase I" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0007943 ! abnormal chromatin organization during meiotic cell cycle
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T13:48:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007945
name: abnormal homologous chromosome pairing at cis-acting homologous chromosome pairing region during meiotic prophase I
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which homologous chromosome pairing during meiosis I prophase is abnormal at a cis-acting homologous chromosome pairing region such as the sme2 locus." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0003052 ! abnormal homologous chromosome pairing at cis-acting homologous chromosome pairing region
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T13:59:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007946
name: decreased protein ubiquitination
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the occurrence of ubiquitination of one or more specific proteins, or of specific protein sites, is decreased." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0006977 ! abnormal protein ubiquitination
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T14:11:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007947
name: sensitive to echinocandin
def: "A phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells show increased sensitivity to echinocandin. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of echinocandin that allows wild type cells to grow." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0000127 ! increased sensitivity to chemical during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T15:31:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007948
name: elongated multinucleate multiseptate spore
def: "A cell phenotype in which a spore is longer than normal, is multinucleate and multiseptate." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0001123 ! elongated spore
is_a: FYPO:0003342 ! elongated multinucleate cell
is_a: FYPO:0005277 ! multinucleate multiseptate cell
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T15:41:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007949
name: increased (1->3)-beta-D-glucan level
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of (1->3)-beta-D-glucan measured is greater than normal." [PomBase:val]
synonym: "increased (1,3)beta-D-glucan level" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0001194 ! increased beta-glucan level
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T16:19:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007950
name: increased mating efficency during nitrogen stress
def: "A biological process phenotype in which the observed mating efficiency, as determined by counting zygotes, asci, and sometimes spores, is higher than normal when a cell is subject to nitrogen stress." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0001043 ! increased mating efficiency
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T16:26:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007951
name: increased mating effciency during nitrogen starvation
def: "A biological process phenotype in which the observed mating efficiency, as determined by counting zygotes, asci, and sometimes spores, is higher than normal when a cell is subject to nitrogen starvation." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0001043 ! increased mating efficiency
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T16:27:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007952
name: normal protein level during stationary phase
def: "A cell phenotype in which the amount of protein measured in a cell is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type), during stationary phase. Total protein or a specific protein may be affected." [PomBase:val]
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
is_a: FYPO:0004083 ! normal protein level
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T16:38:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007953
name: increased spatial extent of heterochromatin assembly
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which heterochromatin is assembled over a larger portion of the chromosome than normal." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0008425 ! increased heterochromatin assembly
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-22T16:49:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007954
name: abnormal rate of microtubule depolymerization during vegetative growth
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate or speed of microtubule depolymerization, i.e. the removal of tubulin dimers from a microtubule, is abnormal." [PomBase:mlr, PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0000902 ! abnormal microtubule depolymerization during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-26T11:53:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007955
name: abnormal rate of microtubule polymerization during vegetative growth
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate or speed of microtubule polymerization, i.e. the additionl of tubulin dimers to a microtubule, is abnormal." [PomBase:mlr, PomBase:val]
synonym: "abnormal rate of microtubule polymerisation during vegetative growth" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0004614 ! abnormal microtubule polymerization during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-26T12:06:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007956
name: abnormal duration of microtubule growth event
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the duration of microtubule growth events is abnormal." [PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0000901 ! abnormal microtubule dynamics during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-26T12:12:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007957
name: abnormal microtubule rescue
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which microtubule rescue (the transition from shrinkage to growth) is abnormal. The frequency of rescues as well as the organisation can be affected." [PomBase:mlr]
xref: PomBase:mlr
is_a: FYPO:0000901 ! abnormal microtubule dynamics during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-26T13:19:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007958
name: increased rate of mitotic spindle elongation
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate, or speed, of mitotic spindle elongation is increased during miotic M phase." []
is_a: FYPO:0000131 ! abnormal mitotic spindle elongation
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-27T07:55:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007959
name: increased rate of mitotic spindle elongation during prophase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate, or speed, of mitotic spindle elongation is increased during miotic prophase." [PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0007958 ! increased rate of mitotic spindle elongation
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-27T08:00:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007960
name: decreased rate of mitotic spindle elongation during prophase
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the rate, or speed, of mitotic spindle elongation is decreased during prophase." [PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0003268 ! decreased rate of mitotic spindle elongation
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-27T08:13:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007961
name: transient abrupt spindle length decrease at anaphase onset
def: "A cell phenotype in which the spindle length decreases abruptly at anaphase onset." [PomBase:mlr]
comment: In PMID:24239120, this is likely due to interpolar microtubules being shorter than kinetochore microtubules, so cleavage of cohesin links leads to the shrinkage in length.
is_a: FYPO:0000131 ! abnormal mitotic spindle elongation
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-27T09:27:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007962
name: decreased mating efficiency during nitrogen starvation
def: "A biological process phenotype in which the observed mating efficiency, as determined by counting zygotes, asci, and sometimes spores, is lower than normal after nitrogen removal." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0000708 ! decreased mating efficiency
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-27T17:21:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007963
name: normal mating efficiency during nitrogen stress
def: "A biological process phenotype in which the observed mating efficiency, as determined by counting zygotes, asci, and sometimes spores, is normal (i.e. the same as in wild-type cells) during nitrogen limitation or poor nitrogen source." [PomBase:val]
is_a: FYPO:0001147 ! normal mating efficiency
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-04-27T17:27:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007965
name: increased spontaneous diploidization due to abolished sister chromatid separation
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which heterothallic haploid cells spontaneously form cells with diploid DNA content after failing chromosome segregation and  consequently nuclear division. The nucleus is displaced from the cell center by actin cables, preventing chromosome cut and leading to diploidisation." []
synonym: "escape from mitotic catastrophe" BROAD []
xref: PMID:33506191
xref: PomBase:mlr
is_a: FYPO:0000252 ! increased spontaneous diploidization
relationship: output_of FYPO:0001946 ! abolished mitotic sister chromatid separation
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T12:11:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007966
name: abolished nuclear displacement from cell division site after abolished mitotic sister chromatid separation
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which heterothallic haploid cells failing chromosome segregation and  consequently nuclear division fail to displace the nucleus from the septation site. This is normally mediated by actin cables." [PMID:33506191, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0002071 ! mislocalized nucleus during vegetative growth
relationship: output_of FYPO:0001946 ! abolished mitotic sister chromatid separation
relationship: output_of FYPO:0002435 ! abnormal actin cables
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T12:58:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007968
name: cut with mitotic spindle microtubules protruding beyond spindle pole body
def: "An inviable phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle after normal chromosome separation in which pushing forces exerted by microtubules protruding from the spindle pole bodies displace one of the daughter nuclei to the site of cytokinesis. The septum then physically divides that nucleus into two parts, giving rise to inviable daughter cell." [PMID:26031557, PomBase:mlr, PomBase:vw]
is_a: FYPO:0001055 ! cut following normal mitotic chromosome condensation
relationship: output_of FYPO:0003787 ! long mitotic spindle microtubules protruding beyond spindle pole body
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T14:31:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007969
name: short-lived long mitotic spindle microtubules protruding beyond spindle pole body
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which cells form mitotic spindle microtubules that are longer than normal, extend beyond the spindle pole body and are present transiently. The protruding spindle microtubules are surrounded by an extension of the nuclear envelope." [PMID:26031557] {comment="These protrusions are short-lived and labelled by Mal3 (presumably plus ends)"}
xref: PMID:26031557
xref: PomBase:mlr
is_a: FYPO:0003787 ! long mitotic spindle microtubules protruding beyond spindle pole body
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T14:40:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007970
name: increased rate of microtuble polymerization during vegetative growth
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which microtubule polymerization, i.e. the addition of tubulin dimers to the plus end of a microtubule occurs at a higher rate, or speed, than normal." [PMID:35293864, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0007955 ! abnormal rate of microtubule polymerization during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T15:29:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007971
name: increased rate of interpolar microtubule polymerization during mitotic anaphase B
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed during mitotic anaphase B in which interpolar microtubule polymerization, i.e. the addition of tubulin dimers to the plus end of a microtubule occurs at a higher rate, or speed, than normal." [PMID:35293864, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0007970 ! increased rate of microtuble polymerization during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T15:41:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007972
name: decreased rate of interpolar microtubule polymerization during mitotic anaphase B
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed during mitotic anaphase B in which interpolar microtubule polymerization, i.e. the addition of tubulin dimers to the plus end of a microtubule occurs at a lower rate, or speed, than normal." [PMID:35293864, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0005703 ! decreased rate of microtubule polymerization during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T15:49:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007974
name: increased rate of interpolar microtubule polymerization inside the mitotic nuclear membrane bridge
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed during mitotic anaphase B in which interpolar microtubule polymerization occurs at a higher rate, or speed, than normal for microtubules with their plus ends inside the nuclear membrane bridge formed during mitotic anaphase B." [PMID:35293864, PomBase:mlr]
comment: Microtubule growth speed is normally decreased when plus ends internalise in the nuclear membrane bridge, but this occurs to a lesser extent in this phenotype
is_a: FYPO:0007971 ! increased rate of interpolar microtubule polymerization during mitotic anaphase B
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T16:02:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007975
name: abnormal distribution of interpolar microtubule rescue during anaphase B
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed during anaphase B in which the distribution of the positions of interpolar microtubule rescues is abnormal.\nThe positions of interpolar microtubule rescues are where the transitions from shrinkage to growth occur." [PMID:35293864, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0007957 ! abnormal microtubule rescue
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T16:06:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007976
name: increased duration of interpolar microtubule growth events during anaphase B
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed during anaphase B in which the duration of interpolar microtubule growth events is longer." [PMID:35293864, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0007956 ! abnormal duration of microtubule growth event
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T16:13:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007977
name: abnormal homologous chromosome pairing during meiosis I prophase
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which homologous chromosome pairing during meiosis (synapsis) is abnormal during meiotic prophase I." []
is_a: FYPO:0003024 ! abnormal homologous chromosome pairing
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T16:27:37Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007978
name: decreased homologous chromosome pairing during meiosis I prophase
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which homologous chromosome pairing during meiosis (synapsis) is decreased during meiotic prophase I." []
is_a: FYPO:0007977 ! abnormal homologous chromosome pairing during meiosis I prophase
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2022-05-16T16:31:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007979
name: increased number of microtubules per bundle during mitotic interphase
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which cells contain interphase microtubule bundles with more microtubules than normal." [PMID:15837798, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0005558 ! abnormal microtubule bundle

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007980
name: Increased microtubule overlap length in bundles during mitotic interphase:
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which cells contain interphase microtubule bundles with microtubule overlaps longer than normal." [PMID:15837798, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0005558 ! abnormal microtubule bundle

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007981
name: abnormal interpolar microtubule length distribution during anaphase B
def: "A physical cellular phenotype in which the distribution of lengths of interpolar microtubules in the mitotic spindle is abnormal during anaphase B." [PMID:15689489, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0001574 ! abnormal bipolar mitotic spindle

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007982
name: single microtubule bundle with aster-like microtubules
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which all detectable microtubules are present in a single bundle and are not normally crosslinked, resulting in an aster-like organisation. See PMID:15068790." [PMID:15068790, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0002400 ! single microtubule bundle during mitotic interphase

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007983
name: microtubule bundles detached from the nuclear envelope
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed during mitotic interphase in which some microtubule bundles are not anchored to the nuclear membrane. See PMID:15068790" [PMID:15068790, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0005558 ! abnormal microtubule bundle

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007984
name: abolished eMTOC disassembly
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which equatorial microtubule organizing center (eMTOC) disassembly does not take place after cell division." [PMID:15068790, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0001350 ! abnormal microtubule cytoskeleton organization during vegetative growth

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007985
name: early eMTOC assembly
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which equatorial microtubule organizing center (eMTOC) assembly occurs earlier than normal. eMTOC assembly is the aggregation, arrangement and bonding together of a set of components to form an equatorial microtubule organizing center." [PMID:15068790, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0005690 ! abnormal eMTOC assembly

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007986
name: decreased protein localization to interphase microtubule bundle overlap
def: "A cell phenotype observed during mitotic interphase in which the localization of a protein to the microtubule overlap of cytoplasmic microtubule bundles is decreased." [PMID:19879140, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0006182 ! decreased protein localization to interphase microtubule

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007987
name: decreased rate of spindle elongation during meiotic anaphase B
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the rate, or speed, of meiotic spindle elongation is decreased during anaphase B." [PMID:32327557, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0007260 ! abnormal cellular process during meiotic cell cycle

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007988
name: long spindle microtubules protruding beyond spindle pole body during meiosis I
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in meiosis I in which cells form meotic spindle microtubules that are longer than normal, and extend beyond the spindle pole body. The protruding spindle microtubules are surrounded by an extension of the nuclear envelope." [PMID:32327557, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0000734 ! abnormal meiotic spindle

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007989
name: abolished nuclear congression during mating
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which karyogamy involved in conjugation with cellular fusion does not occur because the nuclei fail to come in physical contact." [PMID:25869666, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0003062 ! abnormal nuclear congression during mating

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007990
name: growth auxotrophic for isoleucine
def: "Auxotrophy in which a cell is unable to synthesize isoleucine, and therefore requires isoleucine in the medium for vegetative cell growth." [PMID:35325114, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "growth auxotrophic for isoleucine during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT []
synonym: "growth auxotrophic for isoleucine during vegetative growth" EXACT []
synonym: "isoleucine auxotrophy" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000128 ! auxotrophy

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007991
name: growth auxotrophic for valine
def: "Auxotrophy in which a cell is unable to synthesize valine, and therefore requires leucine in the medium for vegetative cell growth." [PMID:35325114, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "growth auxotrophic for valine during mitotic cell cycle" EXACT []
synonym: "growth auxotrophic for valine during vegetative growth" EXACT []
synonym: "valine auxotrophy" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000128 ! auxotrophy

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007992
name: decreased protein localization to mitotic spindle pole body during metaphase
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of a protein to the mitotic spindle pole body is decreased during metaphase." [PMID:35286199, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "decreased protein localisation to mitotic spindle pole body during metaphase" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased protein localization to mitotic SPB during metaphase" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0002822 ! decreased protein localization to mitotic spindle pole body during mitosis

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007993
name: decreased protein localization to pericentromeric region during meiosis I
def: "A cell phenotype observed during the first meiotic nuclear division in which the localization of a protein to chromatin at the pericentromeric regions is decreased." [PMID:18716626, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0006529 ! abnormal protein localization to centromere during meiotic cell cycle

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007994
name: normal meiotic sister chromatid cohesion protection during meiotic anaphase I
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which the cohesion protection during anaphase of the first meiotic nuclear division is normal." [PMID:18716626, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0002094 ! normal meiotic sister chromatid cohesion

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007995
name: abolished protein localization to old cell tip during mitotic interphase
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to the old cell tip does not occur during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle." [PMID:15184402, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0003329 ! abolished protein localization to cell tip during mitotic interphase

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007996
name: thin actin cables
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in mitotic interphase in which cells form actin cables that are thinner than normal. This is evidence by lower actin fluorescence signal and is likely due to the presence of fewer actin filaments than normal." [PMID:15184402, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0002031 ! abnormal actin cable morphology

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007997
name: monopolar actin cortical patch localization to new end
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which actin cortical patches are localized to only the new end of a cell following cell division." [PMID:15184402, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0001019 ! monopolar actin cortical patch localization during vegetative growth

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007998
name: abnormal protein localization to interphase microtubule bundle
def: "A cell phenotype observed during mitotic interphase in which the localization of a protein to interphase microtubule bundles is abnormal." [PMID:15184402, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0000931 ! abnormal protein localization to microtubule cytoskeleton during vegetative growth

[Term]
id: FYPO:0007999
name: abolished protein localization to spindle pole body during karyogamy
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein to the spindle pole body is abolished during karyogamy." [PMID:25869666, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0003542 ! abolished protein localization to meiotic spindle pole body

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008000
name: increased sensitivity to chemical in stationary phase
def: "A phenotype in which cells show increased sensitivity to a chemical when the cell population is in stationary phase. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of that chemical that allows wild type cells to grow." [PMID:35618649, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0002683 ! increased sensitivity to chemical

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008001
name: sensitive to menadione in stationary phase
def: "A phenotype in which cells show increased sensitivity to menadione when the cell population is in stationary phase. Cells stop growing (and may die) at a concentration of menadione that allows wild type cells to grow." [PMID:35618649, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "sensitive to menadione during stationary phase" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0008000 ! increased sensitivity to chemical in stationary phase

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008002
name: cell lysis during mating
def: "An inviable phenotype observed during mating in which a cell lyses, i.e. the plasma membrane ruptures and cytoplasm is lost, during the process of cell fusion that occurs during mating. Note that in fission yeast cell lysis, the integrity of the cell wall is also compromised." [PMID:35673994, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "cell lysis during cell fusion" RELATED []
synonym: "cell lysis during cellular fusion" RELATED []
is_a: FYPO:0002488 ! cell lysis

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008003
name: normal protein localization to site of mechanical stress
def: "A cell phenotype in which the localization of a protein at a site of mechanical stress on the cell surface is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PMID:34666001, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0003627 ! normal protein localization

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008004
name: abolished protein localization to site of mechanical stress
def: "A cell phenotype in which a protein does not localize to, and is therefore absent from, a site of mechanical stress on the cell surface where it is normally found." [PMID:34666001, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0001375 ! abolished protein localization

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008005
name: normal reactive oxygen species level during stationary phase
def: "A cell phenotype in which the amount of reactive oxygen species (ROS) measured in a cell that is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during stationary phase." [PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "normal reactive oxygen species accumulation during stationary phase" RELATED []
synonym: "normal reactive oxygen species level in stationary phase" EXACT []
synonym: "normal ROS accumulation during stationary phase" RELATED []
synonym: "normal ROS level during stationary phase" EXACT []
synonym: "normal ROS level in stationary phase" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0001076 ! normal level of substance in cell

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008006
name: dynamic microtubule minus ends in interphase bundles
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton phenotype observed during mitotic interphase in which the microtubule minus ends are dynamic (they alternate between growth and shrinkage phases)." [PMID:21444751, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "dynamic microtubule minus ends during interphase" BROAD []
synonym: "uncapped microtubule minus ends during interphase" BROAD []
synonym: "uncapped microtubule minus ends in interphase bundles" BROAD []
is_a: FYPO:0000901 ! abnormal microtubule dynamics during vegetative growth

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008007
name: mitotic spindle collapse during anaphase B elongation with progressive spindle pole congression
def: "A cell phenotype in which a mitotic spindle assembles and begins to elongate, but collapses during anaphase B, with the collapse being followed by the spindle poles congressing together. In some cases, this is known to be driven by depolymerisation of microtubules part of a merotelic attachment (PMID:19948483)." [PMID:19948483, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0005722 ! mitotic spindle collapse during anaphase B elongation
relationship: output_of FYPO:0004381 ! merotelic kinetochore attachment during mitosis

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008008
name: increased duration of cytoplasmic microtubule growth events during mitotic interphase
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed during mitotic interphase in which the duration of cytoplasmic microtubule growth events is longer." [PMID:22363481, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "longer cytoplasmic microtubule growth events during mitotic interphase" NARROW []
synonym: "lower cytoplasmic microtubule catastrophe during mitotic interphase" NARROW []
synonym: "lower cytoplasmic microtubule catastrophe rate during mitotic interphase" NARROW []
is_a: FYPO:0007956 ! abnormal duration of microtubule growth event

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008009
name: abnormal interphase mitotic telomere clustering during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which telomere clustering is abnormal. Telomere clustering gathers telomeres during or prior to tethering to the nuclear periphery during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle." [PMID:15615848, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "abnormal interphase telomere clustering" BROAD []
synonym: "abnormal mitotic interphase telomere clustering" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal telomere clustering during vegetative growth" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0001362 ! abnormal cellular process during vegetative growth

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008010
name: decreased RNA-dependent RNA polymerase
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the observed rate of RNA-dependent RNA polymerase activity is decreased." [PMID:15615848, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0000663 ! decreased catalytic activity

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008011
name: abolished siRNA loading onto RITS complex
def: "An RNA localization phenotype where the loading of siRNAs onto the RITs complex is abolished." [PMID:15615848, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "abolished recruitment of siRNA onto RITS complex" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased siRNA localization to RITS complex" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000366 ! decreased RNA localization

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008012
name: cell sensitive to mechanical stress
def: "A cell phenotype in which a vegetative cell dies at a level of mechanical stress that wild-type cells can normally withstand." [PMID:34666001, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0003755 ! abnormal vegetative cell phenotype

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008013
name: normal inositol hexakisphosphate kinase activity
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the observed rate of inositol hexakisphosphate kinase activity is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PMID:35536002, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0000660 ! normal catalytic activity

[Term]
