[Term]
id: FYPO:0008022
name: abolished cell population growth on alanine nitrogen source
def: "A vegetative cell population growth phenotype in which a cell population does not grow in a medium containing alanine as the nitrogen source." [PomBase:mlr]
comment: Use this term for a population of cells that does not grow with alanine as the nitrogen source, but does grow using a different nitrogen source (a cell population that does not grow on any media would be considered inviable). Note that cell growth terms refer to growth under aerobic conditions unless stated otherwise.
synonym: "abolished alanine utilization" RELATED [PomBase:mlr, PomBase:vw]
synonym: "abolished growth on alanine nitrogen source" BROAD [PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "abolished vegetative cell population growth on alanine nitrogen source" EXACT [PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "cell population growth on alanine nitrogen source abolished" EXACT [PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0001575 ! abolished vegetative cell population growth

