[Term]
id: FYPO:0008044
name: swollen elongated multinucleate aseptate vegetative cell with more than four nuclei
def: "A cell morphology phenotype in which a vegetative cell is swollen, elongated, has no septum, and contains more than four nucleus. In a swollen cell, both length and diameter may be greater than normal, although the cell is only considered elongated if the length:diameter ratio is also greater than normal." [PMID:10545452]
comment: Multiple nuclear division cycles can cause arrested cells to accumulate up to 32 nuclei.
is_a: FYPO:0002051 ! swollen elongated multinucleate aseptate vegetative cell
is_a: FYPO:0008045 ! elongated vegetative cell with more than four nuclei
created_by: vw
creation_date: 2022-11-30T12:15:08Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008045
name: elongated vegetative cell with more than four nuclei
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell contains more than four nuclei, is longer than normal, and has a greater length:diameter ratio than normal." []
is_a: FYPO:0000133 ! elongated multinucleate vegetative cell
created_by: vw
creation_date: 2022-11-30T12:33:27Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008046
name: decreased sexual agglutination in response to blue light
def: "A cell population phenotype that reflects decreased occurrence of sexual agglutination in response to blue light." [PMID:23873862]
synonym: "decreased conjugation with cellular fusion in response to blue light" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000003 ! cell population phenotype
created_by: vw
creation_date: 2022-11-30T12:58:52Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008047
name: decreased histone H3-K4 dimethylation  at centromere during meiosis
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in meiosis in which dimethylation of lysine at position 4 of histone H3 is decreased at the centromere." []
comment: We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
is_a: FYPO:0006459 ! abnormal protein modification during meiotic cell cycle
created_by: vw
creation_date: 2023-01-25T13:46:16Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008048
name: increased histone H3-K4 dimethylation at centromere during meiosis
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in meiosis in which dimethylation of lysine at position 4 of histone H3 is increased at the centromere." []
is_a: FYPO:0008049 ! increased histone H3-K4 dimethylation during meiosis
created_by: vw
creation_date: 2023-01-25T14:40:53Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008049
name: increased histone H3-K4 dimethylation during meiosis
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in meiosis in which dimethylation of lysine at position 4 of histone H3 is increased." []
is_a: FYPO:0006459 ! abnormal protein modification during meiotic cell cycle
created_by: vw
creation_date: 2023-01-25T14:43:16Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008050
name: abolished histone H3-K4 methylation during meiosis
