[Term]
id: FYPO:0008052
name: increased histone H3-K4 dimethylation during mitosis
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in mitosis in which the dimethylation of lysine at position 4 of histone H3 occurs to a greater extent than normal." []
is_a: FYPO:0005225 ! increased histone H3-K4 dimethylation during vegetative growth
created_by: vw
creation_date: 2023-01-25T14:56:15Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008053
name: decreased intron acceptor binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which an interaction between a protein and mRNA intron acceptor is decreased. One of the relevant gene products may be encoded by the mutated gene, or both the RNA and protein may be encoded by genes other than the mutated one." []
synonym: "'decreased 3' intron binding'" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0002134 ! decreased protein-RNA interaction
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T10:59:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008054
name: decreased homocitrate synthase inhibition by L-lysine
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the observed rate of homocitrate synthase is increased, due to the absence of lysine inhibition." [PMID:20089861]
synonym: "feedback inhibition insensitive" BROAD []
is_a: FYPO:0000662 ! increased catalytic activity
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T11:09:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008055
name: decreased Glc2Man9GlcNAc2 oligosaccharide glucosidase activity
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the observed rate of a Glc2Man9GlcNAc2 oligosaccharide glucosidase activity is decreased." [PMID:23609449]
is_a: FYPO:0000663 ! decreased catalytic activity
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T15:01:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008056
name: abolished poly(A)-specific ribonuclease activity
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which a poly(A)-specific ribonuclease activity is absent." [PMID:19307292]
is_a: FYPO:0006301 ! abolished ribonuclease activity
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T15:10:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008057
name: abnormal enzyme processivity
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the observed  ability of an enzyme to catalyze consecutive reactions without releasing the substrate (i.e. template) is abnormal." [] {def="PMID:19307292"}
is_a: FYPO:0000661 ! abnormal catalytic activity
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T15:19:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008058
name: increased polyA ribonuclease processivity
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the observed  ability of a polyA robonuclease to catalyze consecutive reactions without releasing the substrate (i.e. template) is abnormal." [PMID:19307292]
is_a: FYPO:0008057 ! abnormal enzyme processivity
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T15:26:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008059
name: decreased K48-linked polyubiquitin binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of a protein to K48-linked polyubiquitin occurs to a lower extent than normal." [PMID:16138082]
comment: This term can be used for any protein-protein interaction that is affected by a mutation, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
synonym: "decreased K48-linked polyUb binding" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0001645 ! decreased protein-protein interaction
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T15:38:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008060
name: normal mono ubiquitin binding
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which the binding of one protein to a ubiquitin monomer is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PMID:16138082]
comment: This term can be used for any protein-protein interaction that is tested in a mutant, whether or not the mutated gene product is one of the interacting proteins. We recommend noting which proteins were used in the assay when annotating to this term.
is_a: FYPO:0000703 ! normal protein-protein interaction
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T15:43:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008061
name: abolished phosphorylation of RNA polymerase II C-terminal domain serine 5 residues during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the phosphorylation of the serine residue at position 5 within one or more copies of the heptapeptide repeat (YSPTSPS) of the C-terminal domain of RNA polymerase II does not occur." [PMID:1902677]
is_a: FYPO:0007410 ! abnormal RNA polymerase II C-terminal domain phosphorylation
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T15:50:15Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008062
name: increased chromatin binding at centromere central core
def: "A molecular function phenotype in which occurrence of chromatin binding to the chromatin central core by a gene product (usually a protein) in a mutant is increased. The affected gene product may be encoded by the mutated gene, or by a different gene, and may normally bind DNA, protein, or both in chromatin." [PMID:15908586]
is_a: FYPO:0002980 ! increased chromatin binding
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T15:57:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008063
name: decreased immediate intracellular calcium spike following osmotic shock
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the intracellular calcium ion (Ca2+) concentration briefly increases abnormally, or does not change, immediately following osmotic shock. Normally, the intracellular Ca2+ concentration increases to a peak in a \"burst\" within one minute, and then decreases to a new steady-state concentration." [PMID:36200871]
is_a: FYPO:0001462 ! altered cellular calcium level
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-22T16:02:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008064
name: decreased mating efficiency during phosphate starvation
def: "A biological process phenotype in which the observed mating efficiency, as determined by counting zygotes, asci, and sometimes spores, is lower than normal after phosphate removal." [PMID:36779416]
is_a: FYPO:0000708 ! decreased mating efficiency
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-03-06T12:47:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008065
name: decreased sporulation frequency during phosphate starvation
def: "A cell population phenotype in which the frequency of occurrence of ascospore formation is decreased after phosphate removal." []
is_a: FYPO:0000584 ! decreased sporulation frequency
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-03-06T12:53:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008066
name: abolished cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase in response to phosphate starvation
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which progression through the mitotic cell cycle is no longer arrested during G1 phase when phosphate is removed. Arrest may either occur under conditions where arrest is not a normal occurrence, or may progress differently from normal under conditions where arrest normally does take place." [PMID:36779416]
is_a: FYPO:0005097 ! abnormal cell cycle arrest in mitotic G1 phase
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-03-06T13:08:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008067
name: constricted chained mitochondrion
def: "A physical cellular phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the mitochondrion is abnormally hyperconstricted at the fission sites and has a chained \"beads-on-a-string\" appearance." [PMID:37540145]
is_a: FYPO:0000056 ! mitochondria fused
property_value: creation_dat "2023-08-16T10:22:42Z" xsd:dateTime
created_by: vw

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008068
name: increased spatial extent of chromatin silencing at silent mating-type cassette
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which chromatin silencing at the silent mating-type cassettes is observed over an increased portion of the mating-type region." [PMID:18030666]
is_a: FYPO:0004376 ! increased chromatin silencing at silent mating-type cassette
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-03-06T14:51:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008069
name: increased spatial extent of histone H3-K9 methylation at mating type locus during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which methylation of lysine at position 9 of histone H3 at the mating type locus is observed over an increased portion of the mating-type region." [PMID:18030666]
is_a: FYPO:0005065 ! increased histone H3-K9 methylation at mating type locus during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-03-06T15:01:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008070
name: normal histone H3-K9 methylation at centromere during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the methylation of lysine at position 9 of histone H3 in centromeric regions is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PMID:19394293]
is_a: FYPO:0003232 ! normal histone H3-K9 methylation during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-03-06T15:19:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008071
name: normal spatial extent of histone H3-K9 methylation during vegetative growth
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which methylation of lysine at position 9 of histone H3 occurs over the same portion of the chromosome as normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type)." [PMID:19394293]
synonym: "normal histone H3-K9 methylation spreading during vegetative growth" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0003232 ! normal histone H3-K9 methylation during vegetative growth
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "vw253" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-03-07T13:52:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008072
name: normal spatial extent of histone H3-K9 methylation at peri-centromere during vegetative growth
