[Term]
id: FYPO:0008081
name: decreased vegetative cell population growth when co-cultured with wild-type cells
def: "A cell population phenotype in which the growth of a population of cells is decreased relative to normal in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle when the population is co-cultured with wild-type cells. Decreased growth may reflect a reduced growth rate (i.e. slower growth), growth that occurs to a lesser extent than normal, or both." [PMID:36302945]
synonym: "adaptive growth" RELATED []
is_a: FYPO:0001355 ! decreased vegetative cell population growth
