def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which nucleosome occupancy is lower than normal in the pericentromeres. Nucleosome occupancy measures the tendency for DNA in a given region to be packaged into nucleosomes." [PMID:21211723]
synonym: "decreased nucleosome occupancy at centromeric region" RELATED []
is_a: FYPO:0000855 ! abnormal nucleosome positioning in heterochromatin
is_a: FYPO:0004491 ! decreased nucleosome occupancy
created_by: vw
creation_date: 2024-01-19T11:21:29Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008152
name: normal CUT RNA level
def: "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the amount of transcribed  cryptic unstable trancripts (CUTs) measured in a cell is  normal  (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type).  Total CUT RNA or a CUT transcribed from a specific locus may be affected." []
is_a: FYPO:0001317 ! normal RNA level during vegetative growth
created_by: vw
creation_date: 2024-01-25T07:43:37Z

[Term]
id: FYPO:0008153
