[Term]
id: FYPO:0009000
name: decreased rate of cytoplasmic microtubule polymerization during mitotic interphase
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed during mitotic interphase in which cytoplasmic microtubule polymerization, i.e. the addition of tubulin dimers to the plus end of a microtubule occurs at a lower rate, or speed, than normal." [PMID:36633091, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "decreased cytoplasmic microtubule growth rate during mitotic interphase" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased cytoplasmic microtubule growth speed during mitotic interphase" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased cytoplasmic microtubule polymerisation speed during mitotic interphase" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased cytoplasmic microtubule polymerization speed during mitotic interphase" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased rate of cytoplasmic microtubule polymerisation during mitotic interphase" EXACT []
