[Term]
id: FYPO:0009001
name: decreased duration of cytoplasmic microtubule growth events during mitotic interphase
def: "A microtubule cytoskeleton organization phenotype observed during mitotic interphase in which the duration of cytoplasmic microtubule growth events is shorter." [PMID:36633091, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "higher cytoplasmic microtubule catastrophe during mitotic interphase" NARROW []
synonym: "higher cytoplasmic microtubule catastrophe rate during mitotic interphase" NARROW []
synonym: "shorter cytoplasmic microtubule growth events during mitotic interphase" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0007956 ! abnormal duration of microtubule growth event

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009002
name: increased mitochondrial-associated microtubule fraction during mitotic interphase
def: "A mitochondrion distribution phenotype observed during mitotic interphase in which the length fraction of cytoplasmic microtubules that is bound to mitochondria is increased with respect to the wild type." [PMID:36633091, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "increased microtubule-associated mitochondrial fraction during mitotic interphase" RELATED [] {comment="They are not exactly the same, but equivalent if total mitochondria and microtubules are the same", created_by="PomBase:mlr"}
is_a: FYPO:0000894 ! abnormal intracellular mitochondrion distribution

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009003
name: abolished nuclear fusion with normal nuclear congression during mating
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which karyogamy involved in conjugation with cellular fusion does not occur, despite the nuclei and their SPBs coming together." [PMID:36650056, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "nuclear congression without nuclear fusion" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0000511 ! abolished nuclear fusion during mating

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009004
name: horsetail movement with unfused nuclei
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which horsetail movement occurs without nuclei fusing. This can happen with both nuclei having congressed and their SPBs having coalesced, but nuclei having failed to fuse, see PMID:36650056." [PMID:36650056, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "horsetail movement with two nuclei" EXACT []
synonym: "twin horsetail nuclei" NARROW []
is_a: FYPO:0000197 ! abnormal horsetail movement

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009005
name: increased interphase nuclear movement velocity in daughter cell without mitochondria
def: "A cellular process phenotype observed in mitotic interphase in which microtubule-based movement oscillations occur at a faster speed than normal in a daughter cell that inherits no mitochondria." [PMID:36633091, PomBase:mlr]
synonym: "increased interphase nuclear oscillation velocity in daughter cell without mitochondria" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0005461 ! abnormal microtubule-based movement during vegetative growth

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009006
name: abnormal meiotic cell cycle entry
def: "A cellular process phenotype in which a cell enters the meiotic cell cycle without either of the normal steps that precede it: conjugation with cellular fusion and karyogamy with nuclear fusion." [PMID:36650056, PomBase:mlr]
is_a: FYPO:0000052 ! abnormal meiotic cell cycle

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009007
name: decreased vegetative cell population viability
def: "A vegetative cell population phenotype in which a lower than normal proportion of cells is viable. In High Throughput Phenotyping this is typically assessed using phloxine as a dye." [PMID:34984977, PomBase:mlr]
comment: Not to be confused with cell population growth phenotypes, which are measured with culture density or by serial dilution on solid medium. {xref="PomBase:mlr"}
synonym: "decreased cell population viability during vegetative growth" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0002057 ! cell population viability

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009008
name: increased vegetative cell population viability
def: "A vegetative cell population phenotype in which a larger than normal proportion of cells is viable. In High Throughput Phenotyping this is typically assessed using phloxine as a dye." [PMID:34984977, PomBase:mlr]
comment: Not to be confused with cell population growth phenotypes, which are measured with culture density or by serial dilution on solid medium. {xref="PomBase:mlr"}
synonym: "increased cell population viability during vegetative growth" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0002057 ! cell population viability

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009009
name: decreased cell population growth on arginine nitrogen source
def: "A vegetative cell population growth phenotype in which cell growth is decreased relative to normal in a medium containing arginine as the nitrogen source." [PomBase:mlr]
comment: Note that cell growth terms refer to growth under aerobic conditions unless stated otherwise.
