[Term]
id: FYPO:0009014
name: decreased vegetative cell population viability on xylose carbon source
def: "A vegetative cell population phenotype in which a lower than normal proportion of cells is viable when the medium contains xylose as carbon source. In High Throughput Phenotyping this is typically assessed using phloxine as a dye." [PMID:34984977]
synonym: "decreased viability on xylose carbon source" BROAD []
is_a: FYPO:0009007 ! decreased vegetative cell population viability
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "PomBase:mlr" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-17T10:42:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009015
name: increased cell population viability on glycerol carbon source
def: "A vegetative cell population phenotype in which a larger than normal proportion of cells is viable when grown with glycerol as carbon source. In High Throughput Phenotyping this is typically assessed using phloxine as a dye." []
comment: Not to be confused with cell population growth phenotypes, which are measured with culture density or by serial dilution on solid medium.
synonym: "increased cell population viability during vegetative growth on glycerol carbon source" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0009008 ! increased vegetative cell population viability
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "PomBase:mlr" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-17T18:21:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009016
name: increased cell population viability on xylose carbon source
def: "A vegetative cell population phenotype in which a larger than normal proportion of cells is viable when grown with xylose as carbon source. In High Throughput Phenotyping this is typically assessed using phloxine as a dye." []
comment: Not to be confused with cell population growth phenotypes, which are measured with culture density or by serial dilution on solid medium.
synonym: "increased cell population viability during vegetative growth on xylose carbon source" EXACT []
is_a: FYPO:0009008 ! increased vegetative cell population viability
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "PomBase:mlr" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-17T18:21:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009017
name: reduced viability in stationary phase upon glucose starvation in the presence of cadmium
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a smaller than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable after entering stationary phase, when subjected to glucose starvation and when cadmium is present in the medium in a higher proportion than usual." []
is_a: FYPO:0005231 ! loss of viability in stationary phase upon glucose starvation
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "PomBase:mlr" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-17T12:59:43Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: FYPO:0009018
name: increased viability in stationary phase upon glucose starvation in the presence of cadmium
def: "A cell population phenotype in which a higher than normal proportion of cells in the population remains viable after entering stationary phase, when subjected to glucose starvation and when cadmium is present in the medium in a higher proportion than usual." []
is_a: FYPO:0001309 ! increased viability in stationary phase
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator "PomBase:mlr" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date "2023-02-17T14:12:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
